{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "38 Baby", "line": "Bitch, I bought my own car, started my own dealership", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I bought my own car, started my own dealership (Bought my own car, started my own dealership)"], "meaning": "Definitely not referring to an actual vehicle, here Youngboy slyly boasts that he started his own gang which is known as “NBA”.\n\nIn prison slang, “car” is a term for a group or clique of inmates. Cars are often formed by inmates who share a commonality, like race, home state, or charges.\n\nBy stating that he, “bought my own car” he is making it clear that he didn’t assimilate into an existing gang, but that he “started my own dealership” AKA: Started his own gang. A fact commonly held to be true.", "annotation_id": "34584956", "url": "https://genius.com/34584956", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "38 Baby", "line": "Don’t like the fact that now I’m blowin’ up, nigga, get on your shit", "vault_lines": ["Don't like the fact that now I'm blowin' up, nigga, get on your shit (Get on your shit)"], "meaning": "Youngboy’s talking about how Da Real Gee Money was saying that the fame had got to him and that’s why he switched up.", "annotation_id": "26610082", "url": "https://genius.com/26610082", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
