{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "All In", "line": "Where my styrofoam is", "vault_lines": ["I wish Three was on my left, where my styrofoam is"], "meaning": "Refers to NBA YoungBoy’s association with drinking lean, which is commonly served in a styrofoam cup. It symbolizes a key part of his lifestyle, often linked to both coping mechanisms and his past experiences.", "annotation_id": "34514435", "url": "https://genius.com/34514435", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "All In", "line": "Came up outta that dirt pile, now I’m ballin’", "vault_lines": ["Came up outta that dirt pile, now I'm ballin'"], "meaning": "NBA YoungBoy reflects on his transformation from a difficult, impoverished past to achieving success and fame. “Dirt pile” represents his humble and challenging beginnings, while “ballin'” signifies his current status of wealth and prosperity, showing how far he’s come.", "annotation_id": "34514419", "url": "https://genius.com/34514419", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "All In", "line": "To", "vault_lines": ["Got up out of Cypress, went to the Woodlands, got a safe room in my crib"], "meaning": "until", "annotation_id": "32712945", "url": "https://genius.com/32712945", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "All In", "line": "Ten lines straight, goin’ on ten days, my body ain’t got no fluid", "vault_lines": ["Ten lines straight, goin' on ten days, my body ain't got no fluid"], "meaning": "Youngboy does coke. He took 10 lines of cocaine back to back and he’s been up 10 days straight. Being up for that long can make you feel like a zombie or dehydrated.\n\nSecond meaning: It’s a known fact Youngboy drinks lean. Some people call a ounce  of lean a “line.” This would mean he drank 10 lines of lean for 10 days and now his body feels dehydrated .", "annotation_id": "22078833", "url": "https://genius.com/22078833", "state": "pending", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "All In", "line": "If I say how I feel, would you really listen? If you was all mine, I’d be all in", "vault_lines": ["If you was all mine, I'd be all in"], "meaning": "He wants to know if he’s actually being heard. Yb is telling his girl that if she gave him her all he would be willing to put his all into the relationship.\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: “If i say how i fell you should really listen”", "annotation_id": "21162925", "url": "https://genius.com/21162925", "state": "pending", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "All In", "line": "Got up out of Cypress, went to the Woodlands, got a safe room in my crib Ain’t no tellin’ when I’ma have to use it, we all know how I live", "vault_lines": ["Got up out of Cypress, went to the Woodlands, got a safe room in my crib", "Ain't no tellin' when I'ma have to use it, we all know how I live"], "meaning": "NBA YoungBoy’s stay in Cypress, Texas was not smooth.\n\nIn April 2020, it was revealed that YoungBoy was living in the city after he was detained at his Cypress home. A video filmed at the scene gave a good look of the street he was staying on. With this information, fans on Twitter from the area began considering pulling up to his house.\n\nWith his whereabouts made public, YoungBoy became an easier target. In June, goons did break into YoungBoy’s crib when he was out of town and filmed themselves in the act. Fans online quickly began to fear for his safety. Just months prior, rapper Pop Smoke was murdered inside his Hollywood Hills home. He had posted his location on social media.\n\nYoungBoy lets us know he has finally moved on from Cypress to The Woodlands, a wealthier and safer place nearby. But even so, given his history with run-ins, his new home still has a safe room.", "annotation_id": "20589110", "url": "https://genius.com/20589110", "state": "pending", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
