{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Another Episode", "line": "Bro shot five times from the Honda", "vault_lines": ["Bro shot five times from the Honda, pussy bitch tried runnin' (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Honda cars are sometimes mentioned in NBA YoungBoy’s songs; for example, in 86 Prayers: “Tell Sherhonda I need a Honda, I’m way too dirty for Lotuses.” YoungBoy and his crew would ALLEGEDLY slide on their opps using common, non-luxury cars to avoid suspicion.", "annotation_id": "38347258", "url": "https://genius.com/38347258", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Another Episode", "line": "I got plenty bodies (Yeah), I like to rap about it (Yeah, yeah) I don’t give no fuck about it (Yeah), bitch, I’ll shoot up your body (Hold on)", "vault_lines": ["I got plenty bodies (Yeah), I like to rap about it (Yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Mentions how he knows that in each released and unreleased song, that seems “self snitched” about his ALLEGED bodies, he doesn’t care and raps about it cause its something he enjoys", "annotation_id": "38345417", "url": "https://genius.com/38345417", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Another Episode", "line": "Neighbors ain’t want they children runnin’ with me ’cause I slump niggas", "vault_lines": ["Neighbors ain't want they children runnin' with me 'cause I slump niggas"], "meaning": "Parents of children didn’t want them to hang out with Youngboy because of the words that spread about what he was doing as a child", "annotation_id": "38345389", "url": "https://genius.com/38345389", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Another Episode", "line": "I was fucked up inside my hood as a young nigga", "vault_lines": ["I was fucked up inside my hood as a young nigga"], "meaning": "He was a trouble maker when he was young and growing up in a rough part of Louisiana, smoking his family members cig butts whatever had left.\nAs he lost his grandmother, it had a impact on him and fell in a grief where he took risky ideas and actions to be able to survive, which deep down he has stated, didn’t like. In an interview with 33, 33 stated that they would commit criminal acts to be able to pay for YoungBoy’s studio time.\n\nIn his past, he was in juvenile detention in Baton Rouge, Louisiana somewhere 2015, as he mentioned on his released song from February 11, 2025, “Yo Night” stating, “Fresh outta Ryan detention center.”\nhttps://genius.com/38345312", "annotation_id": "38345296", "url": "https://genius.com/38345296", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Another Episode", "line": "Capitol Middle", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Capitol Middle* refers to the Capitol Middle Magnet School in Baton Rouge, Louisiana.", "annotation_id": "38331649", "url": "https://genius.com/38331649", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Another Episode", "line": "Nigga, I step in 23s, I say, “I’m born to walk that walk”", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, I step in 23s, I say, \"I'm born to walk that walk\""], "meaning": "This is a play on words with the rapper JayDaYoungan who went by the nickname “23.” YB saying he steps in 23s and is born to walk that walk is him basically saying he stepped on JayDaYoungan so this confirms he’s really about murder. JayDaYoungan did mess with Michael Jordan, too, one of his albums got him on there in a Michael Jordan Jersey.\n\nhttps://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcQvPRcSjQbq9Wa805dpLsqUZNTdPhvEb_nr_ePGbZpY3w&s=10", "annotation_id": "38319890", "url": "https://genius.com/38319890", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Another Episode", "line": "I throw my 5, I twist my fingers and watch my daughter throw that North", "vault_lines": ["I throw my 5, I twist my fingers and watch my daughter throw that North"], "meaning": "“Five” means throwing up the Five Nation sign with his hands. “North” refers to his roots in North Baton Rouge, specifically Chippewa 38th Street, and his affiliation with the Bloods.\n\n\n\nIn recent videos, he has often been seen throwing up the two-gun symbol in reference to Peter Rollock, street name Pistol Pete, the founder of SMM (Sex Money Murda), which has been affiliated with the UBN since 1996.\n\nAt the end of the song “I-10 Baby,” from the project 38 Baby 2, YoungBoy says,\n“Blood gang or no gang, UBN or UB out,” affirming his identification with the United Blood Nation.", "annotation_id": "38315731", "url": "https://genius.com/38315731", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Another Episode", "line": "Where the nigga who I killed? Dead right now Was poppin’ pills with him and breakin’ and enterin’", "vault_lines": ["Where the nigga who I killed? Dead right now", "Was poppin' pills with him and breakin' and enterin'"], "meaning": "Another reference to Gee Money. Gee Money was essentially NBA YoungBoy’s mentor and you can hear the influence in most of his early rap back in 2016", "annotation_id": "38309574", "url": "https://genius.com/38309574", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Another Episode", "line": "Why you think the industry don’t like me? I knocked ’bout three of these bitches off", "vault_lines": ["Why you think the industry don't like me? I knocked 'bout three of these bitches off"], "meaning": "Reference to King Von (Dayvon Daquan Bennett), Blvd Quick (Ashton Wells), and Gee Money (Garrett Burton). Who are all diseased, hypothetically and allegedly due to YoungBoy.", "annotation_id": "38309542", "url": "https://genius.com/38309542", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
