{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Ben Lomond Mountain", "line": "Lord Father, I pray that my daddy come home For some time Montana been holdin’ me down", "vault_lines": ["Lord Father, I pray that my daddy come home", "For some time Montana been holdin' me down"], "meaning": "YoungBoy hopes his father is released from prison, his fathers currently serving out a 55 year prison sentence after a robbery gone wrong. Montana being his manager and father figure from the very beginning of his career.", "annotation_id": "32827535", "url": "https://genius.com/32827535", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Ben Lomond Mountain", "line": "She gon’ blow up me all night, ’til I come over or give in", "vault_lines": ["She gon' blow up me all night, 'til I come over or give in"], "meaning": "He actually says, “she gon’ blow me up all night.\nTil’ I come over or give in.\n\nHe’s referring to a woman, I assume, calling his phone all night until he comes over or answers the phone. Hence the line, “til I come over or give in.”", "annotation_id": "32772938", "url": "https://genius.com/32772938", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Ben Lomond Mountain", "line": "Weber State", "vault_lines": ["She told me that she go to Weber State"], "meaning": "Refers to Weber State University, located in Ogden Utah and at the foot of the Wasatch Mountains, the mountain range Ben Lomond is a part of.", "annotation_id": "28833151", "url": "https://genius.com/28833151", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Ben Lomond Mountain", "line": "Toy", "vault_lines": ["Saw it in the spot and I playеd with the toy"], "meaning": "Tar* referring to black tar heroin", "annotation_id": "28274629", "url": "https://genius.com/28274629", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Ben Lomond Mountain", "line": "Maybach 4MATIC, highspeed chase, I ain’t wit’ the hype", "vault_lines": ["Maybach 4MATIC, highspeed chase, I ain't wit' the hype"], "meaning": "4MATIC is an all-wheel drive range from Mercedes Benz designed to create traction on slippery surfaces when driving. Maybach is a sub-brand owned by Mercedes—the brand produced higher-end, more luxurious vehicles than Mercedes.\n\nYoungBoy rapping about a Maybach with a 4MATIC system could refer to his current house arrest in Utah, as the weather in Utah features heavy snow, hence why a 4MATIC system would be safer and easier to maneuver as it provides extra traction.\n\nFurthermore, YoungBoy has rapped about his car collection with Maybachs several times, most notably in the Internet Money-produced, “Flossin'” as he rapped:\n\nRidin' in a Maybach flossin'\nShawty with me wonder why I get her often", "annotation_id": "27316200", "url": "https://genius.com/27316200", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Ben Lomond Mountain", "line": "High inside the mountains, Salt Lake Can you hear me from Ben Lomond (Ben Lomond) Rocky, down the route that I take All this money, I ain’t never lonely", "vault_lines": ["Rocky, down the route that I take", "All this money, I ain't never lonely"], "meaning": "Ben Lomond Mountain is a peak in Utah, which is a section of the Wasatch Mountains mountain range.  From the mountain’s peak, Utah’s capital, Salt Lake City is visibly seen.\n\nIn October 2021, YoungBoy was granted bail, claiming a $1.5 million bond after he was arrested on federal firearm charges in March 2021. Following his bond hearing, he was ordered to serve strict, twenty-four-hour house arrest in Utah.\n\nIn addition, YoungBoy has boasted about his situation once he relocated to his Utah home in several songs including his September 2022 single “Fresh Prince Of Utah,” where he rapped about his legal struggles. Earlier in his January 2022 hot hitting track “Bring The Hook,” YoungBoy had taken a more vicious approach, rapping:\n\nNorthside, nigga know that’s my side\nUtah, come here bitch, get hogtied, another died\nOh Lord, man this nigga crazy, he do not respect them boys\n\nIn the music video for YoungBoy’s “Put It On Me,” he’s seen dancing on the roof of his Utah house with Salt Lake City in the backdrop.", "annotation_id": "27316062", "url": "https://genius.com/27316062", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
