{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bitch Let’s Do It", "line": "I hop out first with that chopper, I bust first at them cowards", "vault_lines": ["I hop out first with that chopper, I bust first at them cowards"], "meaning": "Youngboy is likely referencing the November 2, 2016 shooting where The 17-year-old Kentrell was accused of firing a gun multiple times during a drive-by shooting in the 2000 block of Kentucky Street During the incident, a passenger of the vehicle was shot in the neck.\n\n after the shooting the driver fled the scene, but got a flat tire and crashed the car on E. Lakeshore Drive Gaulden, the driver, and the other passenger who was uninjured all fled the scene before police arrived.\n\nThe driver of the vehicle, who was a juvenile, at the time was later arrested and booked into the Juvenile Detention Center for principal to attempted first-degree murder.\n\nInvestigators issued a warrant for Gaulden’s arrested. He was located on November 28 in Austin, TX at a concert and was arrested by local authorities.\n\nGaulden was transported back to Louisiana and booked into the East Baton Rouge Parish Prison on Wednesday, December 7. His bond is set at $200,000.", "annotation_id": "36717887", "url": "https://genius.com/36717887", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
