{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bitch Let’s Do It", "line": "Chasely, where’d you find that?", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is one of the few producer tags, by Hip Hop producer Chasely.", "annotation_id": "28591130", "url": "https://genius.com/28591130", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bitch Let’s Do It", "line": "And I was fucked up with Ten, wear the same clothes, that’s my partner He broke the code and I zipped him, this nigga used to be on side me I was mad at my boy, but, shit, I’m grown, you can’t stop me He got me hooked on that boy, we both was goin’ through some problems", "vault_lines": ["And I was fucked up with Ten, wear the same clothes, that's my partner", "He broke the code and I zipped him, this nigga used to be on side me", "I was mad at my boy, but, shit, I'm grown, you can't stop me", "He got me hooked on that boy, we both was goin' through some problems"], "meaning": "Mentioned here is NBA Ben10, known also as “Ten” who has been with YoungBoy since his early stages of his career, one of those who have stayed true to him and his label.\n\nSince struggling to a point were close friends or brothers wear each other’s clothes, being that they can’t afford a lot of clothes resulting to sharing between two homies or brothers, since these stages, NBA Ben10 has been with NBA YoungBoy.\n\nThe line “He broke the code and I zipped him” more than likely is referring to late rapper Da Real Gee Money, Gee Money and YoungBoy grew up as friends, but the two ended up beefing after Gee Money had sex with YoungBoy’s sister and bragged about it. The feud escalating which eventually lead to the death of Gee Money.", "annotation_id": "28591106", "url": "https://genius.com/28591106", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bitch Let’s Do It", "line": "Since I was sixteen, had money, I say, “I grew up stuntin’”", "vault_lines": ["Since I was sixteen, had money, I say, \"I grew up stuntin'\""], "meaning": "Having to quickly go from struggle to fame, NBA YoungBoy has been in the music industry for a long time, having to achieve major success from a very young and early age, as young as 16.\n\nWith that success only having to go up and up ever since then, with consistency and hard work YoungBoy has maintained and increased he’s financial value/money.", "annotation_id": "28591096", "url": "https://genius.com/28591096", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bitch Let’s Do It", "line": "Since I was sixteen, had money, I say, “I grew up stuntin’”", "vault_lines": ["Since I was sixteen, had money, I say, \"I grew up stuntin'\""], "meaning": "Having to quickly go from struggle to fame, NBA YoungBoy has been in the music industry for a long time, having to achieve major success from a very young and early age, as young as 16.\n\nWith that success only having to go up and up ever since then, with consistency and hard work YoungBoy has maintained and increased he’s financial value/money.", "annotation_id": "28591070", "url": "https://genius.com/28591070", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
