{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Black Ball", "line": "In the slums, right in that North, where the fuck I was found", "vault_lines": ["In the slums, right in that North, where the fuck I was found"], "meaning": "“In the slums” -> He’s talking about growing up in the trenches, the poverty, and the rough environment he came from.\n\n“Right in that North” -> Refers to North Baton Rouge, Louisiana — his hometown. The North is infamous for being dangerous, violent, and full of hardship.\n\n“Where the f*ck I was found” -> Like saying, “This is where they got me from”.", "annotation_id": "35012263", "url": "https://genius.com/35012263", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Black Ball", "line": "Try to block me out, blackball, but they see me now", "vault_lines": ["Try to block me out, blackball, but they see me now"], "meaning": "“Try to block me out, blackball” -> Kentrell is saying the industry, media, or even haters tried to blackball him, meaning they tried to ruin his career, shut him out of opportunities, or prevent him from blowing up.\n\nIn the music world, being “blackballed” = people in power purposely trying to keep you out the spotlight.\n\n“But they see me now” -> Despite all the hate, he’s still successful, still in front of everyone, still making noise.", "annotation_id": "35012245", "url": "https://genius.com/35012245", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
