{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Boot Up", "line": "Pussy want to Insta’ beef, he Tweetin’ and I see all of that", "vault_lines": ["Pussy want to Insta' beef, he Tweetin' and I see all of that"], "meaning": "NBA YoungBoy is perhaps alluding to his feud with Lil Durk since their long-term internet beef has been ongoing after the tragic death of a fellow friend of Lil Durk, King Von who was murdered by an NBA YoungBoy signee. Here, YoungBoy is referencing Lil Durk’s tweets here, which Lil Durk tweeted:\n\nSome people support you cause they don’t want to look crazy for not supporting you …. pay attention.\n[…]\nI’m not mentioning the dead in my songs no more or performing songs with they name in it…… – big Smurk\n\nThe pair have been going back and forth on diss tracks such as in Durk’s February 2022 single “AHHH HA” and NBA YoungBoy’s February 2022 track “I Hate YoungBoy.” Furthermore, both artists uploaded pictures on Instagram, possibly wanting both to “slide” on each other, hence the Instagram feud.", "annotation_id": "26867904", "url": "https://genius.com/26867904", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Boot Up", "line": "A switch on back, I burst ’em (Bah, bah, bah)", "vault_lines": ["A switch on back, I burst 'em (Bah, bah, bah)"], "meaning": "A “switch” is an illegal firearm attachment that turns a semi-automatic firearm — more specifically a pistol — into a fully automatic firearm, resulting in it “burst[ing].” Being caught with a switch-customed firearm can lead to a sentence from two to five years in Federal prison.\n\nYoungBoy has previously rapped about the same firearm attachment on his January 2022 track, “No Switch:”\n\nAll these niggas talkin' ‘bout them switches, choppa came automatic\nRed flag, you know the business\nPop his ass, we drop his ass\nThat be that green flag activity\n\n\n\nPictured: The magazine in a Glock with a switch being emptied in seconds due to it being made automatic.", "annotation_id": "26867407", "url": "https://genius.com/26867407", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Boot Up", "line": "Monkey nuts, this bitch got monkey nuts", "vault_lines": ["Monkey nuts, this bitch got monkey nuts"], "meaning": "Youngboy is dissing Kodak Black here, after Kodak called Youngboy out and Youngboy responded by Calling Kodak a “pussy”, Kodak went to twitter and posted claiming that he is “Monkey nuts”", "annotation_id": "26704174", "url": "https://genius.com/26704174", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Boot Up", "line": "’Cause ain’t none of y’all ’bout murders", "vault_lines": ["'Cause ain't none of y'all 'bout murders (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Youngboy is sending direct shots to Chicago Rapper ‘King Von’;\n\nHe claim’s that the Late King Von is nothing about being a murderer as he was shot in 2020 by Youngboy’s Crew.", "annotation_id": "26664865", "url": "https://genius.com/26664865", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
