{"type": "song", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bounce", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Youngboy-never-broke-again-bounce-lyrics", "genius_title": "Bounce", "genius_id": 11505689, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bout My Business", "line": "I just bought a brand-new bezel (It’s Vade on the keys) For to make the hard times look pretty And I came up straight up from the block I watched my grandpa save pennies", "vault_lines": ["I just bought a brand-new bezel (It's Vade on the keys)", "For to make the hard times look pretty", "And I came up straight up from the block", "I watched my grandpa save pennies"], "meaning": "A “bezel” is often a term to refer to a watch — in this case, YoungBoy notes that he bought a watch to display his growth from poverty by employing a metaphorical juxtaposition as “pretty” contrasts “the block” — a slang term to refer to poverty-ridden neighborhoods. Furthermore, YoungBoy boasts his affluence to prove his success further.\n\nYoungBoy was born and raised in North Baton Rouge — an area with high violence rates alongside high poverty rates, hence why he referred to the “hard times.”\n\nHe further noted that he watched his grandfather “save pennies,” portraying YoungBoy’s lack of financial stability while growing up. This, in particular, has been ridiculed on social media, particularly on TikTok for sounding phonetically similar to “I watched my grandpa say penis.”\n\nMore so, YoungBoy often refers to his grandparent’s involvement in his childhood, particularly in his August 2018, “No Mentions” in which he rapped:\n\nCut my ties with my people, now my grandfather poppin'\nRan it up, all by myself though, now they never gon' stop me\nAnd I see they say I flop though, yeah, yeah\nIn my head I know what I know", "annotation_id": "24901110", "url": "https://genius.com/24901110", "state": "accepted", "votes": 110, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bout My Business", "line": "Hello? Pawpaw Huh? Whatchu doin’? I’m just tryna watch TV, TV watchin’ me Haha, whole lotta nothin’ I miss you I miss you too, man Aren’t you supposed to be comin’ to, um, Southern, for a concert now? Yeah, I’ll see you there I’ma be there, when is it? On the twenty-eighth or twenty-sixth? It’s one of them days, I’ma make sure you know I love you, though, I was tryna make sure I talk to you Okay, I’m glad you called, man, glad you called I love you, Pawpaw I love you too Slime Alright, man (Ooh, ah) (Ooh, ah)", "vault_lines": ["I love you, though, I was tryna make sure I talk to you", "Okay, I'm glad you called, man, glad you called", "I love you, Pawpaw", "I love you too"], "meaning": "In the intro to the track, YoungBoy can be heard having a rather general conversation with his grandfather. Youngboy was born and raised by his grandparents in Baton Rouge, Louisiana.\n\nYoungBoy has shown his appreciation for his grandfather multiple times before, such as on a Facebook post, which he captioned “My grandfather been my father for as long as i can remember #MC\":\n\n\n\n A fictionalization of YoungBoy as a child playing with his grandfather. \n\n\n\n\nHe’s also previously mentioned his grandparents' presence on “Preach,“ rapping:\n\nI miss the Nawf just like my granny, my heart in them trenches", "annotation_id": "19687497", "url": "https://genius.com/19687497", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
