{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "And I’m still ridin’ wit’ that 45, and it’s still illegal Tell them niggas get at me, slime You heard me?", "vault_lines": ["And I'm still ridin' wit' that 45, and it's still illegal", "Tell them niggas get at me, slime"], "meaning": "YoungBoy is still riding around the city in one of his luxurious cars with a .45 ACP Glock that he still has no license for, making it illegal. He’s telling us to tell anybody that doesn’t like him to get at him while he’s riding around with dangerous guns, so he can show them what he’s about.", "annotation_id": "40138381", "url": "https://genius.com/40138381", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "Tell these niggas bring it on, they some motherfuckin’ cheerleaders You heard me?", "vault_lines": ["Tell these niggas bring it on, they some motherfuckin' cheerleaders"], "meaning": "Bring It On (2000) is a teen comedy film about a high school cheerleading squad that discovers their award-winning routines were stolen from an inner-city school, forcing them to create new ones to compete at the national championships. By calling his opponents “cheerleaders,” YoungBoy accuses his rivals of being cowards who avoid direct confrontation and simply watch from the sidelines, acting as loud spectators rather than active participants in street violence. He further compares them to a “pep squad” that thrives on internet drama and clout-chasing, contrasting their vocal social media presence with the silent, dangerous behavior of real, street-level threats.", "annotation_id": "40138263", "url": "https://genius.com/40138263", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "I see a new hat, nigga with a blue flag", "vault_lines": ["I see a new hat, nigga with a blue flag"], "meaning": "Might be a reference towards lil Durks “V.Roy” hat", "annotation_id": "31911942", "url": "https://genius.com/31911942", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "They know that they can’t clone me", "vault_lines": ["They know that they can't clone me"], "meaning": "It has been speculated that rappers might be cloned while in jail and that their clones might be outside while the rapper is still locked up. YoungBoy mentions that and says that he is too unique to be cloned and that he can never be cloned.", "annotation_id": "30323824", "url": "https://genius.com/30323824", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "Know the police on me", "vault_lines": ["Know the police on me"], "meaning": "He refers to how the police have been eager to jail him ever since he became a top-selling rapper. He even references this in his song ‘No Switch’:\n\n“Hold on, bro don’t call my phone, I’m being investigated by DOJ (Department of Justice) and the feds”", "annotation_id": "30323781", "url": "https://genius.com/30323781", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "Rap niggas catch this whole semi", "vault_lines": ["Rap niggas catch this whole semi"], "meaning": "YoungBoy in this lyric is dissing Rapper King Von who tried to jump Quando Rondo and his crew outside at the Monaco Hookah Lounge where Von died due to Quando Rondo’s shooter, ‘Lul Timm’ letting shots off at King Von who would seemingly die at an hospital.", "annotation_id": "30323755", "url": "https://genius.com/30323755", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "Bitch ass nigga, we dyin’ behind this green flag", "vault_lines": ["Bitch ass nigga, we dyin' behind this green flag"], "meaning": "Slime is a subculture of the Blood gang. It was popularized by Young Thug and other members of YSL. People who rep this term often wear green flags. You may also be familiar with the phrase “slatt” which stands for “slime love all the time”.", "annotation_id": "29804406", "url": "https://genius.com/29804406", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "It’s Northside, 38, 4KT, FreeDDawg", "vault_lines": ["It's Northside, 38, 4KT, FreeDDawg"], "meaning": "Youngboy is from north Baton Rouge. More specifically, he was raised on 3863 Chippewa St. which he shortens to 38. 4KT is speculated to mean a lot of things. It stands for 4/For/ K Trey. Some think it means Four Killer Team, other think it’s homage to his 4 sons, 3 of which names start with the letter “K” and the other begins with “T”.", "annotation_id": "29804348", "url": "https://genius.com/29804348", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "I been tryna raise my children, ain’t whack something in a lil’ minute", "vault_lines": ["I been tryna raise my children, ain't whack something in a lil' minute"], "meaning": "Youngboy states that he hasn’t killed anybody because he wants to raise his kids (doesn’t want to go to jail).\n\nYoungboy’s father robbed a convenience store on December 1st, 2009 and shot a store clerk. He was charged with armed robbery and attempted first degree murder and was sentenced to 55 years. For most of Youngboy’s childhood he had no father figure, and since his mother Sherhonda was in and out of his life he lived with his grandma, but she after her passing in 2010 he had to stay in a group home.", "annotation_id": "29804277", "url": "https://genius.com/29804277", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "Said them young niggas wit’ them 30s sittin’", "vault_lines": ["Said them young niggas wit' them 30s sittin'"], "meaning": "This line refers to the Glock 30. Its one of the most reliable pistols out there and is akin to the Glock 21, just more compact.", "annotation_id": "29804215", "url": "https://genius.com/29804215", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "Plenty killings in the fuckin’ city", "vault_lines": ["Plenty killings in the fuckin' city"], "meaning": "Baton Rouge has the 6th highest murder rate out of every city in America, at 31.72 per 100,000, with only St. Louis, Baltimore, Birmingham, Detroit, and Dayton topping it (in that order, from first to fifth).", "annotation_id": "29804185", "url": "https://genius.com/29804185", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "Big Mac, catch ’em, let it go, nigga, fetch that", "vault_lines": ["Big Mac, catch 'em, let it go, nigga, fetch that"], "meaning": "“Big Mac” its a nickname for the MAC-10 gun. It’s similar to an Uzi in terms of appearance and other aspects. In this line he talks about firing his gun and killing somebody.", "annotation_id": "29804125", "url": "https://genius.com/29804125", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "Ring around the rosie Pussy tryna dome me", "vault_lines": ["Ring around the rosie", "Pussy tryna dome me"], "meaning": "2 meanings\n\nRing around the rosie is a kids nursery rhyme with a dark meaning (were not going into that look it up).\n\nAnd this is a similar line on his 2020 song called “Step on Shit” when he said “Look, ring around the rosie, pussy say he on me (Let’s go)” kinda has the same flow.", "annotation_id": "26939252", "url": "https://genius.com/26939252", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "This ain’t no Hellcat, nigga, this a catch-him", "vault_lines": ["This ain't no Hellcat, nigga, this a catch-him"], "meaning": "This could be a sneak diss towards Lil Durk, who often mentions hellcats in his songs, in particular the song “Hellcats & Trackhawks”.", "annotation_id": "26635008", "url": "https://genius.com/26635008", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
