{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "Ever since a toddler, been a problem", "vault_lines": ["Ever since a toddler, been a problem, they can't fuckin' get me"], "meaning": "Youngboy has been a menace since he was a lil kid. He had an ankle monitor when he was only 12 years old.", "annotation_id": "25167149", "url": "https://genius.com/25167149", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "They know I’m bloody and got more bodies then they whole committee", "vault_lines": ["They know I'm bloody and got more bodies then they whole committee"], "meaning": "Kentrell means that he is a blood and just by himself he has killed more people that probably all of his opps in total.", "annotation_id": "25132422", "url": "https://genius.com/25132422", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bring It On", "line": "Left him baptized right there on that corner They know who the fuck blessed him", "vault_lines": ["Left him baptized right there on that corner", "They know who the fuck blessed him"], "meaning": "This is a very clever play on words by Youngboy. He compares him murdering someone to baptism, which is interesting in it’s own right. Baptism is a Christian practice that involves dumping a person in “holy” water and represents cleansing away all sins and acceptance into the church. On the other hand, Youngboy murdering someone would be sort of similar, given that this person would go to meet God.", "annotation_id": "25044156", "url": "https://genius.com/25044156", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
