{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bruce Wayne", "line": "She treat me just like I’m a child She’s pickin’ up any time that I call Liftin’ me up every time that I fall Lil’ shawty so perfect, I wanna run out", "vault_lines": ["She treat me just like I'm a child", "She's pickin' up any time that I call", "Liftin' me up every time that I fall", "Lil' shawty so perfect, I wanna run out"], "meaning": "Even though Youngboy’s childhood trauma fucked him up real bad, he finds comfort in his lady. This is a common theme among many of his love songs, how a lady can hold him down and keep him safe from his thoughts.", "annotation_id": "38659210", "url": "https://genius.com/38659210", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bruce Wayne", "line": "Number one, I’m on top of the game", "vault_lines": ["Number one, I'm on top of the game"], "meaning": "out of prison his songs were doing crazy numbers like shot calling, he’s referencing his recent hits", "annotation_id": "38659204", "url": "https://genius.com/38659204", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bruce Wayne", "line": "I’m the man in the city, I’m holdin’ them millions, they callin’ me Bruce Wayne", "vault_lines": ["I'm the man in the city, I'm holdin' them millions, they callin' me Bruce Wayne"], "meaning": "Youngboy’s referred to Bruce Wayne in other songs, one lyric in Digital states “Youngboy just like Bruce Wayne”. This likely stems from him losing his father to prison at a very young age, and having to live with his grandmother yet still being rich and having power.", "annotation_id": "38659194", "url": "https://genius.com/38659194", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Bruce Wayne", "line": "Treat her just like them killers, ain’t never desert her", "vault_lines": ["Treat her just like them killers, ain't never desert her"], "meaning": "Youngboy’s referring to a common theme in many of his songs which is that he can’t quit all that gang shit, he’s saying that he can’t ever desert the gang lifestyle and his hitters from back when he was young, and he can’t leave his girl.", "annotation_id": "38659185", "url": "https://genius.com/38659185", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
