{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Callin", "line": "Thinking ’bout how I just told T I meant war about my set Other words, willing to die, ain’t tryna put some shit to rest", "vault_lines": ["Thinking 'bout how I just told T I meant war about my set", "Other words, willing to die, ain't tryna put some shit to rest"], "meaning": "YoungBoy recollects when he was talking to his close friend T about the fact that is willing to protect his gang and hood at all costs, whether it means dying or killing.\n\n(LINE CORRECTION)\nBefore: ain’t tryna put some shit to rest\nAfter: and tryna put some shit to rest", "annotation_id": "20728349", "url": "https://genius.com/20728349", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Callin", "line": "Beat cases, still had money, now a nigga nameless", "vault_lines": ["Beat cases, still had money, now a nigga nameless"], "meaning": "Youngboy speaks on Kodak Black’s past situations when he was arrested In April 2016 and May 2016, had a net worth of 500k-1M and is currently in jail as of September 2020, unable to keep his name relevant.\n\nTensions between YoungBoy Never Broke Again and Kodak Black were ignited in early April 2020 after Kodak accused YoungBoy of cooperating with the police in connection to a stabbing that took place at his home.", "annotation_id": "20728283", "url": "https://genius.com/20728283", "state": "pending", "votes": -2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
