{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Callin", "line": "Plans like Andretti, me and my stepper bumpin’ Spitta, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Plans like Andretti, me and my stepper bumpin' Spitta, nigga"], "meaning": "Youngboy shouts out New Orleans rapper Curren$y AKA “Andretti Spitta”\nHe speaks on his busy schedule mentioning that he is always on the move, comparing his plan book to Curren$y’s, while stating that him and his stepper also listen to Curren$y while handling his business.\n\n(Stepper simply means a close friend or ride or die, somebody who steps with you and is willing to die with you)", "annotation_id": "20728070", "url": "https://genius.com/20728070", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Callin", "line": "Blue rag in my back pocket (Crip)", "vault_lines": ["Blue rag in my back pocket (Crip)"], "meaning": "Snoop is referring to his affiliation with the Rollin' 20s Crips in his hometown of Long Beach, California. While there is some debate regarding actual membership, Snoop Dogg has represented himself as a Crip throughout his music career. Similar lyrics representing his affiliation with the Crips can be found throughout his work, such as in his hit single Drop It Like It’s Hot [https://genius.com/Snoop-dogg-drop-it-like-its-hot-lyrics], where he raps,\nI keep a blue flag hanging out my backside\nBut only on the left side, yeah that’s the Crip side", "annotation_id": "20721772", "url": "https://genius.com/20721772", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
