{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Can We Be Friends (From The Biggest 5ive)", "line": "Think ’bout Kaell, uh", "vault_lines": ["Whenever I think KD, think 'bout Kaell, uh (Ooh)"], "meaning": "The “Kaell” Youngboy is referring to is one of his younger sons Kaell Gaulden who was born in June 2021, Kaell is the son of Youngboy and Arcola Smith.", "annotation_id": "40804085", "url": "https://genius.com/40804085", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Can We Be Friends (From The Biggest 5ive)", "line": "I ain’t did no drank I ain’t smoke nothin’, and I ain’t smoke shit in a minute You heard me? I threw away my whole pack of cigarettes You heard me? Them bitches hated They don’t like to see the slime doin’ fine, believe that", "vault_lines": ["I ain't smoke nothin', and I ain't smoke shit in a minute", "You heard me? I threw away my whole pack of cigarettes", "You heard me? Them bitches hated", "They don't like to see the slime doin' fine, believe that"], "meaning": "To go with the annotation before this, YoungBoy “got the monkey off his back” by finally getting rid of a lingering problem/ source of stress. What he’s talking about represents overcoming a serious challenge, or conquering an addiction. At least, in these lines, knowing how YB expresses the heavy pain he’s experienced as well. So I wouldn’t take anything away from the last annotation. Anyways, he’s happily expressing how he doesn’t smoke anymore. Then, states how he means weed or cigarettes, letting you know that he means what he’s saying at that moment, as if you look now he’s back smoking something. He then expressed how people hated on him during that time period because they ain’t wanna see him doing good in life. Rich nor healthy. But he happily expressed that he was doing better.", "annotation_id": "40780827", "url": "https://genius.com/40780827", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Can We Be Friends (From The Biggest 5ive)", "line": "I got that monkey off my back,", "vault_lines": ["I got that monkey off my back, I ain't did no drank"], "meaning": "To “get the monkey off your back” means to finally rid yourself of a lingering problem, heavy burden, or source of stress. It represents the sweet relief of shedding a nagging responsibility, overcoming a serious challenge, or conquering an addiction. – Gemini Ai\n(Or literal meaning, he had a pet monkey back in 2023.)", "annotation_id": "40778066", "url": "https://genius.com/40778066", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Can We Be Friends (From The Biggest 5ive)", "line": "I’m so disrespectful, I know you don’t like how I up and start wildin’ But it come from my childhood, I’m so childish", "vault_lines": ["I'm so disrespectful, I know you don't like how I up and start wildin'", "But it come from my childhood, I'm so childish"], "meaning": "He’s aware on how hasn’t matured emotionally.", "annotation_id": "40774584", "url": "https://genius.com/40774584", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Can We Be Friends (From The Biggest 5ive)", "line": "Tell ‘em I got a casket in this motherfucker, I’m leavin’ them up inside that motherfucker", "vault_lines": ["Tell 'em I got twelve bodies"], "meaning": "Shown in a old music video.", "annotation_id": "40773755", "url": "https://genius.com/40773755", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Can We Be Friends (From The Biggest 5ive)", "line": "Can we be friends? I wan’ come through for you, I’ll buy you a new coupe I say, “Can you be my friend?”", "vault_lines": ["I say, \"Can you be my friend?\""], "meaning": "Just saying can you be there for me, but meaning that if you keep it real, he’ll help you out/treat you right because you deserve it.", "annotation_id": "39474120", "url": "https://genius.com/39474120", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
