{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Can We Be Friends (From The Biggest 5ive)", "line": "I know that they see I’ve been paintin’ my nails They think I got touched while I was up in that cell When you know I’m a gangster, you know I ain’t playin’ like that, bitch, I’ll still be up in jail", "vault_lines": ["I know that they see I've been paintin' my nails", "They think I got touched while I was up in that cell", "When you know I'm a gangster, you know I ain't playin' like that, bitch, I'll still be up in jail"], "meaning": "When he started painting his nails in 2022-2023ish, people thought he was gay for doing so, and wearing Long earrings, he’s just trying to say that he still a gangsta, meaning that faith and true intentions better than what people think. It’s like what you wear is what you like, while people gonna judge and assume your this and that, while your not what people truly say.", "annotation_id": "39473951", "url": "https://genius.com/39473951", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Can We Be Friends (From The Biggest 5ive)", "line": "They know I’ve been tryna stop violence", "vault_lines": ["They know I've been tryna stop violence"], "meaning": "His stop the violence campaign is from when he recorded songs around the “I Rest My Case” album\nHe also posted that video, late at night, him on the balcony, where he states, “Stop the violence”\n\n\n\nHe’s been trying to change his image and leading the youth and people who listen to his music, that violence isn’t worth it.\n\nMuch more is said in this 2023 interview.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q76TpEu5TXw", "annotation_id": "39473928", "url": "https://genius.com/39473928", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
