{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Carter Son", "line": "Soprano, no Soprino, we live life like Gambino", "vault_lines": ["Soprano, no Soprino, we live life like Gambino"], "meaning": "The Sopranos is a fictional American crime drama series by David Chase. The series' lead character Tony Soprano played by James Gandolfini is an American-Italian crime boss and is the main protagonist in the series.\n\nSimilar to The Sopranos, the Gambino crime family is a non-fiction Italian-American Mafia crime family led by Carlo Gambino who died in October 1976 of natural causes at the age of seventy-four.\n\nYoungBoy notes that he lives a similar lifestyle to the Sopranos and the Gambinos, involving himself in drugs and handling the transportation of narcotics. NBA namedropped cartel leader Medellín Cartel, who is one of the infamous leaders in his December 2018 track “Slime Belief”:\n\nNow can you make it better? Trap out like Griselda", "annotation_id": "27620434", "url": "https://genius.com/27620434", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Carter Son", "line": "I’m the top on YouTube, fuck a new school, I don’t use no Vevo", "vault_lines": ["I'm the top on YouTube, fuck a new school, I don't use no Vevo"], "meaning": "On the release week preceding the release of this song, NBA Youngboy was in fact at the #1 position on the Youtube Music charts for the United States–having been on the charts for 139 weeks with 42M views.\n\n\n\nFurthermore, Youngboy uses his own channel as opposed to artists who use popular hosting service Vevo to distribute their music videos.", "annotation_id": "18238412", "url": "https://genius.com/18238412", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
