{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Casket", "line": "I come as a sinner, Lord, I’m takin’ me to your scriptures", "vault_lines": ["I come as a sinner, Lord, I’m takin' me to your scriptures"], "meaning": "The phrase “I come as a sinner, Lord, I’m takin' me to your scriptures” is not a direct quote from the Bible, but it reflects a common theme in Christianity of acknowledging one’s own sinfulness and seeking guidance from God’s word. There are many Bible verses and prayers that express this sentiment, such as Luke 5:8 where Simon Peter falls to his knees and says “Go away from me, Lord; I am a sinful man!”. Other verses and prayers ask for forgiveness and salvation, such as the Sinner’s Prayer in which one confesses their sins and asks Jesus to come into their heart and be their Savior.", "annotation_id": "28453995", "url": "https://genius.com/28453995", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
