{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Change On Me", "line": "Don’t care ‘bout that money, I’m turnin’ it down", "vault_lines": ["Don't care 'bout that money, I'm turnin' it down"], "meaning": "Despite boasting his money and expensive items in several of his hit songs such as “Outside Today,” “Make No Sense,” and “Lil Top,” YoungBoy contrasts his previous materialistic views by explaining how — now that he’s even richer and more prominent in the rap industry — he doesn’t care about the money he receives as it can’t make his pain disappear.\n\nYoungBoy also mentions that he’s “turning [the money] down,” possibly referring to YoungBoy refusing a contract renewal from Atlantic Records.\n\nOn May 17, 2022, according to DJ Akademiks, it was announced that YoungBoy had rejected a $25 million record deal from his previous label, Atlantic Records. YoungBoy rejected the record deal due to his discomfort and continuous feud with his label, enabling him to make a statement about signing with them:\n\nDon’t sign to Atlantic unless you want to be a slave. I repeat, don’t", "annotation_id": "27001217", "url": "https://genius.com/27001217", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
