{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Closed Case", "line": "Helicopter on top me, I get gone, I’m not slowin’ down", "vault_lines": ["Helicopter on top me, I get gone, I'm not slowin' down"], "meaning": "During YoungBoy’s March 2021 federal arrest in California, officers attempted to stop the vehicle YB was in, resulting in him ditching the car and taking off on foot; he was later caught and arrested with reports noting that an LAPD helicopter was flying above the neighborhood attempting to find him.\n\nThe track’s official music video sees YoungBoy recreating his police chase:\n\n\n\nClip from the music video of “Closed Case” seeing YoungBoy reenacting his police chase with the helicopter", "annotation_id": "30924156", "url": "https://genius.com/30924156", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Closed Case", "line": "The FBI had took me down, they ain’t wan’ free me", "vault_lines": ["The FBI had took me down, they ain't wan' free me"], "meaning": "In two different instances, YoungBoy has been arrested and charged by the FBI. The first was in September 2020 regarding drug and firearm charges. The second was in March 2021 after fleeing from the police and being caught with firearms which YB took to trial in July 2022 and was found not guilty.\n\nYoungBoy states that the federal government is targeting him and is set to lock him up due to the multiple charges he’s racked up.\n\nHe notes that the government doesn’t want him to be free, referring to him being on house arrest since October 2021. Despite filing several motions with the courts to amend his regulations to allow him to perform, he continues to stay on 24-hour house arrest as of the song’s release.\n\n\n\nNBA YoungBoy after being found not guilty in his federal firearm case in California", "annotation_id": "30924036", "url": "https://genius.com/30924036", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Closed Case", "line": "Who walk in that bitch on money shit? Like Rue SanTan", "vault_lines": ["Who walk in that bitch on money shit? Like Rue SanTan"], "meaning": "These lyrics are a reference to  Bktherula’s 2022 song “TAN,” where she rapped along the chorus:\n\nWho walk in this bitch on some money shit?\nRue Santan (Yeah)\n\n“Rue Satan” is also Bktherula’s alter ego, which she experimented with in songs such as “SANTANNY.”", "annotation_id": "30916249", "url": "https://genius.com/30916249", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
