{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Cook Dope", "line": "I know how to take, break, and make it shake and do it right like dynamite", "vault_lines": ["I know how to take, break, and make it shake and do it right like dynamite"], "meaning": "In the context of the track, “take” and “break” are slang terms often used in hip-hop to describe handling or using a woman in a sexual way — “take” meaning to have sex with her, and “break” meaning to have sex with her in a more intense or dominant way. “Make it shake” is a euphemism for having sex with her in a way that causes her to feel pleasure or arousal.\n\nThe phrase “do it right like dynamite” is a metaphor — “dynamite” here is used to suggest performing in a way that’s explosive, intense, and satisfying, as if the act is powerful and effective. It’s a common rap trope to use explosive imagery to convey confidence, skill, and dominance in sexual encounters.", "annotation_id": "38617242", "url": "https://genius.com/38617242", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
