{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Coordination", "line": "Under tint in them foreign cars (ayy)", "vault_lines": ["Under tint in them foreign cars (ayy)"], "meaning": "He’s riding in expensive imported vehicles with heavily tinted windows. The dark window tint hides who is inside the vehicle.\n\nThis ties directly into the previous line about staying off the radar.\n\nThe image is:\n\nYoungBoy sitting behind dark-tinted windows where nobody can easily identify or track him.", "annotation_id": "40144179", "url": "https://genius.com/40144179", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Coordination", "line": "I stay hidden from the radar (hidden from the radar)", "vault_lines": ["I stay hidden from the radar (hidden from the radar)"], "meaning": "He avoids detection and keeps a low profile. A Radar is technology used to track objects. Here it symbolises: Police surveillance,  Federal investigations,     Public scrutiny. Youngboy claims he knows how to move discreetly despite his fame.\n\nThis line creates tension with the first lyric.\n\nFirst he says:\n\n“The feds got us on they billboards.”\n\nThen:\n\n“I stay hidden from the radar.”\n\nThe contradiction is intentional.\n\nThe idea is:\n\n“They know who I am, but they don’t know where I am or what I’m doing.”\n\nIt’s the difference between being famous and being accessible.", "annotation_id": "40144176", "url": "https://genius.com/40144176", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Coordination", "line": "But you know that I ain’t goin’ for it (you know that I ain’t goin’ for it)", "vault_lines": ["But you know that I ain't goin' for it (you know that I ain't goin' for it)"], "meaning": "He’s refusing to accept being controlled, monitored, intimidated, or caught. The federal attention mentioned in the first line doesn’t scare him into changing his behaviour. He’s saying: “Even though they’re watching me, I’m not letting that stop me.”", "annotation_id": "40144137", "url": "https://genius.com/40144137", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Coordination", "line": "Feds got us on they billboards (got us on they billboards)", "vault_lines": ["Feds got us on they billboards (got us on they billboards)"], "meaning": "YoungBoy is saying that federal law enforcement agencies have made him and the people around him highly visible targets. He isn’t necessarily talking about actual roadside billboards. In street slang and rap, this often refers to, having photos circulated among law enforcement, being publicly identified by authorities, feeling like police and federal agents are constantly watching and tracking him. YoungBoy has dealt with numerous legal issues throughout his career. This line reflects a mindset common in street rap where success and notoriety bring increased attention from federal agencies.", "annotation_id": "40144129", "url": "https://genius.com/40144129", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
