{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Dangerous Love", "line": "Ran up my check, ain’t buy no vest, I’m still at war ’bout my set I say you pussy bitches play, we goin’ to war, it won’t end Walk down the streets over black coat with dirty rods tucked up in", "vault_lines": ["Walk down the streets over black coat with dirty rods tucked up in"], "meaning": "In these lines, Youngboy is saying he extremely rich now and he is truly never broke again, he still hasn’t bought a bulletproof vest because he feels like there’s no point if you’re still at war. He’s also saying that if the enemies try to start a war with him, due to his anger management issues and need to protect himself his family and his brand he will not stop once this war has started. He even expresses that it might get to the point where he himself is walking down the street in a black coat with illegal guns tucked beneath in pursuit.\n\nIronically, this was the cover of his album in 2021, The Last Slimeto, which shows him in an all black leather coat.", "annotation_id": "37067588", "url": "https://genius.com/37067588", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Dangerous Love", "line": "Hope you feel me, I’m diggin’ deep, from behind, I pull out your weave", "vault_lines": ["Hope you feel me, I'm diggin' deep, from behind, I pull out your weave"], "meaning": "In this line YoungBoy uses a double entendre, for the phrase digging deep. He uses it first by saying digging deep as in opening up, as an addition to the previous two lines. He also uses it in reference to sex in the next line as he says he is digging deep “from behind”. Hence why he says “hope you feel me”, to connect the double entendre to make sure she both understands his pain and feels his pleasure.", "annotation_id": "29562541", "url": "https://genius.com/29562541", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Dangerous Love", "line": "Or if the blogs been bashin’ me, they don’t wanna see me achieve, man, bitch please", "vault_lines": ["Or if the blogs been bashin' me, they don't wanna see me achieve, man, bitch please"], "meaning": "NBA Youngboy is yet again saying that the industry hates him. He states that online all the big articles always hate him and despise his name.", "annotation_id": "28835641", "url": "https://genius.com/28835641", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Dangerous Love", "line": "They gon’ hear about me from on the news or if they bump my CD", "vault_lines": ["They gon' hear about me from on the news or if they bump my CD"], "meaning": "Youngboy is saying he isn’t just famous from music, but also extremely infamous due to his crimes and this has helped him spread his music especially in his hometown of Baton Rouge.", "annotation_id": "28835634", "url": "https://genius.com/28835634", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Dangerous Love", "line": "Grandma baby, she died, drove me crazy, then I turned to the murder gang", "vault_lines": ["Grandma baby, she died, drove me crazy, then I turned to the murder gang"], "meaning": "NBA Youngboy’s father was serving a 55 year sentence, so he lived with his grandmother for 11 years until she died from a heart attack. This made him hate the world and he decided to go to the gang life. He was successful and got an ankle monitor at just 12 years old.", "annotation_id": "28835578", "url": "https://genius.com/28835578", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
