{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Dedicated", "line": "Like a pirate, I’m just searchin’ for some gold", "vault_lines": ["Like a pirate, I'm just searchin' for some gold"], "meaning": "Youngboy claims he is searching for his paper, how a pirate searches for gold. He is about the paper, how a pirate is about his gold.", "annotation_id": "36999256", "url": "https://genius.com/36999256", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Dedicated", "line": "They done slept on me and criticised me, talkin’ down", "vault_lines": ["They done slept on me and criticised me, talkin' down"], "meaning": "NBA Youngboy is no stranger to criticism, in fact throughout his entire career he’s faced heavy criticism. Most of his criticism comes from his never ending beefs (Gucci Mane, Lil Durk, Fredo Bang, YNW Melly, etc.) and considering these artists have fan bases of their own, it’s no surprise as to why this would get him public backlash. Also, much of his critiques are non constructive and attempts to ruin his brand and/ or gain social media attention.", "annotation_id": "29197209", "url": "https://genius.com/29197209", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Dedicated", "line": "As a youngin’ I been jumped up off that porch", "vault_lines": ["As a youngin' I been jumped up off that porch"], "meaning": "In music, “jumping off the porch” is a phrase commonly used to describe someone leaving their safety zone and going into risky/ dangerous measures to improve their life.", "annotation_id": "29197184", "url": "https://genius.com/29197184", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Dedicated", "line": "“You gotta get it, nigga,” that’s what I was told", "vault_lines": ["\"You gotta get it, nigga,\" that's what I was told"], "meaning": "Youngboy is referring to everyone that supported him on the come up of his career, telling him that he needs to get money.", "annotation_id": "28753421", "url": "https://genius.com/28753421", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Dedicated", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Youngboy-never-broke-again-dedicated-lyrics", "genius_title": "Dedicated", "genius_id": 3182579, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Deep Down", "line": "Please don’t let them youngins get close up on your car side You know YoungBoy got ‘em on you, you gon’ slip up and gon’ die, bitch", "vault_lines": ["You know YoungBoy got 'em on you, you gon' slip up and gon' die, bitch"], "meaning": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again appears to be reflecting on a past drive-by shooting incident he was involved in back in November 2016. According to the report, YoungBoy was the shooter out of the three passengers in the vehicle and allegedly shot the driver of the opposing car in the neck, which caused them to crash, fleeing the scene.\n\nYoungBoy Never Broke Again was charged with two counts of attempted second-degree murder, along with a $200,000 bond. On December 7, 2016, he was free of charge until further investigation.", "annotation_id": "30227661", "url": "https://genius.com/30227661", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Deep Down", "line": "Jump off the porch with dirty K’s, then watch my mama cry ’bout Dave", "vault_lines": ["Jump off the porch with dirty K's, then watch my mama cry 'bout Dave"], "meaning": "“[Jumping] off the porch” is a slang term to refer to someone joining a gang. YoungBoy notes that the death of his friend influenced his decision to join a gang.\n\nDavid “Lil Dave” Cobb’s name is commonly repeated throughout YoungBoy’s discography. Cobb was a close friend of YoungBoy who was shot and killed in March 2010 while at a “Rest in Peace” picnic. YoungBoy has referred to the loss of his friend as “traumatic” as he was just ten years old at the time of Cobb’s death.\n\nIn YoungBoy’s January 2022 track “Gangsta,” featuring Quando Rondo, he described how Cobb’s death influenced the way he’d continue to live his life, noting that he’d begin to carry a gun after his death:\n\nKnow I keep that iron, I remember when Lil Dave died", "annotation_id": "29937541", "url": "https://genius.com/29937541", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Deep Down", "line": "Deep, deep down in the water’s where I was raised, hey (Ooh) You’ll probably find the gun we knocked your mans off with", "vault_lines": ["Deep, deep down in the water's where I was raised, hey (Ooh)", "You'll probably find the gun we knocked your mans off with"], "meaning": "YoungBoy is stating that he grew up in “deep waters,” both a reference to being in difficult situations and the amount of waterways present in Louisiana, such as The Mississippi River — which flows through Baton Rouge, his hometown — or the numerous swamps in the state.\n\nYoungBoy is also saying that you could find the guns he and his partners killed someone with in these literal waters, which he’s referenced before on the track “Foolish Figure.”\n\nInside of Mississippi River, where we threw them choppers\nWe kill one with that same pistol, used to be my partner\nCan’t even tell you ‘bout it", "annotation_id": "29915723", "url": "https://genius.com/29915723", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
