{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Diamond Teeth Samurai", "line": "Tupac Shakur, ridin’ through the North up in the Bentley", "vault_lines": ["Tupac Shakur, ridin' through the North up in the Bentley"], "meaning": "Tupac Shakur was a famous rapper that came from the hood, Youngboy is comparing himself to Tupac since Youngboy is also a famous rapper from the hood. The only difference is that he is from the northside of Baton Rouge Lousiana whereas Tupac was from New York.", "annotation_id": "25773492", "url": "https://genius.com/25773492", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Diamond Teeth Samurai", "line": "23 shots, Lebron James I shoot the cavalier", "vault_lines": ["23 shots, Lebron James I shoot the cavalier"], "meaning": "Youngboy shouts out NBA player LeBron James. In 2014 after moving back to his original team, the Cleveland Cavaliers, he re-adopted the #23 on his jersey.", "annotation_id": "20643590", "url": "https://genius.com/20643590", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Diamond Teeth Samurai", "line": "Me and Meek Mill watchin’ movies in Rick Ross’ mansion", "vault_lines": ["Me and Meek Mill watchin' movies in Rick Ross' mansion"], "meaning": "In January 2014 Ross bought a 254-acre mansion previously owned by former heavyweight champion Evander Holyfield.\n\nThe mansion was built in 1994, it has a pool that holds 350,000 gallons of water, an indoor pool, a movie theater and a bowling alley. There are 12 bedrooms, and the dining room seats 100 people.\n\n\n\nMeek Mill is a rapper signed to Ross' Maybach Music Group label.  He was a cameo in the music video for Youngboy’s 2017 song “41”.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=onFsegQsdpk", "annotation_id": "18613112", "url": "https://genius.com/18613112", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Diamond Teeth Samurai", "line": "Whole lotta killin’, Helter Skelter like I’m Charles Manson", "vault_lines": ["Whole lotta killin', Helter Skelter like I'm Charles Manson"], "meaning": "Charles Manson was an American criminal, cult leader and musician. In mid-1967, he began forming what became known as the Manson Family, a quasi-commune based in California. Manson’s followers committed a series of nine murders at four locations in July and August 1969. In 1971, he was convicted of first-degree murder and conspiracy to commit murder for the deaths of seven people, all of which members of the group carried out at his instruction. Manson was also convicted of first-degree murder for two other deaths.\n Helter Skelter was a theory that the world would end because of rising racial tensions in the 1960s, and that there would have been all out war. Manson and his followers were convicted of the murders based on the prosecution’s theory that they were part of a plan to trigger the Helter Skelter scenario.", "annotation_id": "16691590", "url": "https://genius.com/16691590", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Diamond Teeth Samurai", "line": "I’m in the all white Porsche wit’ Fee ridin’ through Hollygrove", "vault_lines": ["I'm in the all white Porsche wit' Fee ridin' through Hollygrove"], "meaning": "Hollygrove is the hood in New Orleans where Lil Wayne grew up. YoungBoy is paying homage to Wayne throughout the song, including interpolating one of his songs for the bridge.\n\nFee Banks is a childhood friend of Wayne’s and fellow member of Hip-Hop group Sqad Up. Fee is also good friends with YoungBoy, with YoungBoy being featured all over Fee’s Instagram page.", "annotation_id": "14383327", "url": "https://genius.com/14383327", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Diamond Teeth Samurai", "line": "Nigga, you got that yayo?", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, you got that yayo? (Well cook somethin' nigga)"], "meaning": "Yayo is slang for the highly addictive drug, cocaine. This slang word was first used by the Cuban drug lord, Antonio “Tony” Montana, A.K.A. “Scarface” in the movie Scarface.", "annotation_id": "14250336", "url": "https://genius.com/14250336", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Diamond Teeth Samurai", "line": "Curtis Jackson, ain’t no actin’ when I’m on a mission", "vault_lines": ["Curtis Jackson, ain't no actin' when I'm on a mission"], "meaning": "Curtis Jackson a.k.a. 50 Cent is an American Rapper from South Jamaica, Queens, New York. He is known for having being shot point-blank nine times and surviving the incident.\n\nWith this line YBNBA could be alluding to the fact that 50 keeps everything real, and doesn’t put on a fake persona. The two of them are both genuine, and really live the lives that they describe in their music.", "annotation_id": "14237287", "url": "https://genius.com/14237287", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Diamond Teeth Samurai", "line": "I’m a Bad Boy, never met Diddy but that’s what it is", "vault_lines": ["I'm a Bad Boy, never met Diddy but that's what it is"], "meaning": "Referencing one of Diddy’s most popular songs “Bad Boy for Life”.\n\nDiddy is also the founder and owner of Bad Boy Records.", "annotation_id": "14236822", "url": "https://genius.com/14236822", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Diamond Teeth Samurai", "line": "(Well cook somethin’ nigga) Nigga, you let them Ks go? (Well bust somethin’ nigga) Are you duckin’ them laws? (You better run from them nigga) Are you playin’ with that raw? (Well look here, front somethin’ nigga)", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, you let them Ks go? (Well bust somethin' nigga)", "Are you duckin' them laws? (You better run from them nigga)"], "meaning": "During the bridge, Youngboy puts his own Cash Money spin on the track, paying homage to Lil Wayne’s debut studio album, Tha Block Is Hot, as well as the chorus to the iconic single.\n\nHe specifically payed the most tribute months before this song’s release with a snippet released on Instagram, where he built up hype by reciting the bridge:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YRL_uD60n-w", "annotation_id": "14229216", "url": "https://genius.com/14229216", "state": "accepted", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
