{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Diamonds", "line": "I hope I motivate your soul", "vault_lines": ["I hope I motivate your soul"], "meaning": "This line completes the foregoing line where he explains how people can only see his success. He hopes to motivate those who see him and his accomplishments, he knows that nothing comes easy but while accepting that people don’t see things in a bigger perspective he’s content with giving them some sort of drive.", "annotation_id": "25771861", "url": "https://genius.com/25771861", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Diamonds", "line": "These niggas ain’t seen me when I jumped out, they just seen all these diamonds", "vault_lines": ["These niggas ain't seen me when I jumped out, they just seen all these diamonds"], "meaning": "People only see YoungBoys success and not the history behind it. His diamonds could be a symbol not only for his jewelry but also everything else he has achieved.\n\nThe struggles he went through to get where he is today remains in “his diamonds”. It’s only the diamonds that is visible to the public and not what’s behind.", "annotation_id": "25771773", "url": "https://genius.com/25771773", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
