{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Diamonds", "line": "I wish my grandmother could see me now, ’cause I say I’m that nigga now", "vault_lines": ["I wish my grandmother could see me now, 'cause I say I'm that nigga now"], "meaning": "In these lines, YoungBoy reminisces about his grandmother and the influence she had on him. He keeps with the similar tone to the opener of 38 Baby 2, “Bout My Business,” on which he raps similar bars:\n\nI wish my grandma was right here standin' on side of me", "annotation_id": "19659963", "url": "https://genius.com/19659963", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
