{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Digital", "line": "Baseball", "vault_lines": ["My old-head, he like to play baseball"], "meaning": "*Days of Old\n\nDays of Ild is a song by B.B. King and Eric Clapton, hence being called “Old Head.” This line also pays homage to Louisiana’s being the historical epicenter of Jazz. Finally this can be heard in YB’s other songs which obviously have a huge “Bayou Jazz” influence with the large but short note swings in his other songs. See Long Live, ect.", "annotation_id": "26488030", "url": "https://genius.com/26488030", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Digital", "line": "This pack what I’m smokin’ famous", "vault_lines": ["This pack what I'm smokin' famous"], "meaning": "Smoking a “pack” primarily refers to one mocking an oppositions death by saying they’re smoking them. The term is often used in the rap industry and has even been used by YoungBoy himself in “Bring The Hook” where he disses the late King Von:\n\nNigga, this that Squid Game, O'Block pack get rolled up\nMurder what they told us, Atlanta boy get fold up\n\nHere, YoungBoy Never Broke Again could again be speaking on King Von’s death due to his altercation with Lil Durk with both of their diss tracks — “AHHH HA” and “I Hate YoungBoy” — going viral on social media — ultimately causing a split in the music industry.\n\nFurthermore, Von is a famous and influential artist in the music industry, collaborating with some of the most significant rap acts such as Polo G and YNW Melly.\n\nLastly, YoungBoy could be referencing the death of JayDaYoungan with whom he had several altercations prior to his untimely death.", "annotation_id": "26452013", "url": "https://genius.com/26452013", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Digital", "line": "Digital scale with a digital pole", "vault_lines": ["Digital scale with a digital pole"], "meaning": "A “digital scale” refers to a regular compact scale along with a digital display. However, in this case, NBA YoungBoy sets use to the scale via measuring drugs—supposedly marijuana,— as well as dealers and gang members to sell them to regular customers.\n\n\n\nPictured: A digital scale.\n\nHowever, following that, a “digital pole” alludes to a thermometer, in order to clearly make out the temperature of the drugs, more often made in trap houses to avoid suspicion from the police.", "annotation_id": "26451669", "url": "https://genius.com/26451669", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
