{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Dirty Iyanna", "line": "After I’m asking “Can we have a child?”", "vault_lines": ["After I'm asking \"Can we have a child?\""], "meaning": "In January of 2021, NBA YoungBoy did have a child with Iyanna\n\nhttps://www.thesun.co.uk/news/13789691/floyd-mayweather-daughter-nba-youngboy-seventh-kid/", "annotation_id": "21937099", "url": "https://genius.com/21937099", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Dirty Iyanna", "line": "I see she won’t leave me ’lone She slashed the tires on my car", "vault_lines": ["I see she won't leave me 'lone", "She slashed the tires on my car"], "meaning": "YoungBoy seemingly references a conflict he had with his former girlfriend, Iyanna Mayweather, the daughter of all-time great boxer Floyd Mayweather, and maybe the inspiration of the title of this song.\n\nYoungBoy accused Iyanna of slashing his tires in March via an Instagram story, and seemingly brings the issue up again in this track.", "annotation_id": "18674035", "url": "https://genius.com/18674035", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Dirty Iyanna", "line": "Dirty Iyanna, oh Dirty Iyanna, oh Dirty Iyanna, oh Dirty Iyanna", "vault_lines": ["Dirty Iyanna, Dirty Iyanna"], "meaning": "YoungBoy samples and interpolates Michael Jackson’s “Dirty Diana.” On the 1987 track, Jackson expresses his frustration with groupies who aggressively sought to seduce him:\n\nDirty Diana, nah\nDirty Diana, nah\nDirty Diana, no\nDirty Diana, let me be!\nOh no, oh no, oh no\n\nHere, YoungBoy could be referencing his past relationship with Iyanna Mayweather, daughter of boxer Floyd Mayweather. As mentioned on Genius' Song Stories, YoungBoy’s short-lived relationship with Iyanna came to a close after he accused her of slashing his tires.", "annotation_id": "18673429", "url": "https://genius.com/18673429", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Dirty Iyanna", "line": "Still trappin’ like Griselda", "vault_lines": ["Still trappin' like Griselda"], "meaning": "Griselda Blanco, otherwise known as La Madrina or the Godmother of Cocaine, was a major Colombian cocaine trafficker through the Medellín Cartel, founded by Pablo Escobar. Responsible for more than 200 murders, she played a central role in the violent Miami drug wars of the 1970s and 1980s.\n\nDespite spending much of 2019 under house arrest, YoungBoy maintains that his actions can still be compared to Griselda.\n\n\n\nIt is also worth noting that YoungBoy has mentioned Griselda Blanco in previous songs such as “Slime Belief”:\n\nCan you make it better? Trap out like Griselda", "annotation_id": "18673335", "url": "https://genius.com/18673335", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
