{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Don’t Leave", "line": "I done let go of the wheel, like I just know it’s God drivin’ But I mostly for surely know that it’s my grandma who got me", "vault_lines": ["I done let go of the wheel, like I just know it's God drivin'", "But I mostly for surely know that it's my grandma who got me"], "meaning": "Here YoungBoy mentions his late grandmother, Alice, who he refers to in many of his other songs. He credits her for being the woman who raised him.", "annotation_id": "29174887", "url": "https://genius.com/29174887", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
