{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Double My Cup", "line": "And I know that he hurt, he was in, they knock Dump off", "vault_lines": ["And I know that he hurt, he was in, they knock Dump off"], "meaning": "Desmond, who is mainly known as Big Dump, who was YoungBoy’s former manager, died on May, 2018.\nRumours was that it was TBG members that did this, which Big Dump as someone ran towards his car and shot at him. This TBG vs NBA beef was born since Gee money dissed YoungBoy, while YB’s song talks about Gee being his brother, but doing stuff with his sister in, “Pour one”, and with YoungBoy being BBG, Bottom Boy Gorillaz, while TBG being Top Boy Gorillaz.\n\nThere are two songs dedicated to Big Dump,\n“Dear Dump” having two different files, which one has a finished mixing with heavier bass and louder verses, while one is more calm and unfinished.\nThe other being, “Letter To Big Dump” which is a 9 minute song that talks about YoungBoy’s life and how he’s been coping with the loss ever since.\n\nLater on, YoungBoy disses TBG even more, and talks about dump’s death in later songs (Unreleased and released), by often paying respect and talking about him.", "annotation_id": "39267848", "url": "https://genius.com/39267848", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
