{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Dropout", "line": "38 Baby 2", "vault_lines": ["(uh, rock out) yeah bitch, 38 Baby 2"], "meaning": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again released a mixtape titled 38 Baby 2 on April 24, 2020. Originally, the mixtape was set to release sometime between October and November 2018, but was delayed due to unknown reasons.\n\n\n\nOriginal album cover for ‘38 Baby 2’", "annotation_id": "27130464", "url": "https://genius.com/27130464", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Dropout", "line": "I’m a rich fuckin’ dropout", "vault_lines": ["Want smoke? we gon' rock out, I'm a rich fuckin' dropout (yeah)"], "meaning": "Youngboy dropped out of school at 9th grade to focus on his rap career but was later arrested and sent to a detention center due to a robbery that he allegedly committed. Despite the legal troubles, his talents were noticed and landed him a record deal with Atlantic Records", "annotation_id": "25990600", "url": "https://genius.com/25990600", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
