{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "FWYT", "line": "Bitch, I’m big Velveeta", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm big Velveeta"], "meaning": "Calling himself “big Velveeta” plays on the cheese brand Velveeta, using “cheese” as slang for money. The line serves as a boast about financial success, a common rap metaphor where wealth is equated with cheese, reinforcing YoungBoy’s status following his commercial dominance during the early 2020s.", "annotation_id": "38740747", "url": "https://genius.com/38740747", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "FWYT", "line": "She don’t even know one song, but know she know about me (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["She don't even know one song, but know she know about me (Woah)"], "meaning": "YoungBoy points out how his fame extends beyond his music, suggesting people recognize his public image or reputation even if they are unfamiliar with his catalog. The line reflects the heightened visibility he experienced during the Top and Sincerely, Kentrell eras, when legal issues and constant media attention made his personal life as recognizable as his music career.", "annotation_id": "38740729", "url": "https://genius.com/38740729", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
