{"type": "song", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "FWYT", "status": "done", "targets": 14, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Youngboy-never-broke-again-fwyt-lyrics", "genius_title": "FWYT", "genius_id": 12980156, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Fact", "line": "This for the ones who betrayed me (Who betrayed me) Say you with me, but you hate me (You hate me) I feel like you tryna snake me (Huh?) Boy, what the fuck is you thinkin’? (Boy) On the block clutchin’ a banger (Huh?) Gettin’ loaded, just me and Lil’ Ben (Lil’ Ben) We had to run from the laws (The laws), we got away again (Again) Grindin’ and stackin’ them M’s (Them M’s) Want money, I don’t want no friends (I don’t want no friends) On the Megabus by myself, with the pints in my bag (My bag) That’s Lil’ Ben (Hello?) Nigga play around with that sack (What?) So we loaded with them straps (We strapped) Pap and OG in the back (In the back) Floatin’ ’round Park Forest (Yeah) We tryna see where they at (Where they at) Catch ’em, hit ’em, boom Put his shit straight on the flat (Pow) I had a show up in XO, you know I turnt up bad (Bad) I was stuntin’ wit’ the cash (Cash) These niggas know we ain’t friends (Nah)", "vault_lines": ["This for the ones who betrayed me (Who betrayed me)", "Say you with me, but you hate me (You hate me)", "I feel like you tryna snake me (Huh?)"], "meaning": "This section of the song is a deep dive into NBA YoungBoy’s mindset, betrayed by people he trusted, constantly on edge, emotionally numb, and focused only on money and survival. It’s both a memoir of his past life on the streets and a statement of who he is now, hard, untrusting, and emotionally guarded. The lyrics blend pain, loyalty, violence, and ambition into a powerful testimony of trauma and resilience.", "annotation_id": "35681033", "url": "https://genius.com/35681033", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Fact", "line": "They wanna kill me cause I’m next to blow", "vault_lines": ["They wanna kill me cause I'm next to blow"], "meaning": "Some people gon be jealous when you tryna get rich", "annotation_id": "35681016", "url": "https://genius.com/35681016", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Fact", "line": "I remember I ain’t had nothin’ I had to go get some racks (Some racks) I was hustlin’ at the store, tryna get me some cash (Some cash) A month ago I was broke, I ain’t never goin’ back (Them days) In these streets it ain’t no joke, so you know I keep a strap (Ayy)", "vault_lines": ["A month ago I was broke, I ain't never goin' back (Them days)", "In these streets it ain't no joke, so you know I keep a strap (Ayy)"], "meaning": "These lyrics paint a vivid picture of rising from poverty through grit, hustle, and survival, with an undercurrent of street realism. NBA YoungBoy is emphasizing how far he’s come in a short time, how dangerous his environment was (and still may be), and how his past shapes his current mindset. It’s a testament to resilience, but also a cautionary tale about what it took to get there.", "annotation_id": "35681015", "url": "https://genius.com/35681015", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
