{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Feel Good", "line": "I got power with this 50 Glock, make you take off all your Cuban links", "vault_lines": ["I got power with this 50 Glock, make you take off all your Cuban links"], "meaning": "I got (power) with this (50) Gluck, make you take off all your (Cuban links).\n\nIn this line yb Referring to “50 Cent” and his TV Show, “Power\"\n\n“Cuban links” is a style of jewelry but it also the name of 50cent girlfriend", "annotation_id": "26204486", "url": "https://genius.com/26204486", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Feel Good", "line": "Dancin’ around like Raven, you my cheetah", "vault_lines": ["Dancin' around like Raven, you my cheetah"], "meaning": "Raven was a star on Disney’s hit kid’s show The Cheetah Girls.", "annotation_id": "26199405", "url": "https://genius.com/26199405", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Feel Good", "line": "No “Pat-a-Cake,” I’m Babe Ruth, hittin’ it for the home run", "vault_lines": ["No \"Pat-a-Cake,\" I'm Babe Ruth, hittin' it for the home run"], "meaning": "“Pat-a-Cake” is an old, English nursery rhyme that was first known to originate in the 1600s. The children’s nursery rhyme is often accompanied by its own dance.\n\nGeorge Herman Ruth, Jr., most notably known as Babe Ruth was a Baltimore, Maryland-born professional Baseball player who played in the MLB from 1914 through 1935.\n\nYoungBoy brings up Ruth and his impressive ability to hit a home run as Ruth was and still is one of the MLB’s most respected, and greatest players. Ruth is known widely for his ability to score a home run, achieving the highest score for a total of twelve seasons prior to his retirement and unfortunate death. He is among three other players to achieve over 700 home runs.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HkEX0eb2eBo\nPictured: Babe Ruth’s 1932 World Series home run\n\nHome runs being extremely hard to score, ensuring players run the whole route without stopping at any of the bases, YoungBoy describes how he aims to do things as successful despite the difficulties, or any obstacles in his path.", "annotation_id": "26194366", "url": "https://genius.com/26194366", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
