{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Fly Away", "line": "Girl, look, what I drive You ain’t gotta tell me no lie, you gon’ make me think you playin’ with my mind Be yourself, you just my type, yeah, I don’t really run ’cross your kind She amazed by the BNB, my crib might fuck up her whole mind", "vault_lines": ["Girl, look, what I drive", "You ain't gotta tell me no lie, you gon' make me think you playin' with my mind", "Be yourself, you just my type, yeah, I don't really run 'cross your kind", "She amazed by the BNB, my crib might fuck up her whole mind"], "meaning": "Literally, YoungBoy points to his high-end vehicle as a symbol of his established status, repeating that she doesn’t need to play mind games or lie to impress him. He tells her to simply be her authentic self, calling her his exact type and noting how rare women like her are, before concluding with how completely overwhelmed she is by the sheer luxury of the mansion or Airbnb he lives in. – Gemini AI", "annotation_id": "40395142", "url": "https://genius.com/40395142", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Fly Away", "line": "[Chorus] And all for you, I travel miles away And all for you, I go about my way With your love I be runnin’, I won’t fumble Come with me, I don’t need to leave you with my number", "vault_lines": ["And all for you, I travel miles away", "And all for you, I go about my way", "With your love I be runnin', I won't fumble", "Come with me, I don't need to leave you with my number"], "meaning": "YoungBoy declares that he is willing to go entirely out of his way, and travel anywhere to go see a specific woman. He states that her affection gives him the drive and focus to keep moving forward without making mistakes, and he urges her to run away with him permanently, noting that they have no need to exchange phone numbers. – Gemini AI", "annotation_id": "40394805", "url": "https://genius.com/40394805", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Fly Away", "line": "The young niggas wildin’, now Work, no clockin’ out Whole team got me shinin’, woo Know I’m poppin’ out Stack money, need I’ll buy ya new Jimmy Choo", "vault_lines": ["The young niggas wildin', now", "Work, no clockin' out", "Whole team got me shinin', woo", "Know I'm poppin' out", "I'll buy ya new Jimmy Choo"], "meaning": "YoungBoy describes how the youth in this new generation are behaving recklessly, and how he grinds with no breaks. He credits his team for elevating and keeping him looking successful, states that he goes outside with no fear in mind, and how he’s obsessed with stacking money. He ends the sequence by stating that he uses this money to purchase Jimmy Choo footwear for a specific woman.", "annotation_id": "40394796", "url": "https://genius.com/40394796", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Fly Away", "line": "Been in situations, that wasn’t his fault, and plus he beat some cases Your love got my heart racin’ When we argue, it make me think ‘bout separation and that’s just somethin’ that bother", "vault_lines": ["Been in situations, that wasn't his fault, and plus he beat some cases", "Your love got my heart racin'"], "meaning": "YoungBoy talks about being in dangerous situations that could’ve led to jail time that were not his fault and how he managed to overcome the justice system, and win his freedom. He then shifts to a deeply personal confession, admitting that his love to a specific woman causes his anxiety to rise immediately. He notes that whenever they get into a disagreement, it makes him think the relationship is over.", "annotation_id": "40394784", "url": "https://genius.com/40394784", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Fly Away", "line": "Bases loaded, this a major trait that I’m at a major base and I’m finna take it in Hustlin’, he come in late Know I wait for you to play, I’ma shoot that Glock straight at your face", "vault_lines": ["Bases loaded, this a major trait that I'm at a major base and I'm finna take it in", "Hustlin', he come in late", "Know I wait for you to play, I'ma shoot that Glock straight at your face"], "meaning": "He begins with a baseball metaphor to celebrate his own massive success and momentum, stating that the bases are loaded and he is about to bring a victory home. He then goes into third-person and talks about a man who is out hustling late to stack extra money. Finally, he delivers a warning to everyone, stating that he is ready for someone to try to kill or take something from him so he can meet them with immediate, lethal gunfire.", "annotation_id": "40394740", "url": "https://genius.com/40394740", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Fly Away", "line": "I treat her different, make her figure when I do her like that I ain’t mean to treat her like that How can you treat her that way?", "vault_lines": ["I treat her different, make her figure when I do her like that", "I ain't mean to treat her like that", "How can you treat her that way?"], "meaning": "YoungBoy is talking about how he treats a woman so terribly, leaving her to question his decisions. He expresses his regret for his hot-and-cold behavior, but then abruptly directs his attention to her actual boyfriend, questioning how that man can treat her so poorly when he has her as his girl.", "annotation_id": "40394624", "url": "https://genius.com/40394624", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Fly Away", "line": "Never let you lift me up to bring me down and break me, nigga Know that I could lift her up and take her down to break the nigga But the truth is that I fuck with her, don’t wan’ do her like that", "vault_lines": ["Know that I could lift her up and take her down to break the nigga"], "meaning": "YoungBoy explicitly states that he wouldn’t dare let anyone play him foolish. He then immediately flips the exact same psychological tactic onto his rival, boasting that he has the power to sexually dominate the rival’s girlfriend, an act that would utterly destroy that man’s pride. However, he immediately checks himself, stating that because he genuinely cares for her and respects her, he refuses to weaponize her body or ruin her life just to hurt his enemy.", "annotation_id": "40394590", "url": "https://genius.com/40394590", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Fly Away", "line": "Know my daddy was a gangster, my uncle rode inside them caddies, too", "vault_lines": ["Know my daddy was a gangster, my uncle rode inside them caddies, too"], "meaning": "YoungBoy is talking about how his father, Jeffery Staden, and his uncle were gangster figures from the hood who cruised the neighborhood in classic Cadillacs (“caddies”) looking for crimes to commit. This lifestyle culminated in a devastating 2007 or 2008 armed robbery when YoungBoy was just eight years old, resulting in his father being sentenced to 55 years in prison after his uncle snitched to get off the hook.\n\nThere’s a deeper meaning behind this that shows a deep and painful contrast between loyalty and betrayal within the same bloodline. While the uncle chose to rat to secure freedom, Jeffery Staden took the massive 55-year sentence on the chin, staying solid and never squealing. Having served roughly 18 to 19 years of that time already, his father still faces about 36 to 37 years remaining on his countdown.", "annotation_id": "40394517", "url": "https://genius.com/40394517", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Fly Away", "line": "Through the night, try to make it right, I’m talkin’ miles away She dealt with pain, say, “I been through the same,” her pops work like a slave", "vault_lines": ["She dealt with pain, say, \"I been through the same,\" her pops work like a slave"], "meaning": "YoungBoy describes staying up through the late-night hours trying to resolve an emotional conflict with a woman while he is physically miles away. He notes that she has experienced significant emotional suffering in her life, and he communicates to her that he has endured that exact same kind of pain. He finishes by acknowledging her dad for working hard, like a slave.", "annotation_id": "40394490", "url": "https://genius.com/40394490", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Fly Away", "line": "Stuck inside the streets’ll make you feel like ain’t no wrong in life She love him more than anything, feel like he won’t lead her wrong in life", "vault_lines": ["She love him more than anything, feel like he won't lead her wrong in life"], "meaning": "YoungBoy explicitly states that being a street dude makes you think sin is just a part of life since it’s all you’re used to. YoungBoy is making up dialogue about a male who is living a lawless lifestyle alongside a woman who is completely devoted to him. He explains how her love for the man is so strong that she’s too delusional to see that he’d lead her wrong with the choices he makes.", "annotation_id": "40394487", "url": "https://genius.com/40394487", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Fly Away", "line": "In the streets, where I grew, your life at risk, so you just pray that you make it out", "vault_lines": ["In the streets, where I grew, your life at risk, so you just pray that you make it out"], "meaning": "YoungBoy reflects on the dangers of the neighborhood that raised him, explicitly stating that survival in that environment is never a guarantee and ultimately requires genuine prayer just to make it out alive.\n\nThe subtext deals with the deep, lingering trauma of a survivor mentally, even though YoungBoy achieved the dream of escaping poverty and making it out of his environment physically. Framing his escape around “prayer” rather than just hard work or talent emphasizes just how random and perilous street life is, where living to see another day feels like an act of divine luck.\n\nThis section serves as a heavy, grounding reality check within the verse. It strips away the glamour of fame and luxury, forcing the listener to remember the violent, high-stakes backdrop that shaped YoungBoy’s hardened perspective and survival instincts.", "annotation_id": "40394480", "url": "https://genius.com/40394480", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
