{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Food (Kill Or Take)", "line": "And I’m a drug user (Drug user) I ain’t never mistreated her (I ain’t never mistreated her) She the one abusive (One abusive) And she love when I use her Inside I feel like tearin’ up She know what she doin’", "vault_lines": ["And I'm a drug user (Drug user)", "I ain't never mistreated her (I ain't never mistreated her)", "She the one abusive (One abusive)", "And she love when I use her", "Inside I feel like tearin' up", "She know what she doin'"], "meaning": "YoungBoy is not talking about a girl. Instead, he is putting the gender of a female on the different types of drugs he uses. Talking about how he uses narcotics, never mistreated them and how they’re the one abusive. Figuratively putting the blame on the drugs for his actions, and not himself. As drugs can make you someone you’re not when your high kicks in. Says the drugs love when he uses them. While inside he feels like crying, he says the drugs knows exactly what they’re doing.", "annotation_id": "40958851", "url": "https://genius.com/40958851", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
