{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "For a Reason", "line": "And I ain’t cut no corners with you I’ma fucking say it I got a strong feeling I’ma prolly end up dead", "vault_lines": ["And I ain't cut no corners with you Imma fucking say it"], "meaning": "When YoungBoy was a teenager, a kid even, he got into a lot of gang stuff (as he probably insinuates in the two last lines of the second verse), like gang-banging and etc. Anybody related to that life can die due to relations or any problems beetween gangs.", "annotation_id": "39605061", "url": "https://genius.com/39605061", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "For a Reason", "line": "They killed my nigga Dave Man", "vault_lines": ["They killed my nigga Dave Man (for a reason)"], "meaning": "Lil Dave (real name David Cobb) was YB’s cousin, and was very close to him. In 2010, Lil Dave was shot and killed in a party and was held a funeral. Journalist Naomi Martin provided a journal entry, which said:\n\n“David Cobb, 16, was shot during a party at a BREC park on Woodpecker Street on March 27, 2010. A fight broke out and bullets started flying, one of which hit Cobb in his spine. He later died in a hospital.\n\nThe party had attracted hundreds of people over several hours, Gertrude Cobb said. Despite the potential for eyewitnesses, the case has gone cold in the Baton Rouge Police Department’s file.\n\n“There were too many people out there not to know what happened,” Cobb said, her voice breaking.”\n\nNBA YoungBoy has several released and unreleased tracks about Lil Dave. Lil Dave meant very much for NBA YoungBoy in his early life in Baton Rouge.", "annotation_id": "39467224", "url": "https://genius.com/39467224", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "For a Reason", "line": "My daddy use to lie to me", "vault_lines": ["My daddy use to lie to me"], "meaning": "Could be how some dads lie to their kids about stuff, but in this context he could be referring to several thing before his dad got booked for 55 years in prison.\nHis dad could’ve lied about many things thats heart breaking and something for kids to remember once they are older.", "annotation_id": "38767982", "url": "https://genius.com/38767982", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
