{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "For a Reason", "line": "Police told me, my momma she my best friend", "vault_lines": ["Police told me my Momma she my best friend"], "meaning": "When kids often get in trouble or just in general, the police always comforts and mentors the young kids or teens, in order for them to not cause any trouble and go down a bad path.\n\nIn this sentence, he just saying that the police wants him to know that his mom, he can always listen to her and talk to her about stuff.", "annotation_id": "38536579", "url": "https://genius.com/38536579", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "For a Reason", "line": "Charge it to the game", "vault_lines": ["But everything that happen a blessing charge it to the game"], "meaning": "You just accept a win, loss, or mistake and say “Mane I can’t do nothing about it, or change, all I gotta do is move on and go forward” (Charging it to the game)", "annotation_id": "38536568", "url": "https://genius.com/38536568", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
