{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Games of War", "line": "Nigga, I was broken as a child, but learned to cope with pain", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, I was broken as a child, but learned to cope with pain"], "meaning": "YoungBoy reflects on a rough childhood, where emotional scars ran deep. “Broken” speaks to trauma, not just poverty. Learning to “cope with pain” shows he didn’t heal — he adapted. It’s survival, not recovery.", "annotation_id": "36409454", "url": "https://genius.com/36409454", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Games of War", "line": "I got some bitches, they my gang, initiated like Mulan", "vault_lines": ["I got some bitches, they my gang, initiated like Mulan"], "meaning": "NBA YoungBoy is saying he has women who are loyal to him like gang members — they’ve been “initiated” into his crew. The mention of Mulan refers to the Disney character who disguised herself as a man to join the army, symbolizing bravery and commitment. So, he’s comparing these women to Mulan — implying they’re tough, loyal, and willing to go to war for him.", "annotation_id": "36359873", "url": "https://genius.com/36359873", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Games of War", "line": "Then I fell in love with that chopper just like Tay-K", "vault_lines": ["Then I fell in love with that chopper just like Tay-K"], "meaning": "In this line, NBA YoungBoy references Tay-K’s song “I <3 My Choppa”, a cult track from the Texas rapper where he expresses his attachment to firearms. By saying “I fell in love with that chopper just like Tay-K”, YoungBoy isn’t just talking about using weapons, he’s echoing a specific rap moment and persona. It’s a nod to Tay-K’s early notoriety and the fascination with violence in youth culture, especially within the trap scene. The reference connects both artists through a shared imagery of danger, rebellion, and fame at a young age.\n\n\n\nIn rap and street slang, a “chopper” is a nickname for a fully automatic weapon, usually an AK-47 or a similar assault rifle. It’s called a chopper because of the “chopping” sound it makes when firing rapidly.", "annotation_id": "36359822", "url": "https://genius.com/36359822", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Games of War", "line": "Boomer", "vault_lines": ["Boomer take your ass down like a task force"], "meaning": "Boomer also known as NBA Big B or NBA SelfPaid", "annotation_id": "36358896", "url": "https://genius.com/36358896", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Games of War", "line": "Hold on, hold on, just left, Karl Malone (Ayy)", "vault_lines": ["Hold on, hold on, just left, Karl Malone (Ayy)"], "meaning": "Here YoungBoy is referencing the NBA player Karl Malone who is famously known for his time spent on the Utah Jazz.\n\nYoungBoy previously spent 3.5 years on house arrest in Utah. Being released in March 2025", "annotation_id": "36356181", "url": "https://genius.com/36356181", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Games of War", "line": "Bitch, I got the wave, I could grab my phone and hit up Rod", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I got the wave, I could grab my phone and hit up Rod"], "meaning": "Shouting out rapper and singer Rod Wave. They are known to be good friends\n\nThey’ve collaborated on tracks such as “Better Than Ever” and “Home Ain’t Home”\n\nhttps://images.app.goo.gl/MxMPrVL9nmDbLcGD7", "annotation_id": "36354040", "url": "https://genius.com/36354040", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Games of War", "line": "Nigga, I’ve been gettin’ money like the Juiceman (Ayy)", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, I've been gettin' money like the Juiceman (Ayy)"], "meaning": "Here YB is referencing OJ Da Juiceman’s 2008 single “I’m Getting’ Money” then uses OJ’s Signature Adlib “Aye”", "annotation_id": "36352428", "url": "https://genius.com/36352428", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Games of War", "line": "Skrrt, skrrt, that’s a brand-new Range, now catch up with me", "vault_lines": ["Skrrt, skrrt, that's a brand-new Range, now catch up with me"], "meaning": "“Range \"refers  to \"Range Rover”, a specific brand of luxury off-road vehicles manufactured by Land Rover. Although often used synonymously with “Land Rover,” Range Rover is actually a specific model within the Land Rover lineup, similar to how “Mustang” is a specific Ford model.", "annotation_id": "36352349", "url": "https://genius.com/36352349", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Games of War", "line": "I come straight from the concrete", "vault_lines": ["I been gettin' money, bitch, I come straight from the concrete"], "meaning": "The slang term “from the concrete” is often used to describe someone who is considered street-smart, resourceful, and resilient, having grown up in an urban environment, particularly one characterized by hardship or a lack of privilege. It implies a certain toughness and ability to navigate challenging situations.", "annotation_id": "36352319", "url": "https://genius.com/36352319", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
