{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Gangsta", "line": "Know I keep that iron, I remember when Lil Dave died", "vault_lines": ["Know I keep that iron, I remember when Lil Dave died"], "meaning": "David Cobb aka Lil Dave was an young Baton Rouge hoodstar. He was born on May 29, 1993.\nHe was shot during a party on Woodpecker Street on March 27, 2010, at the age of 16.\nYoungBoy mentioned this incident on Rich The Kid’s track “For Keeps.”\n\nDave died from that chopper at 16, wish I can call him", "annotation_id": "25060118", "url": "https://genius.com/25060118", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Gangsta", "line": "Sex, money, and murder, plus, Lil Dee hold fire like Damu (Damu)", "vault_lines": ["Sex, money, and murder, plus, Lil Dee hold fire like Damu (Damu)"], "meaning": "Lil Dee is Youngboy’s cousin. As he raps in “Bring the Hook.”\n\nLil Dee, that’s my cousin, man\n\nSex Money Murder is a street gang operating on the East Coast of the United States. It is one of the original sets of the Bloods. Youngboy often claims to be part of the Bloods gang.", "annotation_id": "25060075", "url": "https://genius.com/25060075", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Gangsta", "line": "(Mario)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Supah Mario is a North American Music Producer best known for his work with Drake, Young Thug, and Lil Uzi Vert.\n\nFrom a very early age, Supah Mario was exposed to, and captivated by, music. At the age of three, he flourished with playing the drums in his church.\nAs time progressed, Supah Mario began “making beats and writing songs at twelve” and began to cultivate and expand in the art of music earnestly once at the age of sixteen.\n\nIf average music is a product of the planet Earth, then Columbia, South Carolina born-and-bred producer/writer, Supah Mario… is from beyond the asteroid belt…. Supah Mario’s creations know no boundaries, and has combined influences from all genres to create an idiosyncratic and dynamic harmony that is highly sought after by emcees and vocalists, but rarely found. Supah Mario has mastered the ranging soundscapes of hip-hop and is experimenting with other genres. Mario continues to challenge the boundaries of hip-hop and forge genre-bending creations for artists from all walks.\n\nFrom Supah Mario’s soundcloud page.", "annotation_id": "25059991", "url": "https://genius.com/25059991", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Gangsta", "line": "Industry don’t like me ‘cause I’m thuggin’ and I’m dangerous (Brrah)", "vault_lines": ["Industry don't like me 'cause I'm thuggin' and I'm dangerous (Brrah)"], "meaning": "Ever since Quando Rondo’s friend Lul Tim killed King Von outside a hookah lounge in Atlanta on November 6th, 2020 NBA YoungBoy and Quando Rondo have been black balled and are showed fake love.", "annotation_id": "24966069", "url": "https://genius.com/24966069", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Gangsta", "line": "Three hundred bands later, I still ain’t drop and y’all united", "vault_lines": ["Three hundred bands later, I still ain't drop and y'all united"], "meaning": "“Three hundred bands later” is Quando referencing the fact that people from Vons camp got $300,000 on his head. He also refers to to Vons camp clickin up with his bum ass oops but he’s still hasn’t dropped and is very much alive.", "annotation_id": "24959888", "url": "https://genius.com/24959888", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Gangsta", "line": "They say Lul Timm the biggest opp Stepped on that boy, don’t do no fightin’", "vault_lines": ["They say Lul Timm the biggest opp", "Stepped on that boy, don't do no fightin'"], "meaning": "Here Quando Rondo may be talking about November 6th 2020, when an altercation started between him and King Von which tragically ended with Von losing his life because Lul Tim gunned him down while Von was beating Quandos Ass.", "annotation_id": "24933758", "url": "https://genius.com/24933758", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
