{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Ghost", "line": "Baby, I was broke Now I don’t know a hot summer, I don’t know a cold winter (I don’t know) My desire adapted with my money", "vault_lines": ["Now I don't know a hot summer, I don't know a cold winter (I don't know)", "My desire adapted with my money"], "meaning": "Youngboy is saying he has now reached new heights of monetary status and accumulation. He no longer has off-seasons and droughts when it comes to revenue and as he has gotten more money, his desires have also only steadily increased.", "annotation_id": "25498102", "url": "https://genius.com/25498102", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
