{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Graffiti", "line": "Fly time, prime time, I’m ballin’ hard sideline", "vault_lines": ["Fly time, prime time, I'm ballin' hard sideline"], "meaning": "NBA Youngboy is comparing himself to a basketball player because of the significance of his rapper name “NBA Youngboy” and also the term “ballin'” which has two meanings of selling drugs and also playing basketball.\n\nThis song along with it’s album was released when he felt like he was in his “prime time” of his carea.", "annotation_id": "36023113", "url": "https://genius.com/36023113", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Graffiti", "line": "I can’t swim but I’m deep off in that ocean I go to sleep in my drip", "vault_lines": ["I can't swim but I'm deep off in that ocean"], "meaning": "NBA Youngboy uses irony & symbolism with the phrase “I can’t swim” and “deep off in that ovean,” describing how he can’t cope with his issues yet he’s deep within them.He continues his lyrics with “drip & sleeping,” solidifying these bars as double entendres by claiming he “goes to sleep with his drip” a word that describes a drop of liquid and also an alternate word for clothing.", "annotation_id": "29197122", "url": "https://genius.com/29197122", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Graffiti", "line": "I’m never exposin’ my pain", "vault_lines": ["I'm never exposin' my pain"], "meaning": "NBA Youngboy commonly express his personal negative experiences such as betrayal, heartbreak, gun violence and many more. These heartbreaking experiences alongside the expectation of being a Man, makes it hard for YB to open up to other people, which is why he uses music as an outlet. It’s no surprise as to why NBA Youngboy blocks the his pain from the world. How can he trust sharing his pain to a world that made him lose faith in people’s generosity.", "annotation_id": "29197025", "url": "https://genius.com/29197025", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
