{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Gravity", "line": "I’m from Baton Rouge, Louisiana, I done came far", "vault_lines": ["I'm from Baton Rouge, Louisiana, I done came far"], "meaning": "Kentrell hails from North Baton Rouge, if you were to look up  3863 Chippewa St, he can be seen standing on the front lawn of the property. North Baton Rouge is considered one of the most dangerous parts of the city, specifically the neighborhoods north of the interstate and around North Gate near LSU. This line is pretty self explanatory, this just serves as some background info on the area.", "annotation_id": "27808597", "url": "https://genius.com/27808597", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Gravity", "line": "So much pain in my body, know you can see it in my eyes You say that you was with me, promised that you was down to ride Now when I look around, you ain’t no where by my side", "vault_lines": ["So much pain in my body, know you can see it in my eyes", "You say that you was with me, promised that you was down to ride", "Now when I look around, you ain't no where by my side"], "meaning": "pain", "annotation_id": "24467214", "url": "https://genius.com/24467214", "state": "pending", "votes": -7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Gravity", "line": "My limit the stars and I wanna grammy Yeah, I just wanna grammy You know? I’m on a whole ’nother level right now", "vault_lines": ["My limit the stars and I wanna grammy", "Yeah, I just wanna grammy", "You know? I'm on a whole 'nother level right now"], "meaning": "YoungBoy feels that he’s limitless and can go as far as he wants in his career.", "annotation_id": "24251901", "url": "https://genius.com/24251901", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Gravity", "line": "Aye, I can’t even lie, I really miss my daddy (My daddy)", "vault_lines": ["Aye, I can't even lie, I really miss my daddy (My daddy)"], "meaning": "YoungBoy’s father was never around when he grew up. His mother, Sherhonda Gaulden, took care of him, but according to YoungBoy himself he was raised mainly by his grandma, Monique.\n\nWhen NBA YoungBoy was eight years old, his father was arrested and sentenced to 55 years in prison for a robbery gone wrong. His mother, Sherhonda, moved out of the neighbourhood, and YoungBoy was then raised by his maternal grandmother. After his grandmother died in 2010, he was taken in by fellow budding rapper NBA 3Three’s family, which he today considers as his real brother.", "annotation_id": "24251876", "url": "https://genius.com/24251876", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
