{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Head Busted", "line": "Bitch I’m cutthroat, to my opp and sure, I don’t fuck wit’ gremlins", "vault_lines": ["Bitch I'm cutthroat, to my opp and sure, I don't fuck wit' gremlins"], "meaning": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again sends a shot at the Florida native rapper Kodak Black, which he refers to as a “gremlin” due to his viral single, “Super Gremlin.”\n\nYoungBoy and Kodak have had several conflicts since 2020 after Kodak accused YoungBoy of snitching.. The conflict between the two rappers has since escalated to 2022 where Kodak called out YoungBoy and his fans in a tweet, reading:\n\nBra I Like YoungBoy Music ITS JUST THIS NIGGA FANS HOMIE! OR WHOEVER TF BEHIND ALL THIS #YBBETTER SHIT THAT SHIT BE IRRITATING…AND CANT NOBODY ELSE SAY THEY DONT FEEL ME, A NIGGA TOO REAL I AINT HATING ON NO FUCKIN BODY I JUST SAY WHAT EVERYBODY ELSE SCARED TO SAY.\n\nKodak’s message was followed up by a quick response from YoungBoy where he briefly replied:\n\nPs. you don’t like my fans I don’t like you ‘pussy’ #TLS\n\nThis was later mellowed down until Kodak announced the release of his fifth studio album, Kutthroat Bill: Vol. 1 which was scheduled to release on October 7, 2022 — the same day as 3800 Degrees — however, it was later pushed back to October 28, 2022. This was later followed by a Tweet which fans speculate is aimed at YoungBoy:\n\n😂 Ya Lil Hoe Ass Thought I Was Dropping @ Midnight 🤷 NOPE 🤪", "annotation_id": "26863101", "url": "https://genius.com/26863101", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
