{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Head Shot", "line": "I know he proud right now ’bout how he saw I beat the feds, huh? Stop now, pow-pow, then sped off I’m with that shit, we tear it down Ol’ bitch-ass nigga, boy, you gon’ fuck around and get your body found Free my daddy, I wanna face my problems like my mama", "vault_lines": ["I know he proud right now 'bout how he saw I beat the feds, huh?", "Stop now, pow-pow, then sped off"], "meaning": "YoungBoy pleads for his father, Jeffery Staden’s release who is currently serving fifty-five years in prison after being an alleged assailant in an armed robbery case in 2009.\n\nWhile pleading for his father’s release, YoungBoy notes that his father is proud of him due to him being found not guilty of his California Federal firearm case in which he was accused of running from the police after being found with several firearms. In July 2022, YoungBoy was found not guilty of all charges, beating a federal case. He seemingly uses this as a flex due to the United States' Federal government having a conviction rate of 99.8%, making YoungBoy a part of the 0.2% of people who are found not guilty.\n\nDespite YoungBoy beating his California Federal gun charge, he has a pending charge in his home city of Baton Rouge which he’s charged with in a Federal firearm indictment after being arrested on drug and firearm charges among sixteen others while shooting the music video for his November 2020, “Chopper City.” Due to this current case, YB is still on house arrest despite beating the other.\n\nIn spite of his pending charges, YoungBoy notes that he shares similar personality traits to his mother, Sherondah Gaulden — who appeared as a feature on his April 2020 “Bout My Business” — sharing that he, like his mother, is confrontational and refuses to go behind peoples backs.", "annotation_id": "28383308", "url": "https://genius.com/28383308", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
