{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Heart & Soul", "line": "I ain’t beefin’ wit’ all these niggas, don’t even mention me They gon’ kill me if they can No need for dissin’, come get rid of me", "vault_lines": ["They gon' kill me if they can", "No need for dissin', come get rid of me"], "meaning": "YoungBoy has said on ClubHouse that he doesn’t want beef with anyone, unless they want him dead.", "annotation_id": "24705033", "url": "https://genius.com/24705033", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Heart & Soul", "line": "Who am I? Like, aha, who was I?", "vault_lines": ["Who am I? Like, aha, who was I?"], "meaning": "NBA YoungBoy is questioning and reflecting on his past that was filled and driven by gang affiliation. He then laughs at his old self while referring to himself in a past tense, which shows that NBA YoungBoy has changed.", "annotation_id": "24631195", "url": "https://genius.com/24631195", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Heart & Soul", "line": "I been watchin’ the way I influence now I ain’t post not a picture, I moved on", "vault_lines": ["I been watchin' the way I influence now", "I ain't post not a picture, I moved on"], "meaning": "NBA YoungBoy is attentive to the way he influences his fans and therefore he opted out of addressing any of his old conflicts.\n\nIn terms of posting pictures, NBA YoungBoy has expressed that he does not like social media. He stated that roughly 80% of what is seen on social media does not correspond to reality and therefore it’s meaningless.", "annotation_id": "24558590", "url": "https://genius.com/24558590", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Heart & Soul", "line": "I ain’t even been worried ’bout the jury now I been wanna do right since I touched down", "vault_lines": ["I ain't even been worried 'bout the jury now", "I been wanna do right since I touched down"], "meaning": "This line further illustrates NBA YoungBoy’s thought process. He moves completely to the beat of his own drum.\n\nRecognizing that the jury’s decision is outside of the sphere of his control, he has instead chosen to focus on bettering himself while he is outside with his children.", "annotation_id": "24558577", "url": "https://genius.com/24558577", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Heart & Soul", "line": "I ain’t even been worried ’bout no jewelry now So my girl don’t want her a bust down", "vault_lines": ["I ain't even been worried 'bout no jewelry now", "So my girl don't want her a bust down"], "meaning": "Further illustrating NBA YoungBoy’s growth, he expresses that he is not interested in jewelry. This demonstrates that NBA YoungBoy is not as materialistic as he once was.\n\nIn his recent interview with DJ Akademiks, he states that he had a phase where he was into cars and jewelry, but these things do not interest him anymore. He has also stated that he does not like to carry cash anymore, as this is childish behaviour.", "annotation_id": "24558566", "url": "https://genius.com/24558566", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Heart & Soul", "line": "My soul, I still ain’t think I found When I tell bro on the phone", "vault_lines": ["My soul, I still ain't think I found", "When I tell bro on the phone"], "meaning": "NBA YoungBoy is just 22 years old. Therefore, he is still trying to find himself.\n\nNBA YoungBoy is unapologetic about being himself. He has stated that he enjoys painting his face with makeup, as this makes him feel more comfortable. He expressed that he does not worry about the judgments of others in these matters.", "annotation_id": "24558545", "url": "https://genius.com/24558545", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Heart & Soul", "line": "They say that he ain’t gon’ be here long I see myself on top the mountain I’m smokin’ strong, I’m keepin’ strong", "vault_lines": ["They say that he ain't gon' be here long", "I see myself on top the mountain", "I'm smokin' strong, I'm keepin' strong"], "meaning": "NBA YoungBoy has been involved in rap feuds that have led to deaths. Furthermore, he has been in ongoing trouble with the law.\n\nThese factors have led many to believe that NBA YoungBoy might die at a young age. Per NBA YoungBoy’s interviews, he does not seem to be very concerned with the concept of death. He has expressed that one cannot avoid what is meant for them. Additionally, NBA YoungBoy expressed that he feels he is old in a recent interview with DJ Akademiks.", "annotation_id": "24558491", "url": "https://genius.com/24558491", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Heart & Soul", "line": "I just fail to accept that you not good for anyone” Oh, oh-oh, oh, oh-oh, oh, oh-oh I can feel it in my soul", "vault_lines": ["I just fail to accept that you not good for anyone\"", "Oh, oh-oh, oh, oh-oh, oh, oh-oh", "I can feel it in my soul"], "meaning": "The chorus culminates here, where NBA YoungBoy expresses that he feels that he’s not good for anyone.\n\nIn an interview with DJ Akademiks, NBA YoungBoy has stated that some of his friends have become disabled, and others have died around the conflicts that he has had.\n\nAdditionally, if NBA YoungBoy continues to get into trouble with the law, his family, children and associates will face financial hardships.\n\nThese pressures have likely led the rapper to express that he feels that he is not good for anyone.", "annotation_id": "24558462", "url": "https://genius.com/24558462", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Heart & Soul", "line": "I’m like, ”DeSean, thuggin’, you just hustlin’ backwards Nigga, you done won", "vault_lines": ["I'm like, \"DeSean, thuggin', you just hustlin' backwards", "Nigga, you done won"], "meaning": "Now, NBA YoungBoy addresses himself by his middle name, DeSean. He expresses regret with his past actions. All of the acts that he took part in the past to be a thug ultimately did not serve him.\n\nAs a rapper, NBA YoungBoy has been tremendously successful and he has an avenue through which he can change the lives of his family and associates. Therefore, NBA YoungBoy has already won at life and has no need to prove anything to anyone.", "annotation_id": "24558437", "url": "https://genius.com/24558437", "state": "pending", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Heart & Soul", "line": "Kentrell, you got to man up, you done had all these kids I’m like, “Kentrell, you got to stand up, it’s your time, I see it”", "vault_lines": ["Kentrell, you got to man up, you done had all these kids", "I'm like, \"Kentrell, you got to stand up, it's your time, I see it\""], "meaning": "In the form of soliloquy, NBA YoungBoy addresses himself by his first name Kentrell. He is admonishing himself, urging himself to be a man and face his responsibilities with respect to raising his children.", "annotation_id": "24558378", "url": "https://genius.com/24558378", "state": "pending", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Heart & Soul", "line": "Went to jail, came home, time passed, went back again All the pain I felt inside myself, thought it would never end I just thought I would blame myself, can’t even blame my friends I was criticizin’ myself like, you ain’t never gon’ win", "vault_lines": ["Went to jail, came home", "I just thought I would blame myself, can't even blame my friends", "I was criticizin' myself like, you ain't never gon' win"], "meaning": "NBA YoungBoy has had recurring trouble with the law, going back to 2016.\n\nThese lyrics from “Still Waiting” provide further insight into the pain that NBA YoungBoy felt during his time in jail:\n\n“How I’m feeling, it ain’t no one I can tell it to\nWho really love me? I can say a few\nMama, I’m so sorry, I can’t save myself\nGrandpa, just your opinion matter, it ain’t no one else\nMomo, I miss your love, I been tryna find myself\nDon’t wanna be in jail, just tell ‘em I accept the chair”\n\nIt is evident that NBA YoungBoy feels as though he is responsible for all that happened to him. He does not want to put the blame on anyone else, including his friends. NBA YoungBoy hit rock bottom, even wishing that he would be sentenced to death.", "annotation_id": "24558339", "url": "https://genius.com/24558339", "state": "pending", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
