{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hell & Back", "line": "Bob and weave like a boxer", "vault_lines": ["Bob and weave like a boxer"], "meaning": "Boxers use a technique called the ‘bob and weave’ where they use a sideways dipping motion in order to dodge oncoming blows directed towards them\n\n\n\nBy using this analogy, he’s saying he’s gonna dodge all the blows people are sending his way as he won’t let them stop him. This along with the theme of this 2nd verse of pressing forward no matter what, Youngboy’s saying that he won’t stop, regardless of what/who tries to stop him.", "annotation_id": "11651252", "url": "https://genius.com/11651252", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
