{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hey Pops", "line": "Everybody clap for Raf Simons, yeah (For Raf Simons)", "vault_lines": ["Everybody clap for Raf Simons, yeah (For Raf Simons)"], "meaning": "Raf Simons is a Belgian fashion designer and founder of clothing brand Raf Simons, which he has decided to shut down after 27 years.", "annotation_id": "27516569", "url": "https://genius.com/27516569", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hey Pops", "line": "Hey pop, are you proud of me? Well, I don’t care ’Cause now, I got a mansion and I got them racks, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Hey pop, are you proud of me? Well, I don't care"], "meaning": "When YoungBoy was 8 years old his father was arrested and sentenced to 55 years in prison.\n\nSince he was a young boy (see what I did there) he had the goal of making his father proud. But now that he is successful he no longer feels the need for his fathers approval of him. This can be interpreted as how personal growth by time deletes certain old needs or habits.\n\nHe certainly has had some issues growing up without his parents, according to YoungBoy his grandmother raised him and not his mom nor dad. His need for them to be proud could come from the lack of their presence in his childhood.", "annotation_id": "27516459", "url": "https://genius.com/27516459", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
