{"type": "song", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "He’s a Thug (Plenty Bodies)", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Youngboy-never-broke-again-hes-a-thug-plenty-bodies-lyrics", "genius_title": "He’s a Thug (Plenty Bodies)", "genius_id": 4406732, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hi Haters", "line": "Ain’t been respondin’ to these niggas, I’m way more rich, I know they see (They see)", "vault_lines": ["Ain't been respondin' to these niggas, I'm way more rich, I know they see (They see)"], "meaning": "People was dissing Kentrell during his house arrest in “I HATE YOUNG BOY” there was a line saying that they feel that they can diss home because he is in house arrest.", "annotation_id": "29486430", "url": "https://genius.com/29486430", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hi Haters", "line": "Wanna say, “Stop violence,” but, it don’t add up to my name Known to bring pain, I bust his brain Like, “Boy, you disrespect gang” (You know)", "vault_lines": ["Wanna say, \"Stop violence,\" but, it don't add up to my name", "Known to bring pain, I bust his brain", "Like, \"Boy, you disrespect gang\" (You know)"], "meaning": "After YoungBoy reactivated his Instagram for the first time since the release of his fourth studio album, The Last Slimeto, on November 22, 2022, YoungBoy had taken to Instagram to share a video of him urging for “the violence” to stop ahead of his team donating turkeys in Baton Rouge:\n\nAye! Stop the violence. Look at me! I could promise you it’s a bigger side of life. Stop the violence. You could be a rich nixxa, ya heard me? I could promise you. I ain’t gon’ tell you what’s in my bank account bixxh but aye – stop the violence!\n\nYoungBoy follows up by stating that despite wanting to stop “the violence” — referring to the deaths of several of his companions — stopping the violence is inevitable as he has represented himself in such a way in his past, YB even being affiliated with the Blood Gang, rapping about his affiliation in several songs such as “I Hate YoungBoy,” and “I-10 Baby.”\n\nYoungBoy further states that if you disrespect his “gang,” there will be major consequences, further explained in “Lost Soul Survivor” as he rapped:\n\nKnow that my brother, he gotta get mutual respect and if you disrespect, that’s your ass", "annotation_id": "27201374", "url": "https://genius.com/27201374", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hi Haters", "line": "Gotta keep that stick inside my pants, like Baboon (Know I gotta keep that stick)", "vault_lines": ["Gotta keep that stick inside my pants, like Baboon (Know I gotta keep that stick)"], "meaning": "Listening to this line may confuse a lesser-man into wondering, “Did he just call him self a monkey?” However, fear not dear reader, allow me to explain the outstanding message that this lyric is presenting.\n\nYou see, Mr. Gualden isn’t one to fool around when it comes to his unique and unmatchable level of lyricism and this line is no exception.\n\nThis line is a reference to the classic Disney movie, “The Lion King”, but more specifically a character in the film known as Rafiki.\n\n\n\nRafiki\n\n\nRafiki is a wise Baboon who statures highly among the animal kingdom within the movie and notably wields a large stick throughout the film.\n\nThe clever Kentrell DeSean Gualden is comparing Rafiki’s signature stick to a firearm which is popularly referred to as a “stick”.\n\nThe genius Mr. Gualden has tapped into this magnificent lyricism in the past in his song title, “Sticks With Me” along with the legendary words within the piece of music.\n\nCover art for Sticks With Me by Youngboy Never Broke Again\n\n\nNow dear reader, apologies for this extension but I must express this outrageous news I have come upon.\n\nYou see, as of writing this annotation, I realized something: While bringing this lyric into existence to bless our ears, Kentrell DeSean Gualden must have been working alongside God himself and here’s why.\n\nAs did you, I believed this lyric had just the meaning explained before, however, it gets deeper.\n\nRemember when I called Rafiki wise? It seemed to have swept past my mind that Mr. Gualden was also referring to himself as Rafiki, in terms of his wise mind for carrying his firearm or “stick” for protection.\n\nMr. Gualden’s brain vs. the average human brain\n\n\nNow as I was finishing up deciphering this lyric, I realized something much more perplexing. THE STICK IS FOR THE HATERS. What is the song name? Excellence from the Kentrell DeSean Gualden at it’s finest.\n\nThank you for your time.", "annotation_id": "27195573", "url": "https://genius.com/27195573", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hi Haters", "line": "Try and pray five times a day, name another Christian do the same (Amen) And I gotta thank the Lord for my kids (My kids) Harper got smart on that big", "vault_lines": ["Try and pray five times a day, name another Christian do the same (Amen)", "And I gotta thank the Lord for my kids (My kids)", "Harper got smart on that big"], "meaning": "While recollecting the already astoundingly long list of perplexingly-honorable traits from Grammy Award-winning artist, Kentrell DeSean Gualden, we are reminded of one of the most important. Mr. Gualden is a man of Christ. Thanking the almighty life-giver himself for blessing him with his children, a truly beautiful thing to hear about.\n\nListeners are left in a jaw-dropping state of awe when listening to this line. To be blessed with the stupefying knowledge that Mr. Gualden, prays to the man above five times a day. Not even your overly-religious grandmother could dream of accomplishing such an astonishing feat.\n\nListeners are still waiting for a daring soul to even try and name a follower of Christianity that can compete with this amazing dedication as the bold Kentrell  DeSean Gualden has challenged us to do so.", "annotation_id": "27195507", "url": "https://genius.com/27195507", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hi Haters", "line": "To all the haters, I say, “Hey” I made it through another day I’m blessed, so how can I complain? It ain’t one thing that they can say", "vault_lines": ["To all the haters, I say, \"Hey\"", "I made it through another day", "I'm blessed, so how can I complain?", "It ain't one thing that they can say"], "meaning": "Perhaps in the most eloquent way ever spoken into existence, Kentrell DeSean Gualden begins one of the most extravagant choruses of mankind by expressing he isn’t affected by his haters.\n\nIf you didn’t know, Mr. Gualden, more commonly referred to as Youngboy Never Broke Again or simply, Youngboy, has one of the most relentlessly supporting fanbases in the history of Hip-Hop.\n\nPhoto of a Youngboy supporter with the tattoo, “YB BETTER” embroided accross his chest. YB Better is a phrase simply meaning, Youngboy Better.\n\n\nHowever, some lesser-woke people don’t like the fact that such a specimen that is Youngboy is as successful as he is and choose to hate on him with no reasoning.\nAs he states in the chorus though, there isn’t one thing they can say that can take him off the towering pedestal he’s created for himself at just 23-years old.", "annotation_id": "27193781", "url": "https://genius.com/27193781", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hi Haters", "line": "Nails got some paint up on ‘em, but play, know I’ll kill yo’ big homie", "vault_lines": ["Nails got some paint up on 'em, but play, know I'll kill yo' big homie"], "meaning": "Whilst being amazed from viewing the exquisite music video starring the great multi-platinum artist, Kentrell DeSean Gualden, your eyes may be distracted from his handsome face onto his nails which appear to have been painted a glossy-black color.\n\n\n\nHowever, Mr. Gualden reassures listeners that regardless of the way he presents himself, he is not hesitant to  swap onto his notorious murderous timing if provoked.", "annotation_id": "27193688", "url": "https://genius.com/27193688", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hi Haters", "line": "Tell Charleston White, “I’m a gangster who been misled wrong” I just been leadin’ wrong, but if you ever need me, I’ll send a bag (I’ll send a bag)", "vault_lines": ["Tell Charleston White, \"I'm a gangster who been misled wrong\"", "I just been leadin' wrong, but if you ever need me, I'll send a bag (I'll send a bag)"], "meaning": "He basically saying Charleston white was right and he just admitting he was mislead wrong in life , and he’ll send him money Charleston White’s message getting through to the most influential young rapper is huge. These other lames think it’s cool to diss him in songs while YB learned that he’s been misled by the culture.", "annotation_id": "27191874", "url": "https://genius.com/27191874", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
