{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hold Your Own", "line": "Just paid ten million for my taxes, no time for flashin’", "vault_lines": ["Just paid ten million for my taxes, no time for flashin'"], "meaning": "might be a reach or I might be way off, but I remember yb saying he gotta pay 10M for taxes", "annotation_id": "41266681", "url": "https://genius.com/41266681", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hold Your Own", "line": "Since grandma died, I ain’t go to church, she a gospel woman, the past hurt", "vault_lines": ["Since grandma died, I ain't go to church, she a gospel woman, the past hurt"], "meaning": "Double Entendre he could’ve also said pastor here", "annotation_id": "39861247", "url": "https://genius.com/39861247", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hold Your Own", "line": "In the 8-Atlantic-section, hand in a pot, I’m with VL Been a chef before a rapper, I was tryna show ’em that my recipes still good still", "vault_lines": ["In the 8-Atlantic-section, hand in a pot, I'm with VL", "Been a chef before a rapper, I was tryna show 'em that my recipes still good still"], "meaning": "Section 8, otherwise known as the “eight Atlantic section,” is a common name for the Housing Choice Voucher Program which is funded by the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development, in Atlanta, Georgia.\n\nTo have your “hand in pot” commonly refers to producing drugs, most commonly cocaine — playing onto the next lyric where YoungBoy names himself as a “chef.”\n\nYoungBoy states that he was a drug manufacturer prior to his rise to fame, however, he explains that he occasionally produces drugs to make sure that the specific recipe he uses is nonetheless adequate, despite him not doing it as much as he used to.\n\nWhile engaging in all these activities, YoungBoy was with VL Deck, an American rapper who is born and raised in Atlanta, Georgia. VL grew up in the Edgewood section of Atlanta, otherwise known as Zone 6. The Edgewood section possesses the Section 8 housing program.\n\nVL and YoungBoy have previously released a collaborative mixtape in October 2018, Kane & O-Dog, however, in YoungBoy’s October 2019, “Rich As Hell,” he rapped a similar lyric where he described an almost identical setting:\n\nI can cook that dope just like a worker, you can ask VL\nLook and I can eyeball, I don’t talk loud, I don’t need a scale\nPlenty money, but I’m still thuggin', this the rich as hell", "annotation_id": "26994625", "url": "https://genius.com/26994625", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hold Your Own", "line": "Feelin’ insecure, I could work you good, but feel like a lil’ boy That’s just me, I’m thinkin’ out loud, but your bitch’ll tell you I go hard", "vault_lines": ["Feelin' insecure, I could work you good, but feel like a lil' boy", "That's just me, I'm thinkin' out loud, but your bitch'll tell you I go hard"], "meaning": "What Nba Youngboy is saying is that even though He can get self conscious at times, he still manages to get you to like him. Although he realizes his child-like behaviors, and has the courage to address them, At the end of the day the females will still Adore him", "annotation_id": "26650441", "url": "https://genius.com/26650441", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hold Your Own", "line": "Tryna bring some love around to stop my hustle, I’ll murder Cupid", "vault_lines": ["Tryna bring some love around to stop my hustle, I'll murder Cupid"], "meaning": "Cupid is the son of Venus and the god of Love, youngboy inferring that he will murder love / doesn’t want it around his hustle", "annotation_id": "26449259", "url": "https://genius.com/26449259", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hold Your Own", "line": "How you ‘posed to hustle? You can’t focus, you out here takin’ Roxies", "vault_lines": ["How you 'posed to hustle? You can't focus, you out here takin' Roxies"], "meaning": "slang for Oxycodone, a drug that helps with pain tolerance. These pills are extremely addictive and once you start taking them it is increasingly difficult to stop.", "annotation_id": "26436597", "url": "https://genius.com/26436597", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Hold Your Own", "line": "Youngin’, don’t you want your life? Don’t be stupid, this ain’t kamikaze", "vault_lines": ["Youngin', don't you want your life? Don't be stupid, this ain't kamikaze"], "meaning": "Youngboy is giving advice and a warning to his young audience. Kamikaze is a reference to a suicide mission Japanese pilots went on in WW11. These pilots would deliberately crash their planes into enemies, effectively committing suicide. Youngboy is saying that living this lifestyle can be fatal to others as well as yourself.", "annotation_id": "26436580", "url": "https://genius.com/26436580", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
