{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Home Ain’t Home", "line": "Feelin’ like my home ain’t no home", "vault_lines": ["Feelin' like my home ain't no home"], "meaning": "“Feeling at home” is a popular phrase, meaning to have a relaxed sensation, often feeling comfortable. However, in this line, YoungBoy expresses the pain and emptiness of his un-homely feeling, possibly showing that no one is alongside him anymore.\n\nYoungBoy has rapped corresponding lyrics such as in May 2022’s “Proud Of Myself” where he states:\n\nPaid them millions, I still don’t feel like I’m home\nAnd it’s the small lil' things been goin' wrong\nFeel like my mama gone away for like way too long", "annotation_id": "26474451", "url": "https://genius.com/26474451", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
