{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Admit", "line": "Soon as he say it’s go-time, I get her", "vault_lines": ["Soon as he say it's go-time, I get her"], "meaning": "“As soon as he say go time ima get her” – This is a possible reference to her 2010 feature on “Up all Night” with long time rap comrade Drake. She states “If drizzy say get her ima’ get her”. To get someone in the rap sense means to come for their career and show how much better you are in the style of rap. Nicki asserts her dominance over her female peers in this line.", "annotation_id": "27371952", "url": "https://genius.com/27371952", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Admit", "line": "And know I got plenty bodies", "vault_lines": ["And know I got plеnty bodies"], "meaning": "he is saying that he killed a lot of human or rival gangs", "annotation_id": "27050796", "url": "https://genius.com/27050796", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Admit", "line": "You a amateur, ho, I’m in the league Point guard, tongue out, oh, look at the speed", "vault_lines": ["You a amateur, ho, I'm in the league", "Point guard, tongue out, oh, look at the speed"], "meaning": "Here, Nicki Minaj uses an extended metaphor to reiterate her power in the music industry after being in several disputes with other female rappers such as Cardi B, Latto, and Megan Thee Stallion.\n\nAn “amateur” mainly refers to one who isn’t experienced in something, heavily contrasting to Nicki’s storng influence over the hip-hop industry, placing her “in the league.” This can also be seen as a dig toward other female artists as Nicki uses the term to state that other artists are not on her level.\n\nUsing a double entendre, Nicki extends her basketball metaphor as a point guard is a basketball position. Basketball players often stick their “tongue out” to show their skill and prowess, heavily linking to Nicki’s undeniable rapping skill. Furthermore, the role of a “point guard” is to direct the team’s plays — relating to Nicki having the largest influence over the female rap community.\n\n\n\nPictured: Steph Curry with his tongue out after scoring a three point shot.", "annotation_id": "26977480", "url": "https://genius.com/26977480", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Admit", "line": "Soon as I give it to him, he finna get my name on his next tat’", "vault_lines": ["Soon as I give it to him, he finna get my name on his next tat'"], "meaning": "Nicki took to Instagram in December 2020 to showcase her husband, Kenneth Petty’s new tattoo.\n\n\n\nThe ink reads Nicki’s birth name, “Onika.”\n\nNicki’s ex Safaree also got a tattoo of Nicki Minaj but later got it covered.", "annotation_id": "26959476", "url": "https://genius.com/26959476", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Admit", "line": "Jumpshot wetter, NBA better (Gangsta Grillz)", "vault_lines": ["Jumpshot wetter, NBA better (Gangsta Grillz)"], "meaning": "The term “wet” is slang or a figure of speech in basketball. When a player shoots a basketball into the hoop and it swishes, the player shooting will say wet.\n\n“NBA Better” is a phrase used for support or ironically by trolls to make fun of the rapper and his dedicated fanbase on social media.", "annotation_id": "26959422", "url": "https://genius.com/26959422", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Admit", "line": "Go against me, where your suicide letter?", "vault_lines": ["Go against me, where your suicide letter?"], "meaning": "Nicki used a similar line on the song Make Love with Gucci Mane aimed at Remy Ma in 2017.\n\nGo against Nicki, it’s gon' cost ya\n‘Cause now it’s fuck ya, intercourse ya\n\nUpon this songs' release, Remy Ma has yet to chart on the Billboard Hot 100 after her feud with Nicki Minaj.", "annotation_id": "26959189", "url": "https://genius.com/26959189", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Admit", "line": "I don’t lick the rims on shots, I all net her", "vault_lines": ["I don't lick the rims on shots, I all net her"], "meaning": "Nicki uses a basketball metaphor to affirm her talent in rap, as in the sport, a swish is perfect shot that goes through the basket without touching the rim, hence “all net”.\n\nThis is also a double entendre referring to a rimmed alcoholic shot, suggesting she can handle her liquor straight.\n\n\n\nThrowing or taking shots as also an expression meaning to diss i.e. her disses to people aren’t sweet -like a sugar rim- and never miss.", "annotation_id": "26958951", "url": "https://genius.com/26958951", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Admit", "line": "Ayy, yo, and we still on that get-back Poppin’ chains, don’t give shit back", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, yo, and we still on that get-back", "Poppin' chains, don't give shit back"], "meaning": "4pf recently took Offsets chain. As Akbar V and others was claiming on twitter. Nicki also said love to Lil Baby on twitter for #4pf taking the chain. Offset unfortunately ain’t getting shit back.", "annotation_id": "26955011", "url": "https://genius.com/26955011", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
