{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Like It", "line": "Gotta stay protected, so I stay suited like Steve Harvey", "vault_lines": ["Gotta stay protected, so I stay suited like Steve Harvey"], "meaning": "Steve Harvey is an American television host, actor, and comedian. The star hosts a series of shows including Family Feud, Celebrity Family Feud and his most popular show, Steve Harvey Morning Show.\n\nSteve is also known for the various distinctive suits he wears. Here, YoungBoy associates his gang ties with Steve’s outfit as “staying suited,” alludes to carrying several firearms in order to avoid getting murdered by his rivals, thus, clarifying him “staying protected.”\n\n\n\nPictured: Steve Harvey in a suit.", "annotation_id": "26769831", "url": "https://genius.com/26769831", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Like It", "line": "And I came from EBT, no award won from BET", "vault_lines": ["And I came from EBT, no award won from BET"], "meaning": "EBT — Electronic Benefits Transfer — is a system that allows low-income US citizens to be granted a cash card which will enable them to buy groceries and other items with the cash benefits.\n\nYoungBoy notes that he and his family received cash benefits while growing up due to their inadequate income. From North Baton Rouge — a poverty-ridden city — YoungBoy has often rapped about his challenging adolescence about how he’s made it out of the trenches — a slang term to refer to a low-income area with high levels of crime. YoungBoy most notably rapped about this in his 2018 track, “I Am Who They Say I Am” in which he rapped:\n\nThug nigga from the trenches never had a heart\nDrug dealer, contract killer, loyal from the start (Start)\n\nBlack Entertainment Television — popularly known as BET — is an American cable channel which targets African-Americans. BET holds yearly awards for African-Americans entertainers and performers. YoungBoy notes that despite his success and influence on rap, he has still not won a BET award.\n\nThroughout 2022, YoungBoy made several claims that he was being blackballed by his label Atlantic Records. In several songs such as “Black Ball” and “Proud Of Myself,” YoungBoy noted that he has no respect for the industry due to their lack of respect for him.\n\nFurthermore, while appearing as a guest on [Lil Nas X]’s June 2022, “Late To Da Party (FUCK BET),” the song gained major popularity due to Lil Nas dissing the BET awards in the song:\n\nYeah, fuck BET (Yeah), fuck BET (Yeah), fuck BET (Yeah, yeah)\nYeah, fuck BET (They know that), yeah (They know that)\nYeah, ayy, yeah", "annotation_id": "26666834", "url": "https://genius.com/26666834", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Like It", "line": "You say I ain’t your nigga But I feel I’m somethin’ deeper I’m a softly spoken creature And I know you wanna see me fly I’d die for you, you know Hope you don’t switch up neither", "vault_lines": ["And I know you wanna see me fly", "I'd die for you, you know", "Hope you don't switch up neither"], "meaning": "He is denying rejection and strongly feels a bond with another person when the other part doesn’t feel the same. A way of using ignorance to not feel hurt.", "annotation_id": "26666795", "url": "https://genius.com/26666795", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
