{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Talk", "line": "I don’t talk to my girl friends, and my girl friends don’t talk to me", "vault_lines": ["I don't talk to my girl friends, and my girl friends don't talk to me"], "meaning": "YoungBoy says that he doesnt talk to his girlfriend’s friends, and his girlfriends friends dont talk to him, showing that he is loyal to Jazlyn Mychelle, his current girlfriend.", "annotation_id": "26357832", "url": "https://genius.com/26357832", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Talk", "line": "Later OD’d from off a doja, it was as strong as nightcap", "vault_lines": ["Later OD'd from off a doja, it was as strong as nightcap"], "meaning": "Throughout the hip-hop/rap industry, the term “Doja” became popular. In literal sense, the term refers to weed or marijuana. It can be clearly established that NBA YoungBoy was overdosing on the drug.\n\nUltimately, the rapper has shown his fondness with weed, as well as on previous singles. NBA YoungBoy has stated on a 2019 track titled “Time I’m On” from his mixtape AI YoungBoy 2:\n\nSmoking hella weed, loaded, I just bought another pack", "annotation_id": "26323034", "url": "https://genius.com/26323034", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Talk", "line": "Tell Mike Caren I thank him for that phone call, I’m on now", "vault_lines": ["Tell Mike Caren I thank him for that phone call, I'm on now"], "meaning": "Mike Caren is an American record producer, also the founder and CEO of apg, a music publishing company.\n\nBefore the “blackballing” situation where NBA YoungBoy was blackballed by his old record label Atlantic Records ─ the rapper was previously signed to a label named apg founded by Mike. There are numerous of artists that are signed to the record label including Charlie Puth, 24kGoldn, Don Toliver and many others.\n\nNBA YoungBoy later shows his thankfulness on a phone call to the label after the ungrateful situation with Atlantic Records.", "annotation_id": "26317208", "url": "https://genius.com/26317208", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Talk", "line": "Rap game with a bad name, a platinum album, and a Nawf degree", "vault_lines": ["Rap game with a bad name, a platinum album, and a Nawf degree"], "meaning": "Throughout YoungBoy’s lengthy career which had begun in 2015, YoungBoy has been portrayed in many different ways as he’s been in and out of jail and hit with several charges throughout the majority of his career. YoungBoy is also the father of seven children at the young age of 22, portraying him as careless, and incautious.\n\nOn January 28, 2020, YoungBoy took to Twitter to express his sorrow from being painted by the media, and fans in a bad light:\n\nFucked up how People always make me seem like a bad person I’m just me\n\nIn contrast to YB’s sorrow of being portrayed in a bad light, YoungBoy uses it as a flex as despite being portrayed in such an atrocious way, he is still successful as his debut studio album Until Death Call My Name and his sophomore studio album Top are both certified platinum by the RIAA.\n\nAgain, contrasting YB’s sorrow of being portrayed in a bad light, YoungBoy mentions that he has a “North degree” which means he made it out or graduated from the Northside of Baton Rouge which is known to be poverty-filled and home to many gangs. The lyric heavily relates to the term “made it out the hood.”", "annotation_id": "26308975", "url": "https://genius.com/26308975", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Talk", "line": "Daddy lost his soul inside a trial, that’s fifty-five, one long ride", "vault_lines": ["Daddy lost his soul inside a trial, that's fifty-five, one long ride"], "meaning": "In December 2009, YoungBoy’s father Jeffery Staden, a 29-year-old male, turned himself in after a warrant for his arrest had been issued regarding an armed robbery.\n\nStaden was accused of being an alleged assailant in an armed robbery case alongside his brother, Dallas Staden, who had previously turned himself in on December 4, 2009. Jeffery was accused of shooting the store clerk in the leg, adding an additional first-degree murder charge to his case.\n\nAccording to court documents, Dallas had cooperated with the police and had snitched on his brother Jeffery, resulting in Jeffery being found guilty of all charges and beings sentenced to 55 years in prison.\n\nYoungBoy previously made similar comments on his April 2016 “Cross Me,” where he asserted:\n\nOn my heart, that’s on my soul, I won’t tell no lies\nUncle told, now, my daddy doing 55\n\n\n\nPictured: Jeffery Staden’s December 2009 mugshot", "annotation_id": "26308671", "url": "https://genius.com/26308671", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Talk", "line": "Blackballed me from up out the game, bitch, stripped me out the fame", "vault_lines": ["Blackballеd me from up out the game, bitch, strippеd me out the fame"], "meaning": "Throughout 2022, YoungBoy has continuously expressed how he feels blackballed from the music industry, throwing the blame directly at his record label, Atlantic Records.\n\nWhile the accusations of Atlantic Records trying to blackball YoungBoy had aroused in 2020 after YB tried to buy back his music masters, in 2022, YoungBoy would take several shots at his label while even publically advising artists not to sign with the label.\n\nIn January 2022, after YoungBoy’s seventeenth mixtape Colors was taken off of the Apple Music charts leading to YoungBoy peaking at #2 on the Billboard 200 instead of #1. YoungBoy publically posted his response to this, accusing Atlantic Records of trying to blackball him:\n\nI was going #1 two weeks straight with a mixtape so they took it down off the charts I don’t give a f**k you still can’t stop me don’t sign to Atlantic if you a artist they not gone support you especially if you live a certain way\n\nAdditionaly, in “Proud Of Myself,” YoungBoy continued to mention his hatred for the industry:\n\nGot a hit for every song that they play, what you say?\nI won’t get paid, ain’t no love for the game (Mmm)", "annotation_id": "26308556", "url": "https://genius.com/26308556", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Talk", "status": "done", "targets": 13, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Youngboy-never-broke-again-i-dont-talk-lyrics", "genius_title": "I Don’t Talk", "genius_id": 8213383, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "Pendants I put ’round my neck, make a Cartier Cartier watch, it’s not even a starter pack", "vault_lines": ["Pendants I put 'round my neck, make a Cartier"], "meaning": "Cartier jewelry is a status symbol in hip-hop, but YoungBoy flexes that his level of wealth goes far beyond the “starter pack” of luxury watches and chains. For him, Cartier is just the beginning, not the pinnacle, of what he can afford.", "annotation_id": "36802319", "url": "https://genius.com/36802319", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "I used to ride up to slimes in the Pontiac I got this shit in position, I’m quarterback", "vault_lines": ["I used to ride up to slimes in the Pontiac", "I got this shit in position, I'm quarterback"], "meaning": "He references his old days driving a Pontiac, a modest car compared to his luxury vehicles today. The “quarterback” metaphor shows his leadership role — he’s the one in control, calling the plays and directing his team, both in life and in the music industry.", "annotation_id": "36802316", "url": "https://genius.com/36802316", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "They was talkin’ ’bout me ’cause my clothes was dingy Hand-me-downs, I used to wear from my cousin", "vault_lines": ["They was talkin' 'bout me 'cause my clothes was dingy", "Hand-me-downs, I used to wear from my cousin"], "meaning": "YoungBoy recalls being ridiculed for wearing old, worn-out clothes passed down from family members. This detail highlights the poverty he grew up in and the struggles he faced before fame. It’s a moment of vulnerability that contrasts with his current wealth and success.", "annotation_id": "36802288", "url": "https://genius.com/36802288", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "I had to grind and it take me a minute", "vault_lines": ["I had to grind and it take me a minute"], "meaning": "Here he reflects on his journey. Success didn’t come overnight — it took time, persistence, and hard work. The “grind” refers not only to his career in rap but also to surviving his difficult upbringing.", "annotation_id": "36802283", "url": "https://genius.com/36802283", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "I got some twizzies, they crazy, they kill you, they get you like", "vault_lines": ["I got some twizzies, they crazy, they kill you, they get you like, \"Huh-huh-huh\""], "meaning": "“Twizz” or “Twizzies” is a popular term used by Yeat and underground rappers. A twizz is someone who is someone who is very close to you ( friend , homie, brother ).", "annotation_id": "27217954", "url": "https://genius.com/27217954", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "I mix the Oxy’ with X, bitch, I’m booted like", "vault_lines": ["I mix the Oxy' with X, bitch, I'm booted like, \"Uh\" (Uh, uh)"], "meaning": "Yeat is telling us here that he mixes drugs and becomes booted. The popular drugs are Oxycodone and Xanax. They are often mixed for pill consumption. Booted is a term used for being under the influence of pills", "annotation_id": "27217943", "url": "https://genius.com/27217943", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "DOP", "vault_lines": ["I upgraded my linen, huh, DOP, I don't do no simpin', uh"], "meaning": "*BOP (Big Ol’ Player)", "annotation_id": "27038227", "url": "https://genius.com/27038227", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "I’m at the top of this shit like I’m Big Ole pimpin’", "vault_lines": ["I'm at the top of this shit like I'm Big Ole pimpin' (Yeah, pimpin')"], "meaning": "The “Big ole” part can also be interpreted as “Big O”.\n\nBig O notation is a mathematical notation that describes the limiting behavior of a function when the argument tends towards a particular value or infinity.\n\nBy this, Yeat means that he will always be on top for eternity like the Big O.", "annotation_id": "27005180", "url": "https://genius.com/27005180", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "I’m not your friend, your twizz’, your cousin, listen, no, I’m not friendly", "vault_lines": ["I'm not your friend, your twizz', your cousin, listen, no, I'm not friendly"], "meaning": "Yeat makes it clear, if you are not his friend, Twizz (word for “bro”), or  related, he is going to take you as a threat to him or his money.", "annotation_id": "26964775", "url": "https://genius.com/26964775", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "You broke, lil’ bitch, we in the big boy league, you still countin’ them pennies (Bitch)", "vault_lines": ["You broke, lil' bitch, we in the big boy league, you still countin' them pennies (Bitch)"], "meaning": "Yeat is comparing his vast amounts of wealth to him being in the “big leagues”, making a lot of money. Yeat then states his hater’s wealth is so minuscule they are still collecting Pennies to get by.", "annotation_id": "26964729", "url": "https://genius.com/26964729", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "I’ll fly with the birds", "vault_lines": ["I was just talkin' to God, I'll fly with the birds, I'll fly with the cranes"], "meaning": "This is a nod to Summrs‘ “Bird Business” term he makes in songs like “Swing Ya Pole.”\n\nDon’t get your face took off, lil' pussy, you know I fly with the birds\n\nYeat has collaborated with Summrs numerous times on songs like “Countup,” “Already Said It,” and “Alien Language,” amongst many others.", "annotation_id": "26952630", "url": "https://genius.com/26952630", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
