{"type": "song", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Expect You", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Youngboy-never-broke-again-i-expect-you-lyrics", "genius_title": "I Expect You", "genius_id": 6156756, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Forgive Them", "line": "You’ll do somethin’ low and lose your head, and get your toes up", "vault_lines": ["You'll do somethin' low and lose your head, and get your toes up"], "meaning": "YoungBoy lays out a graphic description of the swift, lethal consequences that come from moving recklessly or dishonorably in the streets.\n\nThe phrase “do somethin' low” refers to committing a dirty, underhanded act—such as snake behavior, crossing an ally, or executing a sloppy, uncalculated hit. In this lifestyle, operating without honor or intelligence instantly lowers a person’s street standing and makes them a target.\n\nThe dual consequences he outlines are absolute:\n\n\n“Lose your head”: This operates on two levels. Literally, it points to decapitation or taking a fatal gunshot to the head during an ambush. Structurally, it describes losing composure or panicking under pressure, which leads to the fatal mistakes that get a person killed.\n“Get your toes up”: A direct reference to a corpse lying flat on a gurney or a morgue table, where the feet are pointed straight up.\n\n\n\nBy chaining these descriptions together, he is reminding his rivals that a single moment of low-level, desperate thinking results in an immediate trip to the graveyard. – Gemini AI & Me", "annotation_id": "40383265", "url": "https://genius.com/40383265", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Forgive Them", "line": "I’m on East Poke livin’ lawless, cocaína in my trousers", "vault_lines": ["I'm on East Poke livin' lawless, cocaína in my trousers"], "meaning": "By shouting out “East Poke,” he is referencing East Polk Street, a familiar area in his hometown of Baton Rouge, Louisiana. Naming a specific block proves he still maintains a direct, physical connection to the neighborhood that raised him.\n\nStating that he is “livin' lawless, cocaína in my trousers” reinforces that his mindset hasn’t shifted just because his operations have evolved. He openly admits to personally carrying weight (“cocaína”) in his own pockets, showing a defiant disregard for law enforcement. It highlights a recurring theme in his music: while he has upgraded his logistics to protect his circle from legal jeopardy, he is still perfectly willing to take those exact same lawless risks on his own shoulders when he is back on his home turf. – Gemini AI", "annotation_id": "40383255", "url": "https://genius.com/40383255", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Forgive Them", "line": "I done upgraded, I don’t need you to hide my dealings in your blouses", "vault_lines": ["I done upgraded, I don't need you to hide my dealings in your blouses"], "meaning": "YoungBoy reflects on his operational growth, highlighting how he has elevated his security and the way he handles his business.\n\nThe declaration “I done upgraded” speaks to a shift in his street operations and lifestyle. He has leveled up his methods, moving away from sloppy, high-risk situations toward a more organized and secure way of moving around.\n\nHe emphasizes this tactical shift by stating, “I don’t need you to hide my dealings in your blouses.” This references a common street tactic where a woman acts as a shield, concealing contraband—like drugs or weapons—inside her clothing to protect a male partner from being searched during a sudden police encounter. By telling her he no longer requires this, he is making it clear that his days of desperate, unorganized hustling are over. He has upgraded his logistics to a point where he no longer has to compromise her safety or place her in legal jeopardy just to protect his circle. – Gemini AI & me", "annotation_id": "40383227", "url": "https://genius.com/40383227", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Forgive Them", "line": "I was thinkin’, conversations about my aroma while I was just lustin’ over coffee", "vault_lines": ["I was thinkin', conversations about my aroma while I was just lustin' over coffee"], "meaning": "YoungBoy contrasts how people online and in the streets obsess over his reputation with how normal his actual, real-time mindset is.\n\nThe phrase “conversations about my aroma” uses scent as a metaphor for his aura. It describes how his name, presence, and street reputation are so heavy that people are constantly talking about him and sensing his “vibe” even when he is completely out of sight.\n\nThe flip side is “while I was just lustin' over coffee.” While everyone else is busy gossiping and tracking his aura, his actual focus is totally mundane. Craving a morning coffee shows he is just trying to clear his head, wake up, and get through the day like a normal person. It reveals a huge disconnect between the chaotic internet drama surrounding his name and his quiet personal routine.\n\nThere is also a clear phonetic double entendre with “lustin' over coffin.” This layer injects his usual dark imagery into the bar, suggesting that while people are casually talking about his aura, he is internally stuck in a grim headspace, obsessing over death and street violence while trying to just enjoy his morning. – Gemini AI", "annotation_id": "40383184", "url": "https://genius.com/40383184", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Forgive Them", "line": "This expedition’ll have tuition, but she done watched me get up off it and come up on you “Hold on, what you said, Top? You lost me”", "vault_lines": ["This expedition'll have tuition, but she done watched me get up off it and come up on you", "\"Hold on, what you said, Top? You lost me\""], "meaning": "YoungBoy uses clever wordplay and structural metaphors to explain how his dangerous journey through life operates like an expensive, real-world education.\n\nThe word “expedition” frames his career and street hustle as a long, perilous journey into unknown territory. Saying this journey “will have tuition” is a metaphor for the high price of admission in the streets. Just like college, learning how to survive and navigate this lifestyle isn’t free—it costs “tuition” in the form of prison time, betrayal, lost money, and bloodshed.\n\nThe phrase “but she done watched me get up off it” points to an intimate observer (likely the woman mentioned earlier in the verse). She has been a firsthand witness to his resilience, watching him bounce back after paying those heavy costs and suffering under strict setbacks.\n\nHe finishes with “and come up on you.” This is a direct flex of dominance over his rivals. Despite the expensive lessons and the struggles he had to endure, his bounce-back was so powerful that he ultimately surpassed and conquered his enemies, leaving him securely on top.\n\nHe immediately follows this up with “Hold on, what you said, Top? You lost me.” Since rap is rooted in storytelling and dialogue, YoungBoy uses this line to quote what a fan or a video reactor would say to themselves while listening. He knows his last clever line would go right over most heads, so he breaks the fourth wall to voice the listener’s exact confusion, highlighting his awareness of his own lyrical depth. – Gemini AI & me.", "annotation_id": "40383149", "url": "https://genius.com/40383149", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Forgive Them", "line": "I was caught up in flaws and it resulted to takin’ losses, but now I’m ballin’", "vault_lines": ["I was caught up in flaws and it resulted to takin' losses, but now I'm ballin'"], "meaning": "YoungBoy reflects on how his own reckless behavior and street wrongdoings heavily impacted his life and career early on.\n\nBeing “caught up in flaws” refers to his own self-destructive actions—such as legal battles, street beefs, or impulsive decisions. These personal missteps directly “resulted to takin' losses.” Primarily, these losses were financial; his wrongdoings cost him massive, lucrative opportunities and career milestones that could have secured him millions.\n\nHowever, the word “losses” also carries a heavy double entendre. While he was losing out on money, he was also taking devastating personal losses, including losing close friends to the system or to street violence due to the dangerous lifestyle.\n\nThe flex comes with “but now I’m ballin'.” Despite the ruined opportunities and immense personal pain of the past, he managed to pivot. He overcame his own mistakes and is now generating so much wealth that his current financial success completely eclipses those early setbacks. – Gemini AI & me", "annotation_id": "40383083", "url": "https://genius.com/40383083", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Forgive Them", "line": "And she know I don’t waste time, goodbye, all night, I grind", "vault_lines": ["And she know I don't waste time, goodbye, all night, I grind"], "meaning": "YoungBoy drops a direct, unfiltered look at his fast-paced lifestyle, showing how quickly he pivots from a sexual encounter right back to his work.\n\nThe phrase “she know I don’t waste time” is a blunt, physical reference. He is making it clear that he isn’t there to cuddle, talk, or drag things out; he gets straight to the point in the bedroom.\n\nThe immediate sign-off, “goodbye,” proves just how fast he moves. The moment he is finished, he is instantly out the door with no hesitation.\n\nHe wraps up the sequence with “all night, I grind,” which serves as his direct excuse for leaving so abruptly. He doesn’t have time to chill or sleep because his entire night is dedicated to his hustle—whether that means locking himself in the studio to record tracks or handling business on the block to keep his money coming in. – Gemini AI & me", "annotation_id": "40383054", "url": "https://genius.com/40383054", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Forgive Them", "line": "As soon as I get in, she gon’ feel it in her waist side", "vault_lines": ["As soon as I get in, she gon' feel it in her waist side"], "meaning": "The phrase “as soon as I get in” acts as a dual metaphor. On a literal level, it describes entering a home, hotel room, or vehicle after a long time away on the block or on tour. On a physical level, it is a direct reference to sexual penetration.\n\nThe consequence, “she gon' feel it in her waist side,” highlights the physical intensity of the encounter. The “waist side” references the pelvic region and hips, implying a heavy, passionate interaction that leaves a lasting physical impression. This type of lyric is a common trope in street rap, showcasing the artist’s transition from a hardened, hyper-vigilant figure outside to an aggressive, dominant partner behind closed doors. – Gemini AI", "annotation_id": "40383016", "url": "https://genius.com/40383016", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Forgive Them", "line": "Survive in the game, we all deal cocaine Officer, again, we don’t give no names", "vault_lines": ["Survive in the game, we all deal cocaine", "Officer, again, we don't give no names"], "meaning": "Selling “cocaine” isn’t flaunted as a choice or a luxury lifestyle; it is presented as a mandatory survival mechanism to escape systemic poverty within his environment.\n\nThe second half of the line pivots to a direct confrontation with law enforcement. Addressing a detective or cop as “Officer, again” implies a repetitive cycle of arrests and interrogations.\n\nThe declaration “we don’t give no names” is a fierce reaffirmation of the street’s absolute code of silence (no snitching). Even under immense pressure from federal or local authorities, loyalty to the crew and the neighborhood entirely outweighs cooperation with the justice system. To break this rule is considered the ultimate betrayal.", "annotation_id": "40383001", "url": "https://genius.com/40383001", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Forgive Them", "line": "Let you know, if you beef with me, my bros, they’ll try to kill them", "vault_lines": ["Let you know, if you beef with me, my bros, they'll try to kill them"], "meaning": "The spiritual mercy of the previous line is instantly shattered as YoungBoy snaps back to the brutal reality of his street ties.\n\nWhile he might personally find the spiritual space to say “I forgive them,” his crew—Never Broke Again / 4KT—does not operate on grace. He is making it clear that his personal forgiveness does not grant immunity. In the streets, “beef” isn’t a personal issue between two individuals; it is an automatic green light for the entire collective.\n\nBy stating “my bros, they’ll try to kill them,” he highlights a terrifying paradox: he can pray for his enemies' souls, but he cannot—and will not—stop the violent machinery of his squad once a line is crossed. Loyalty to the circle overrides any individual mercy. – Gemini AI", "annotation_id": "40382984", "url": "https://genius.com/40382984", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Forgive Them", "line": "Oh, Lord Oh, I forgive them, watch over thy children", "vault_lines": ["Oh, I forgive them, watch over thy children"], "meaning": "This line introduces a striking contrast by shifting from cold street threats to a solemn, gospel-infused prayer.\n\nBy crying out “Oh, Lord,” the speaker taps into a deep sense of spirituality that is common in Southern hip-hop, acknowledging a higher power amidst the chaos of his lifestyle.\n\nThe phrase “Oh, I forgive them” shows a complex mental state. Even though he is actively engaged in a deadly street war, he views his enemies with a sense of detached mercy, almost looking down from a higher spiritual plane. By asking God to “watch over thy children,” he groups both his allies and his enemies together as vulnerable souls who are simply trapped in the same vicious cycle of poverty and violence. He recognizes that everyone in this game is ultimately a “child” of God, lost and needing protection.- Gemini AI", "annotation_id": "40382955", "url": "https://genius.com/40382955", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Forgive Them", "line": "Behind enemy lines, what the fuck to find?", "vault_lines": ["Behind enemy lines, what the fuck to find?"], "meaning": "To be “behind enemy lines” means a rival has crossed over into turf controlled by YoungBoy or his associates (like Never Broke Again / 4KT). In the streets, moving deep into hostile territory without backing or authorization is a near-suicidal move.\n\nBy asking “what the fuck to find?”, he is mocking the intruders' motives. He implies there is absolutely nothing of value, profit, or clout for them to gain by slipping into his neighborhood. The only thing an opp will “find” waiting for them in his territory is a violent ambush or a body bag. – Gemini AI & Me", "annotation_id": "40382919", "url": "https://genius.com/40382919", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Forgive Them", "line": "Break a rule, you kill me, need to run, divide", "vault_lines": ["Break a rule, you kill me, need to run, divide"], "meaning": "YoungBoy drops a direct, icy warning to his rivals. The phrase “break a rule, you kill me” sets up the ultimate offense—if an enemy violates street boundaries or attempts an assassination on his life, the consequences are immediate.\n\nThe command “need to run, divide” is the mandatory survival advice for anyone foolish enough to cross that line. YoungBoy is stating that the moment a rival strikes, their only option to stay alive is to:\n\n\nRun: Instantly flee the city or the country to escape the inevitable retaliation.\nDivide: Completely isolate themselves and cut off their own circle, because YoungBoy’s gang will target anyone associated with them to get revenge.", "annotation_id": "40382902", "url": "https://genius.com/40382902", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Forgive Them", "line": "Know the soldier mind way, I had to bust for my nigga, oh, yeah, I", "vault_lines": ["Know the soldier mind way, I had to bust for my nigga, oh, yeah, I"], "meaning": "YoungBoy is admitting to a past act of violence against a close associate. He doesn’t treat this as a hypothetical scenario; instead, he explains that he actually had to eliminate someone in his inner circle because of a strict, “soldier mind” protocol. In YB’s world, street warfare completely overrides personal loyalty. If a friend becomes a liability or a threat, survival instincts dictate that they must be dealt with immediately like an enemy combatant.", "annotation_id": "40382827", "url": "https://genius.com/40382827", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
