{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Got That Shit", "line": "Eight 12s inside the trunk, nigga, it bump, nigga Fuck wrong with you? I slump niggas", "vault_lines": ["Eight 12s inside the trunk, nigga, it bump, nigga", "Fuck wrong with you? I slump niggas"], "meaning": "Youngboy is saying he has eight 12 inch speakers in his trunk which is extreme trunk rattling volume it indeed does bump", "annotation_id": "40313515", "url": "https://genius.com/40313515", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Got That Shit", "line": "Have them young slimes inside the street, in front your house, screamin’, “Redrum, nigga, redrum, nigga”", "vault_lines": ["Have them young slimes inside the street, in front your house, screamin', \"Redrum, nigga, redrum, nigga\""], "meaning": "“Redrum” is a slang term that means to kill a person as when “Redrum” is spelled backward, it reads, “Murder.” YoungBoy isn’t new to the phase as in October 2017, he released a track titled, “Red Rum” in which he rapped:\n\nThis that red rum shit, fuck how you come shit\nBetter keep your gun, bitch, fuck where you from, bitch\n\nHe also rapped about the term in his April 2018, “Preach” in which he broke down the meaning of the term:\n\nYoung nigga fillin' up his arm with some heroin\nHe was abandoned as a child screamin', “Red rum”\nYou spell it backwards, what that mean? Nigga, murder", "annotation_id": "29347986", "url": "https://genius.com/29347986", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Got That Shit", "line": "Got my cologne on, smellin’ clean, bitch I know you see me on that scene, bitch", "vault_lines": ["Got my cologne on, smellin' clean, bitch", "I know you see me on that scene, bitch"], "meaning": "The topic of the lyrics is about the artist’s confidence and pride in his appearance.\n\nThe phrase “Got my cologne on, smellin' clean” suggests that the artist takes care of his personal hygiene and wants to present himself well.\n\nThe line “I know you see me on that scene” implies that the artist knows he is noticed and admired by others in his social circle.", "annotation_id": "29010756", "url": "https://genius.com/29010756", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Got That Shit", "line": "And I been poppin’ my shit like a model Came from the bottom", "vault_lines": ["And I been poppin' my shit like a model", "Came from the bottom"], "meaning": "The line “And I been poppin' my shit like a model” suggests that the speaker is confident and boastful about their success or achievements. “Came from the bottom” implies that the speaker started from a disadvantaged or humble position and has now risen to a higher level of success. The overall context of the lyrics indicates a celebration of personal achievements and a sense of pride in overcoming adversity.", "annotation_id": "29010721", "url": "https://genius.com/29010721", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Got That Shit", "line": "This for all them young niggas out there gettin’ that money, huh This for all them bad bitches, get they own bread", "vault_lines": ["This for all them bad bitches, get they own bread"], "meaning": "The topic is about acknowledging and celebrating young individuals who are making money. It also recognizes and respects independent women who are financially independent. The context is related to the lyrics of the song “I Got That Shit” by YoungBoy Never Broke Again.", "annotation_id": "29010699", "url": "https://genius.com/29010699", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Got That Shit", "line": "If you see me with Herm, I’m drinkin’ Henn’ out the bottle", "vault_lines": ["If you see me with Herm, I'm drinkin' Henn' out the bottle"], "meaning": "This is reference to NBA Herm aka “Herm The Black Sheep”, NeverBrokeAgain affiliate and close friend of NBA YoungBoy.\n\nA figure who played a huge part in promoting the “Richest Opp” album, having appeared in the snippets and the first time air of the 2 opening song “Bitch Let’s Do It” and “I Got That Shit” on Instagram live.\n\nNBA Herm is also an active artist.", "annotation_id": "28591186", "url": "https://genius.com/28591186", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Got That Shit", "line": "I got that shit on my wrist, yeah (Got that shit on my wrist) Put that shit on my bitch, yeah (I put that shit on my bitch) I put that shit on my broad (Put that shit on my gang) Because she fuck me in the Rolls (Bust you for me in they brain) I got that shit in my pants (Slime), got that shit in my lungs Got that shit in my whip, I got that shit in my car I got that shit on my hip, on my waist with my rod", "vault_lines": ["Got that shit in my whip, I got that shit in my car", "I got that shit on my hip, on my waist with my rod"], "meaning": "On the chorus YoungBoy uses the word “shit” which can refer to “anything” or “something” to allude to how he has something or anything on him.\n\n“I got that shit in my lungs”\n-This can be having marijuana or weed inside his lung\n\n“I got that shit in my pants”\n-This can be having a gun or narcotics in his pants.\n\n“Got that shit in my whip/car”\n-This can mean having a gun or narcotics inside his motor vehicle.\n\n“I got that shit on my hip”\n-This definitely means having a weapon aside him for protection and safety at all times.\n\n“I put that shit on all my bros”\n-This may be a reference to clothes and luxurious designer wear.\n\nThat “shit” may be a reference to clothes, guns, narcotics and many others.", "annotation_id": "28591179", "url": "https://genius.com/28591179", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Got That Shit", "line": "Ho, I got that shit in my pants, got that shit in my lungs Got that shit in my whip, I got that shit in my car I got that shit on my hip, on my waist with my rod I got that shit on my clique, I put that shit all on my broad", "vault_lines": ["I got that shit in my pants, got that shit in my lungs", "Got that shit in my whip, I got that shit in my car", "I got that shit on my hip, on my waist with my rod", "I got that shit on my clique, I put that shit all on my broad"], "meaning": "On the chorus YoungBoy uses the word “shit” which can refer to “anything” or “something” to allude to how he has something or anything on him.\n\n“I got that shit in my lungs”\n-This can be having marijuana or weed inside his lung\n\n“I got that shit in my pants”\n-This can be having a gun or narcotics in his pants.\n\n“Got that shit in my whip/car”\n-This can mean having a gun or narcotics inside his motor vehicle.\n\n“I got that shit on my hip”\n-This definitely means having a weapon aside him for protection and safety at all times.\n\n“I put that shit on all my bros”\n-This may be a reference to clothes and luxurious designer wear.\n\nThat “shit” may be a reference to clothes, guns, narcotics and many others.", "annotation_id": "28591173", "url": "https://genius.com/28591173", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
