{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Free Lil Meechy off the line, niggas know I’m big slime (Big slime)", "vault_lines": ["Free Lil Meechy off the line, niggas know I'm big slime (Big slime)"], "meaning": "Lil Meechy is NBA YoungBoys friend who he later made a song about how he wants him free later on on the mixtape “Richest Opp” https://youtu.be/zU_DYYHyM3o", "annotation_id": "29022163", "url": "https://genius.com/29022163", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Mama told me for to take my Ritalin and I said, “No” (No! No!)", "vault_lines": ["Mama told me for to take my Ritalin and I said, \"No\" (No! No!)"], "meaning": "Ritalin is a brand for the Methylphenidate drug. The drug is used to control behavioural problems and increases one’s focus and attention; the drug is usually taken by people who are diagnosed with ADHD—Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder—a deficit that affects one’s concentration span.\n\nYoungBoy previously rapped about how he refused to take the drug in order to control the disorder in his December 2018, “Big Talk,” in which he rapped:\n\nAnd I remember one time, I think it was in ‘09\nAnd I couldn’t seem to stop cryin’, mama put me on medics\nAnd I never took Ritalin, a real killer, unapologetic\n\nDue to YoungBoy not taking the medication, he seems to not be focused and is always on the edge, leading to him becoming uneasy and destructive.", "annotation_id": "28885332", "url": "https://genius.com/28885332", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "They know I’m on house arrest so they feel like they official (Yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["They know I'm on house arrest so they feel like they official (Yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "On October 26, 2021, YoungBoy was released on a $1.5 million bail and was ordered by the judge to be on twenty-four-hour house arrest in Salt Lake City, Utah. Prior to his release, he was indicted in his home town of Baton Rouge, Louisiana, for a Federal firearm charge after being caught with firearms during the music video shoot for his November 2020, “Chopper City.”\n\nYoungBoy notes that Lil Durk and his affiliates are only dissing him because he’s on house arrest and legally can’t leave his home to get to them.", "annotation_id": "27382786", "url": "https://genius.com/27382786", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Nigga, I’m a real Blood (Blood), and I’m screamin’, “Blatt” (Blatt)", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, I'm a real Blood (Blood), and I'm screamin', \"Blatt\" (Blatt)"], "meaning": "Blatt stands for “blood love all the time”", "annotation_id": "26851889", "url": "https://genius.com/26851889", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Hah, yeah, it’s 4KTrey, Nawfside, 38, nigga, free DDawg", "vault_lines": ["Hah, yeah, it's 4KTrey, Nawfside, 38, nigga, free DDawg"], "meaning": "4KTrey is gang that he represents for slimes (4KT)\n\nNawfside is the place that Youngboy grew up and he mention it plenty of times in songs and made a song about in 2020’s album 38 baby 2 “Nawfside”\n\nDDawg is the cousin of NBA Youngboy and made a song in 2019 called “FREEDDAWG”", "annotation_id": "26851846", "url": "https://genius.com/26851846", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Used to fuck with Gucci ’til I seen he like them pussy niggas (Bitch)", "vault_lines": ["Used to fuck with Gucci 'til I seen he like them pussy niggas (Bitch)"], "meaning": "YoungBoy refers to fellow rapper, Gucci Mane who recently collaborated with Lil Durk on the two’s January 2022, “Rumors.” YoungBoy sends a shot towards Gucci as he feels he’s picking a side between him and Durk.\n\nHowever, Gucci didn’t take lightly to the diss as he followed up with his own track, his March 2022, “Publicity Stunt,” in which he mocked YoungBoy’s October 2019 hit single, “Make No Sense” in which YoungBoy rapped:\n\nI feel like I’m Gucci Mane in 2006\nAll these diamonds dancing on my fucking neck cost like four bricks\nAnd the way that I be toting on that strap don’t make no sense\nHe a million dollar nigga but be posted in the bricks, uh\n\nGucci responded by interpolating YB’s lyrics as he rapped:\n\n(I thought you felt like Gucci Mane in 2006)\n(I thought you felt like Gucci Mane in 2006)\n(I thought you felt like Gucci Mane in 2006)\n(I thought you felt like Gucci Mane in 2006)\n(Well damn)", "annotation_id": "26287249", "url": "https://genius.com/26287249", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "He called me a bitch, that’s India, that be yo’ ho (Yo’ ho)", "vault_lines": ["He called me a bitch, that's India, that be yo' ho (Yo' ho)"], "meaning": "Youngboy takes aim at India Royale,  Lil Durk’s fiance, with this line. India is a fashion influencer, most well-known for her relationship with the Chicago rapper. Top claims that while someone called him a “bitch,” the description is more accurate about India.\n\n\n\nLil Durk and India Royale", "annotation_id": "25276827", "url": "https://genius.com/25276827", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "I don’t fuck with CC, but my oldest brother Crip (Crip)", "vault_lines": ["I don't fuck with CC, but my oldest brother Crip (Crip)"], "meaning": "“CC” is a common substitution of letters “CK” in Crip gang culture, due to CK meaning Crip killer or Crab killer. For this reason, Crip members tend to replace the letters “CK” with “CC”. For example, the phrase “kick back” is written as “kicc bacc”.\n\nBasically, Youngboy is saying he doesn’t mess with CC (Crips), despite the fact that his oldest brother is a Crip.", "annotation_id": "25221266", "url": "https://genius.com/25221266", "state": "pending", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Quando got no filter, and he say that, they ain’t gon’ fuck wit’ him", "vault_lines": ["Quando got no filter, and he say that, they ain't gon' fuck wit' him"], "meaning": "YoungBoy refers to the disrespectful attitude of his label signee Quando Rondo toward Lil Durk, King Von, and their affiliates. Notably, in November 2020, an altercation between Quando and Von took a deadly turn when Quando’s affiliate Lul Tim fatally shot Von.\n\nFollowing Von’s death, Quando has continued to call out Durk and his Only the Family (OTF) crew, on tracks such as “End of Story”:\n\nBlood on your brother on the ground, go and pick your mans up\n\nSuch provocations have led to numerous threats against Quando’s life, forcing many of his shows to be cancelled.", "annotation_id": "25207217", "url": "https://genius.com/25207217", "state": "accepted", "votes": 107, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Feel like Boosie don’t even like me, bitch, don’t call my phone (Fuck you)", "vault_lines": ["Feel like Boosie don't even like me, bitch, don't call my phone (Fuck you)"], "meaning": "Here Youngboy Never Broke Again adds to the long list of people he’s namedropped on this record alone. Shortly after this line, the artist makes it clear that\n\nYou fuck with them, don’t fuck with me and that’s just how that go\n\nFans are unsure why the artist dissed Lil Boosie (also stylized  as simply, Boosie) because the artist has always had a high level of respect for Youngboy, however concluding from the line above, it may be due to the friendships Boosie has with other artists called out on this track.\n\nThis line can be taken with a grain of salt. BR and male lingo in general tends to be harsher when joking with friends. It’s possible he namedropped Boosie as a joke considering he says fuck 10 in his next adlib. Also Boosie just released a tape and last time YB mentioned Boosie (clubhouse) his numbers spiked", "annotation_id": "25204586", "url": "https://genius.com/25204586", "state": "pending", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Stomp him in his fuckin’ face, I left him with my Nike sign (Yeah, yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Stomp him in his fuckin' face, I left him with my Nike sign (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "To leave someone with a sign (common idiom), is to conclude a meetup or conversation by means of some form of physical gesture. A wave goodbye is a prime example of leaving someone with a sign. A nike sign is the symbolic representation of major corporation Nike, one of the most successful sportswear brands in the world, ever. The brand reached status of such renown that logos on storefronts, billboards and athleticwear mostly feature only the nike sign, a representation of how big the brand is as the leading company for sports sneakers and other items.\n\nThe gesture Youngboy Never Broke Again references here is the opposite of a wave goodbye. Following previous violent threats against the various subjects of this diss track, the artist says he will stomp Lil Durk out and leave him with his Nike sign (implying that the parting gesture will be the literal Nike sign off of his shoe due to the harsh impact from stomping the subject out)", "annotation_id": "25204491", "url": "https://genius.com/25204491", "state": "pending", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "How you talkin’ shit when nothin’ ain’t died about your cousin’nem? (Cousin, hah, hah)", "vault_lines": ["How you talkin' shit when nothin' ain't died about your cousin'nem? (Cousin, hah, hah)"], "meaning": "Here, YoungBoy Never Broke Again takes a shot at Lil Durk’s cousin, OTF Nunu, most notably known as Nuski.\n\nOn May 31, 2014, Nuski was fatally shot and eventually killed in the South-side of Chicago as his car was shot up; he tried to drive away while being shot at, however, he crashed and subsequently died.\n\nAs Durk showed love to commemorate his cousin’s death, YoungBoy took the advantage to mock it, and diss Durk as he questioned Durk’s capability to get revenge for the death of Nuski.\n\n\n\nLil Durk’s “Nuski” chain to commemorate his death", "annotation_id": "25204322", "url": "https://genius.com/25204322", "state": "accepted", "votes": 108, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Every nigga did a feature with you, slime out to get ’em", "vault_lines": ["Every nigga did a feature with you, slime out to get 'em"], "meaning": "Here Youngboy further clarifies that anyone who has done a feature with Lil Durk has something coming towards them.\n\n\n\nAnd in this case, it seems to be his homies that are being sent after Lil Durk’s associates with Youngboy being on house arrest for the time being.", "annotation_id": "25204308", "url": "https://genius.com/25204308", "state": "pending", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Bitch, don’t bring my baby mama up, she richer than your niggas (Rich)", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, don't bring my baby mama up, she richer than your niggas (Rich)"], "meaning": "YoungBoy is referring to one of his baby mamas Jania, who was dissed on Lil Durk’s February 2022 track, “AHHH HA:”\n\nI told Von leave that bitch alone, she post on OnlyFans\n\nKing Von was known to have a relationship with Jania before his death on November 6, 2020. Lil Durk disses Jania by insulting the method by which she makes money, while YoungBoy defends her by stating that she has more money than any of Lil Durk’s crew.", "annotation_id": "25204299", "url": "https://genius.com/25204299", "state": "accepted", "votes": 68, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Set ’em up then point a nigga, field goal, Romo Know I keep that nine with me, you can act like that you don’t know (Don’t know)", "vault_lines": ["Set 'em up then point a nigga, field goal, Romo", "Know I keep that nine with me, you can act like that you don't know (Don't know)"], "meaning": "YoungBoy references NFL quarterback Tony Romo, who played for the Dallas Cowboys and retired in 2016. He states that he will set up his opposition similar to an incident involving Tony Romo.\n\nDuring the 2006 NFL season, Tony Romo was responsible for setting up a field goal. Instead, he fumbled the ball which led to the Seahawks winning the 2006 NFC Wild Card game.\n\nRomo frequently held field goal kicks for the Cowboys.", "annotation_id": "25204282", "url": "https://genius.com/25204282", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Sarah Snyder always think I’m trippin’ ‘cause I’m real slow (Real fuckin’ slow)", "vault_lines": ["Sarah Snyder always think I'm trippin' 'cause I'm real slow (Real fuckin' slow)"], "meaning": "Sarah Snyder is the female Youngboy mentioned in his song Snow Bunny. His engineer/producer Jason follows her on instagram. Her IG (sarahfuckingsnyder)\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: Sarah Snyder wasn’t the one he was referring to on “Snow Bunny” because he said she was from Florida plus he also doesn’t know who she is. He obviously knows who Sarah Snyder is so it cant be her", "annotation_id": "25204098", "url": "https://genius.com/25204098", "state": "pending", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Clean up on aisle O (O, O), youngin let that chop blow", "vault_lines": ["Clean up on aisle O (O, O), youngin let that chop blow"], "meaning": "This is basically a declaration of war on O'Block, a low-income apartment complex in Chicago, Illinois. Dubbed “the most dangerous block in Chicago,” O'Block has been the home of popular rappers such as Chief Keef and Lil Durk.\n\n\n\nSpecifically, the “clean up” is likely a reference to the late King Von, who was shot and killed during an altercation with Quando Rondo’s crew. Further, the “youngin” is likely a reference to Lul Tim, who is widely believed to have killed Von.", "annotation_id": "25203332", "url": "https://genius.com/25203332", "state": "accepted", "votes": 79, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "YouTube streamers, they be dick-ridin’, don’t react no more", "vault_lines": ["YouTube streamers, they be dick-ridin', don't react no more (Horrid, run it up, fuck you)"], "meaning": "Youngboy is throwing shots at Reaction channels on youtube who pick and choose sides. He is throwing shots mainly at Adin Ross who he even dissed in another song of his “Dis & Dat” https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QepL7wh-E80\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: This was a shot at Kai Cenat because Kai and AMP was with Lil Durk so he’s basically saying if you fw Lil durk don’t react to my music no more.", "annotation_id": "25202975", "url": "https://genius.com/25202975", "state": "pending", "votes": 89, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "They be hatin’ on Tim and Quando, they act like they wrong (Fuck you)", "vault_lines": ["They be hatin' on Tim and Quando, they act like they wrong (Fuck you)"], "meaning": "Lul Timm is an upcoming rapper from Savannah, Georgia, and is the close friend of Quando Rondo; Timm was the shooter of King Von and is responsible for his death, hence YoungBoy mentioned him to mock Von’s death.\n\nYoungBoy notes that the media depict Timm and Quando as monsters for the death of Von, however, in the police report it was noted that Lul Timm shot Von in self-defence as he thought Quando’s life was in danger. All in all, YoungBoy states that Timm isn’t wrong for killing Von as he was just defending his friend. In August 2023, the murder charges against Timm were dropped as the case was considered self-defence.\n\nIn “Gangsta,” the January 2022 single by YoungBoy and Quando, Quando referred to Timm as he rapped:\n\nI’m steady screamin' gang baby, granny gran' baby righteous\nThree hundred bands later, I still ain’t drop and y'all united\nThey say Lul Timm the biggest opp\nStepped on that boy, don’t do no fightin'", "annotation_id": "25202949", "url": "https://genius.com/25202949", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Tell Apple I said, “Fuck ’em,” they promote his song", "vault_lines": ["Tell Apple I said, \"Fuck 'em,\" they promote his song (Say, 10, fuck you)"], "meaning": "Youngboy is taking shots at the music streaming platform “Apple Music” for promoting Lil Durks new song “Ahh Ha” https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_q6go0G49A0&feature=emb_title dissing Youngboy where he says “Niggas acting like they really like that since my brodie died (Von)\nJust got out the feds, you bring up murders with your police ass\nI told Von to leave that bitch alone, she post on OnlyFans (Yeah, eater)”", "annotation_id": "25202944", "url": "https://genius.com/25202944", "state": "pending", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "And that lil’ bitch, she say, “4L,” huh? I say, “Heads or tails, slime”", "vault_lines": ["And that lil' bitch, she say, \"4L,\" huh? I say, \"Heads or tails, slime\""], "meaning": "YoungBoy is referring to Kayla B, the sister of the late King Von. In particular, YoungBoy refers to a Tweet by Kayla:\n\nPussy, pussy, pussy, pussy!!!! Big 4L I’m a member 😈\n\nKayla was also referred to in YB’s January 2022, “Know Like I Know” in which he rapped:\n\nWhat she say? What she say, she say “Big 4L”? (Lil Top)\nAyy, ayy, I ain’t even finna get on your ass\n\nIn the lyric, YoungBoy raps directly to Von’s sister due to her getting involved in the beef—asking to play heads or tails for her life.", "annotation_id": "25202920", "url": "https://genius.com/25202920", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Your daddy hit the feds, fuck that nigga, he a bitch, too (He a bitch)", "vault_lines": ["Your daddy hit the feds, fuck that nigga, he a bitch, too (He a bitch)"], "meaning": "Youngboy is most likey dissing Lil Durks dad “Big Durk” who was released from jail on Feb 12, 2019. Big Durk was serving a two life sentence without the possibility of parole.\n\n\n\nBig Durk is on the right, sitting next to Lil Durk.", "annotation_id": "25202897", "url": "https://genius.com/25202897", "state": "pending", "votes": 77, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Pussy nigga dissin’ me, mad about his dead homie", "vault_lines": ["Pussy nigga dissin' me, mad about his dead homie"], "meaning": "YoungBoy responds to Durk’s “AHHH HA,” a direct diss against YoungBoy and his affiliates. On the track, Durk finds YoungBoy to only be capable of making empty threats.\n\nThey really don’t mean it, he say it in songs (Yeah, mean it, say it, songs)\nThey really don’t mean it, he play it in songs\n\nYoungBoy identifies that Durk’s anger stems from the death of his close friend and labelmate King Von. In November of 2020, Von was shot and killed in Atlanta following a fight with the artist Quando Rondo, who is signed to YoungBoy’s Never Broke Again label. Quando’s friend, Lul Timm, was charged with the murder of Von.\n\nYoungBoy previously dissed Von on his January 2022 track, “Bring The Hook”:\n\nMurder what they told us, Atlanta boy get fold up\n\nFollowing the release of “Bring The Hook,” YoungBoy and Durk traded threats, laid out in money, toward each other.", "annotation_id": "25202872", "url": "https://genius.com/25202872", "state": "accepted", "votes": 84, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Why he drop that wack-ass song? Pussy bitch, you should’ve known (Should’ve known)", "vault_lines": ["Why he drop that wack-ass song? Pussy bitch, you should've known (Should've known)"], "meaning": "Here, YoungBoy disses Lil Durk and his February 2022 track, “AHHH HA.” Lil Durk is also rumoured to have dissed YoungBoy first on that track, by singing:\n\nNiggas acting like they really like that since my Brodie died (Von)\nJust got out the feds, you bring up murders with your police ass\nI told Von to leave that bitch alone, she post on OnlyFans (Yeah, eater)", "annotation_id": "25202799", "url": "https://genius.com/25202799", "state": "accepted", "votes": 70, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "I’m bumpin’ Wooski, turnt up with some groupies while at my home", "vault_lines": ["I'm bumpin' Wooski, turnt up with some groupies while at my home"], "meaning": "Wooski or FBG Wooski is known to be an opposition of King Von and Lil Durk, with both referring to him several times throughout their songs. In particular, in Von and Durk’s October 2021, “Back Again,” Von rapped:\n\nShoot up everybody that’s outside\nBet Wooski feel this one (Boom-boom, boom-boom)\nI bet Wooski still twitchin' (Damn, damn-damn)\nHe changed, somethin' different\n\nYoungBoy continues to taunt Durk as he gives attention to his opposition, suggesting he’s now cliqued up with them. This could also be a response to Durk’s line in “AHHH HA,”:\n\nOld opps fuckin' with my new opps (Brr), oh, man (Brrah)\n\nIn a February 2022 interview of Billionare Black—one of Wooski’s affiliates—he noted that he spoke with YoungBoy’s friend, Herm Tha Blacksheep while also teasing a collaboration between YoungBoy and Wooski.", "annotation_id": "25202751", "url": "https://genius.com/25202751", "state": "accepted", "votes": 81, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Hate YoungBoy", "line": "Baby with ‘em, 4PF, four poles firin’ (Grr-grr)", "vault_lines": ["Baby with 'em, 4PF, four poles firin' (Grr-grr)"], "meaning": "YoungBoy disses his “Cross Me” and “One Shot” collaborator Lil Baby, namedropping the rapper’s 4PF label and implying that he won’t hesitate to shoot him and his crew.\n\nNotably, it was reported by DJ Akademiks in March 2021 that YoungBoy turned down a collaboration with Lil Baby due to underlying beef that wasn’t yet publicly known.\n\nFurther, Lil Baby is friends with YoungBoy’s adversary Lil Durk, with the duo releasing a collaborative album, The Voice of the Heroes, in June 2021.", "annotation_id": "25202563", "url": "https://genius.com/25202563", "state": "accepted", "votes": 116, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
