{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Know", "line": "Guess I should sit here while the devil dance on my soul", "vault_lines": ["Guess I should sit here while the devil dance on my soul"], "meaning": "is a vivid metaphor for enduring emotional pain and inner turmoil while the other person is absent or leaving.", "annotation_id": "41266635", "url": "https://genius.com/41266635", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Know", "line": "You’re mine, I can trust you and I know that I know", "vault_lines": ["You're mine, I can trust you and I know that I know"], "meaning": "The line “You’re mine, I can trust you and I know that I know” expresses a deep sense of trust and emotional connection. NBA YoungBoy is conveying certainty and security in his relationship with someone, affirming that they belong to each other and that he can rely on them. The repetition of “I know that I know” emphasizes his confidence in this bond, suggesting that despite any doubts or challenges they might face, he’s sure of this person’s loyalty and trustworthiness.\n\nIn the context of YoungBoy’s music, which often deals with themes of betrayal, trust, and vulnerability, this line stands out as a rare moment of emotional clarity and reassurance. It reflects his desire for stability and trust in a world where those qualities are often hard to find.", "annotation_id": "33335579", "url": "https://genius.com/33335579", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Know", "line": "Fire burnin’ in my lungs, can’t get the words off my tongue", "vault_lines": ["Fire burnin' in my lungs, can't get the words off my tongue"], "meaning": "• “Fire burnin’ in my lungs”: This metaphor suggests intense emotional or mental anguish, like he’s holding in a burning feeling that he can’t express. The fire could symbolize anger, sadness, or unresolved feelings that are consuming him from within.\n    • “Can’t get the words off my tongue”: Despite this overwhelming emotion, he’s struggling to communicate what he’s feeling. This could point to difficulty in expressing his emotions or feeling like no one would truly understand him if he did.\n\nThese lines highlight the tension between intense emotions and the difficulty of opening up or finding the right words to convey that pain. It adds to the theme of emotional struggle and isolation that often appears in YoungBoy’s music.", "annotation_id": "33335575", "url": "https://genius.com/33335575", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Know", "line": "You tellin’ me you leavin’ ’cause it’s hard Guess I should sit here while the devil dance on my soul", "vault_lines": ["Guess I should sit here while the devil dance on my soul"], "meaning": "• “You tellin’ me you leavin’ ‘cause it’s hard”: This suggests someone is leaving YoungBoy because the situation or relationship has become difficult. It reflects a sense of betrayal or disappointment, as he expected the person to stay through tough times rather than walking away when things get challenging.\n    • “Guess I should sit here while the devil dance on my soul”: This metaphor speaks to the emotional and spiritual battle he’s going through. The “devil dancing on my soul” suggests he’s feeling overwhelmed by negativity, pain, or inner demons. It implies he’s left to struggle alone with his suffering, without the support or understanding of those around him.\n\nTogether, these lines convey the deep hurt of being left to face hardships on his own and the emotional toll that betrayal takes on him. It highlights YoungBoy’s internal conflicts and the sense of isolation he often expresses in his music.", "annotation_id": "33335559", "url": "https://genius.com/33335559", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Know", "line": "They throwing bombs and I don’t have no shield", "vault_lines": ["They throwing bombs and I don't have no shield"], "meaning": "Youngboy expresses the lyrics, “They throwing bombs and I don’t have no shield” because he has nobody to help him and support through the stuff and pain he has been going through. Being overwhelmed by emotions or sadness, without any way to protect yourself from it.", "annotation_id": "33274830", "url": "https://genius.com/33274830", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
