{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I Want You", "line": "Every nigga dissed me, half them dead", "vault_lines": ["Every nigga dissed me, half them dead"], "meaning": "This is a diss to multiple opps so we’ll break it down from the beginning. Garrett Burton AKA Da Real Gee Money was a rapper also from Youngboy’s hometown Baton Rouge, Louisiana. It’s said that Gee Money helped inspire the young YB and if you go back to Gee Money’s old music videos (IPhone 6 in particular) you can see Youngboy in the background. However the two had a falling out around the time Youngboy started his career. Before NBA, he was in another group called TBG (Top Boy Gorillas) but he left because he felt like he wasn’t getting the money or attention that he felt he deserved. In his earlier mixtapes like Mind Of Menace parts 1 and 2, you can find lyrics of Youngboy sneak dissing his old crew.\n\nThis prompted a response from Gee Money who dropped the diss track “Industry”. It got worse when in an interview with SayCheese, Gee Money admitted to sleeping with Youngboy’s sister. Gee Money would later be shot and killed on September 10th, 2017 at 22 years old.\n\nThe most known and popular one however is with Chicago rapper King Von. King Von allegedly had a relationship with Youngboy’s ex-girlfriend (And mother of his son Kacey) Jania Meshell. This prompted Youngboy to make a song with King Von’s ex Asian Doll. Then on an Instagram Livestream, King Von was listening to Youngboy’s music before saying that Youngboy wasn’t a gangster and that he “caps in his raps”. Youngboy would then respond (not directly) by saying “When my son gets older, I’m gonna make sure he f*ck’s your daughter.”\n\nBut it didn’t seem to be that bad as Von was friends with Youngboy’s artist “Quando Rondo”. But on November 6th 2020, Von was celebrating the release of his debut album “Welcome To O’Block” which had came out a week before in Atlanta (Rondo’s hometown). Strangely enough, Von’s album was a 1 number higher on the charts than Youngboy’s second studio album “Top”. And another strange thing is that when Von was leaving his show, he was listening to a track by Youngboy and Lil Wayne. Von would later travel to Monoco Hookah Lounge for unknown reasons when someone woke him out of his sleep to inform him that Quando was there.\n\nHe got out the car and proceeded to assault Quando. Quando‘s friend Lul Timm hopped out the car and shot Von 4 times. He would be pronounced dead that night at 26. This would start a beef between Youngboy and Lil Durk (Von’s boss and close friend) with Durk releasing the diss track “AHHH HA!” and Youngboy firing back with “I Hate Youngboy”.\n\nThe recent one is JayDaYoungan, a rapper from Bogalusa, Louisiana. Their beef began with Jay posted a snippet of a song which had a Youngboy feature. Youngboy didn’t like that and went on a rant on Instagram about it. It got even worse when Jay revealed that YB had asked him to stop messing with his ex-girlfriend’s Kaylyn and Jania. Jay then dropped the track “38K” (A diss to Youngboy’s old home address 38 Rd). The beef seemed to die down after a few months or so. But on July 27th 2022, Jay was sitting outside his childhood home with his dad when two men started shooting their way. They tried to run back into the house but two more men came from behind the house and shot him 8 times. He was pronounced dead later that night at 24.\n\nYoungboy never seemed to disrespect him in death however (Until this song of course). It was really his fan base because Jay died a month before Youngboy’s “The Last Slimeto” album came out. So when family and friends took to social media to grieve, YB fans commented under it “Pre-Save The Last Slimeto”\n\nNow you’re probably like, why did you give us this long story. To show you that you shouldn’t diss YB or your going to be meeting the people mentioned in those sections.", "annotation_id": "28315826", "url": "https://genius.com/28315826", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
