{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "It Could Go", "line": "Mama, please, let me wipe the tears off top of your eye I look deep and I could see myself dyin’", "vault_lines": ["Mama, please, let me wipe the tears off top of your eye", "I look deep and I could see myself dyin'"], "meaning": "Mama please let me wipe the tears off top of yo eye i look deep and i could see myself dyin", "annotation_id": "27126694", "url": "https://genius.com/27126694", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "It Could Go", "line": "When you ’round me, don’t type hard, you surround white boys", "vault_lines": ["When you 'round me, don't type hard, you surround white boys"], "meaning": "Yb taking shots at Druski cus he talked bad bout Jaz on Instagram comment. Druski known to stay round Jack Harlow. Don’t type poor*", "annotation_id": "26944056", "url": "https://genius.com/26944056", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "It Could Go", "line": "I ain’t no 2Pac of this generation, I’m AI YoungBoy You try to get ahead of this generation, you’ll get a run for it Got a lot of risks inside my situation, but I was born for it", "vault_lines": ["You try to get ahead of this generation, you'll get a run for it"], "meaning": "Throughout YoungBoy Never Broke Again’s career, he has been compared to and is thought to be the 2Pac of the current music and hip-hop generation.\n\n2Pac or Tupac Shakur was an American rapper who was murdered in 1996. He is widely considered as both the most influential, as well as the one and only greatest rapper of all time.\n\nDespite there being a vast difference between YoungBoy and 2Pac in terms of musical style, both artists have been through a wide range of legal troubles while also being involved in major controversies at their young ages, all while having immense success in their given time, leading to the comparisons.\n\nYoungBoy could also be relating this to The Game’s latest studio album, DRILLMATIC – Heart vs. Mind after he was removed from the album due to his feature price being too far over the budget. This lead to The Game stating that NBA YoungBoy is the 2Pac of the current hip-hop generation.\n\nDespite the honor one might feel after being compared to one of the greatest hip-hop artists to have ever performed, YoungBoy declines the title and makes it clear that he’s nobody but himself—as referred to as AI YoungBoy, a name inspired by basketball hall of famer, Allen Iverson.", "annotation_id": "26863096", "url": "https://genius.com/26863096", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
