{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "I’m Bored (Bang Shit / Thug Nigga Story)", "line": "The police took my tiger, bitch, I’m bout to buy a lion", "vault_lines": ["The police took my tiger, bitch, I'm bout to buy a lion"], "meaning": "YoungBoy has only bought two exotic animals, a monkey and a white tiger cub.    In late 2017/early 2018, NBA YoungBoy posted videos of a white tiger cub, leading to an investigation by the Louisiana Department of Wildlife and Fisheries.  The cub was found in an unpermitted location in Louisiana, suffering from malnutrition and ringworm, and required immediate medical care.The cub, later named Nola, was transferred to the Lions, Tigers & Bears sanctuary in Alpine, California.\nOn January 6th, 2018, it was reported the 5 month old white tiger was seized in Louisiana via news.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/zDsD2CQ9Uxs\nin this video, the tiger is seen to be all better.\nthe channel also had said in the new, “(\"Source: Lions, Tigers, & Bears) The organization says the cub was malnourished, lethargic, and suffering from ringworm when they were contacted about a month ago.”\n\n\n\nHe had also faced blacklash from fans and people who knew about the news of labelling him by animal abuse.\n\n “THANK YOU FOR RESCUING THIS SWEETIE  –  THANK GOD YOU GOT HIM JUST IN TIME  – thank you for your great work – he’s beautiful! – wishing you much success!  – PLEASE, let’s find the criminals who EXPLOIT & abuse these magnificent animals and SHUT THEM DOWN PERMANENTLY! – Laws and their enforcement MUST be applied.” – Commenter from YouTube\n\nOr in a different video, someone worries how Youngboy hold the tigers and states, “Oh poor baby, look at the way he holds him :(” – Commenter from YouTube\n\nAs he posted more and more random videos, snippets of his songs, you can see the white tiger in the videos which you can find on YouTube or a NBA YOUNGBOY page, he was never charged out of anything at the end.", "annotation_id": "38172777", "url": "https://genius.com/38172777", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
