{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Kentrell Talk", "line": "I think, I think, I think the rap game, I think the rap game like just slowly like fadin’ away Like this shit gon’ be over with Like, it ain’t gon’ be the, the hot thing that it is, like", "vault_lines": ["I think, I think, I think the rap game, I think the rap game like just slowly like fadin' away", "Like this shit gon' be over with", "Like, it ain't gon' be the, the hot thing that it is, like"], "meaning": "YoungBoy doesn’t think today’s rap game will last forever, he knows much will change and is open for the possibility that it decreases in popularity over time.\n\nHe has earlier said that he will quit making music and this could be because he no longer feels that the rap is his life. He maybe doesn’t want to see himself solely as a rapper but something different, this isn’t only negative but could mean that he wants to expand in new areas and explore new passions.\n\nSince YoungBoy was a baby up until today his whole life has been about hip-hop, all his inspiration has been taken from rap and hip-hop culture. He might be ready for a change of mind-set and not only focus on one career.", "annotation_id": "26987196", "url": "https://genius.com/26987196", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
