{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "King Of The Jungle", "line": "Lion kings", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "“Lion Kings” can also be heard as an extension of the last line, “Lyin' kings.” Saying that, on the other hand, NBA’s haters are the kings of lying and spreading rumors.\n\nAnd while this might be a stretch, DJ Drama might also be referring to YB’s haters as only lion kings (kings of lions), whilst YB is the king of the entire jungle to say that they are beneath him. He owns their domain which, insinuated by the opening line of the song, is the rap game.", "annotation_id": "41520036", "url": "https://genius.com/41520036", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
