{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Legacy", "line": "Now it’s a bloody empire (I, I, I) To make it there, some of us gotta die (Oh, I, I, I, I)", "vault_lines": ["To make it there, some of us gotta die"], "meaning": "Probably referring to the streets and how there’s always violence, mainly saying how everyone is envious and jealous of each other if they start getting money to get out of the hood.", "annotation_id": "39468272", "url": "https://genius.com/39468272", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Legacy", "line": "I been tryna calm down, but I’m strapped with that glizzy", "vault_lines": ["I be tryna calm down, but I’m strapped with that glizzy"], "meaning": "He still putting his image of how he will protect his life due to his past and current problems.", "annotation_id": "39468264", "url": "https://genius.com/39468264", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Legacy", "line": "But now I’m on the yacht poppin’ bottles with my day one niggas", "vault_lines": ["But now I’m on the yacht poppin bottles with my day one niggas"], "meaning": "After the storm, and his trials, he’s with those who kept it real instead of being fake, by showing that he really made it, and showing that he also made it in a specific part of his life where he really has the money to celebrate with his wins. (2/2)", "annotation_id": "39468235", "url": "https://genius.com/39468235", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Legacy", "line": "They the ones that I never ain’t see Every time I was standin’ in trial", "vault_lines": ["They the ones that I never ain’t see"], "meaning": "This word play refers to how people show up the most important things in your life. His court dates referred to him possibly being away for years in prison, or possibly him winning the court date. It refers to a win or loss situation, which he says he never saw them. (½)", "annotation_id": "39468227", "url": "https://genius.com/39468227", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Legacy", "line": "Mama, I did it (Slide, oh yeah!) All at my funeral, I’m gon’ be flexin’ on ‘em (I’m gon’ be flexin’)", "vault_lines": ["Mama I did it, all in my funeral, gon’ be flexin on em’"], "meaning": "NBA Youngboy, whose real name is Kentrell Gaulden, alludes to a reoccurring theme within his music; Death. NBA YoungBoy & his crew mates (Quando Rondo, Birdman, etc.) have been shot at & have been involved in several attempted assaults that could have resulted in death. NBA expresses the relief of knowing that when he dies he’ll die more successful than his haters, doubters, and/ or rivals.", "annotation_id": "29084487", "url": "https://genius.com/29084487", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
