{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Let ’Em Kno", "line": "Don’t got no father, I’m no nigga’s son", "vault_lines": ["Don't got no father, I'm no nigga's son"], "meaning": "During this time he recorded this, his dad was sent to 55 years in prison when he was 8 years old, because his own brother snitched on him over robbery and an attempted murder. After that he was raised by his grandma, then after she passed, he went to 33’s family since they were already considered as “Brothers.”\n\nWith YoungBoy’s dad being in prison, in most of his songs, he often talks about him, Unreleased and released.\nIt shows the impact of his father had on him, and how he had to learn on his own, and things through Montana, that he claims as a father, but as a step dad because he also showed him the way to survive in BR.", "annotation_id": "38902314", "url": "https://genius.com/38902314", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
