{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Letter to Big Dump", "line": "Got off of drugs, I’m strong, no, they ain’t feelin’ me now", "vault_lines": ["Got off of drugs, I'm strong, no, they ain't feelin' me now"], "meaning": "Since the Baton Rouge Judge placed limits on the drugs Youngboy can have access too, he has no choice but to stay sober and deal with the withdrawals. This led to him finally getting rid of these drugs and he thinks that because of that people are starting to not relate to him as much.", "annotation_id": "27565432", "url": "https://genius.com/27565432", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
