{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Level I Want To Reach", "line": "Got alarms inside the home, but keep a hundred straps", "vault_lines": ["Got alarms inside the home, but keep a hundred straps"], "meaning": "Aside from the alarms Kentrell owns for home security, he also keeps weapons for his own safety as-well as his family’s. Kentrell is a father to eight children, and he will not take a chance on any potential intruder.", "annotation_id": "24038903", "url": "https://genius.com/24038903", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Level I Want To Reach", "line": "We don’t got no room for all your friends Tension in the room soon as you walked in Takin’ off, turned on you just ’cause I can, o", "vault_lines": ["We don't got no room for all your friends"], "meaning": "Youngboy implies he does not want this unnamed girl to bring her friends. He has mentioned on other songs how he enjoys the “one on one” environment with his significant others, such as on his song “No Where”, also from the Sincerely Kentrell album. “I wanted it to be just me and you all alone.”", "annotation_id": "24038895", "url": "https://genius.com/24038895", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
