{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Life Support", "line": "Now I got grams like I’m Frank Matthews, jewelry weigh at least a kilo", "vault_lines": ["Now I got grams like I'm Frank Matthews, jewelry wеigh at least a kilo"], "meaning": "Frank Larry Matthews (born February 13, 1944), also known as “Black Caesar”, “Mark IV” and “Pee Wee” is an American drug trafficker most notably known for the sale of heroin and cocaine in the Eastern states of the USA from 1965 to 1972 prior to his untimely arrest before he allegedly took $20 million and disappeared.\n\nIn the lyric, YoungBoy compares himself to the likes of Matthews suggesting he himself is responsible for the trade and sales of drugs, being charged for the possession of drugs several times throughout his life. This can also be the case since YoungBoy is from the Northside of Baton Rouge, Louisiana, a city with one of the highest crime rates in the USA.\n\nFurthermore, this isn’t the first time YoungBoy has mentioned an infamous drug lord. In his December 2018, “Slime Belief,” YoungBoy rapped about and compared himself to the likes of Griselda Blanco, a Colombian cocaine kingpin:\n\nCan you make it better? Trap out like Griselda\nPost up with Berettas, hustlin' through the night, yeah\n\nYoungBoy also notes that due to his similarities with Matthews, he’s in a position where he can purchase jewelry that weighs a kilo — suggesting that it’s extremely heavy due to its immense worth.\n\n\n\nPictured: Frank Matthews' 1972 mugshot after being indicted on six counts of tax evasion and conspiracy to distribute heroin and cocaine", "annotation_id": "23968100", "url": "https://genius.com/23968100", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Life Support", "line": "I’m like, “Bae, I could have died that night, my whip had flipped over”", "vault_lines": ["I'm like, \"Bae, I could have died that night, my whip had flipped over\""], "meaning": "This line could be stating Youngboys car accident in 2017.\nExotic Car Rental in Los Angeles claims the rapper crashed the 2016 Lamborghini Huracan Spyder on June 29 after speeding down a residential street … then left it on the side of the road with severe damage and took off.\n\nAccording to the docs, YoungBoy’s agent actually rented the car on June 27 and agreed he’d be the only person to operate the Lambo and would be “personally liable for any and all damages.”\n\nExotic Car Rental claims the car was totaled, with damages exceeding $350,000. They want YoungBoy and his agent to pay … plus any additional costs related to the wreck-and-run.\n\nSources close to YoungBoy deny he had any involvement with the car accident and claim the Lambo was rented by a guy in his crew … not his agent. We’re told the reason the car was left behind is because there was an injury that required a ride to the hospital.", "annotation_id": "23948310", "url": "https://genius.com/23948310", "state": "pending", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
