{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Like A Jungle (Out Numbered)", "line": "I ain’t no rat, that’s disrespect, these pussy bitches tried to set traps", "vault_lines": ["I ain't no rat, that's disrespect, these pussy bitches tried to set traps"], "meaning": "Yb is referring to kodak black calling him a rat back in 2020. Kodak also pledged that Yb cooperated with the police back when Yaya Maywheater had stabbed his pregnant ex gf", "annotation_id": "26742173", "url": "https://genius.com/26742173", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Like A Jungle (Out Numbered)", "line": "Inside my cell, me and my dawg got hooked on food, should I sue for that?", "vault_lines": ["Inside my cell, me and my dawg got hooked on food, should I sue for that?"], "meaning": "Here Youngboy is talkin about his time incarcerated, him and his cell mate got hooked on dog food aka Heroin. He says should I sue for that I’m guessing(I could be wrong) but in prison drugs are accessible pretty easily and COs basically do the dealing most of the time.", "annotation_id": "26737563", "url": "https://genius.com/26737563", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Like A Jungle (Out Numbered)", "line": "Just know I’m with you, you on a compound, I’m in a mansion feelin’ chained right now", "vault_lines": ["Just know I'm with you, you on a compound, I'm in a mansion feelin' chained right now"], "meaning": "Speaking directly to C-Murder, YoungBoy Never Broke Again explains how he feels “chained” and incarcerated as though he faces the same circumstances as C-Murder despite being on house arrest in a luxurious mansion, compared to C in a dirty, unhygienic prison — otherwise known as a “compound.”\n\nIn 2002, C-Murder was found guilty of second-degree murder regarding the then 16-year-old Steve Thomas, subsequently being sentenced to life in prison.\n\nIn comparison to this, in September 2020, YoungBoy was acquitted of various charges, including distribution and manufacturing of drugs and possession of stolen firearms. Alongside this, in March 2021, YoungBoy was arrested by the FBI after leading the LAPD on a car chase. Eventually, YB was arrested and booked on federal firearms charges.\n\nIn October 2021, just a month after the release of his chart-topping album Sincerely, Kentrell, YB was released on $1.5 million bail and was set to be on strict 24-hour house arrest.\n\nSince his release, YB has been on house arrest and has not been able to leave his house in Utah. In July 2022, YB was found not guilty of the charges regarding his federal firearm case, however, he still stayed on house arrest. YB’s legal team demanded to be taken off of house arrest, however, the motion was declined.", "annotation_id": "26734840", "url": "https://genius.com/26734840", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Like A Jungle (Out Numbered)", "line": "This for, this for OG Bossalinie (Believe that)", "vault_lines": ["This for, this for OG Bossalinie (Believe that)"], "meaning": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again claims that he went to the American rapper and entrepreneur Master P for “game” — a slang term for advice, in this case, most likely for the music industry or legal issues. However, he mentions that P decided to charge him in exchange for advice.\n\nYoungBoy further mentions that he can get any “game” he needs from the lyrical contents of Bossalinie, the March 1999 pop album released by C-Murder. The album peaked at #2 on the Billboard 200 after selling over 175,000 units in its first week.\n\nFurthermore, “Like A Jungle (Out Numbered)” is a remix of the song “Like a Jungle” which appeared on Bossalinie and was produced by Master P.", "annotation_id": "26727301", "url": "https://genius.com/26727301", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Like A Jungle (Out Numbered)", "line": "OG, right now, I’m battlin’ with some shit with a bitch who I been with since I was a child She a fan of most of my opps, it seemin’ wild", "vault_lines": ["OG, right now, I'm battlin' with some shit with a bitch who I been with since I was a child", "She a fan of most of my opps, it seemin' wild"], "meaning": "Here YoungBoy Never Broke Again refers to the mother of his child, Jania Meshell, most notably known as Nene or Ni, who he had known since he was a child.\n\nYoungBoy explains that she is a “fan of most of [his] opps” which can lead back to Jania’s relationship with the late King Von who was in several altercations with YoungBoy prior to his death who YoungBoy’s affiliate, Lul Timm was responsible for.\n\nJania was previously mentioned by Von’s close friend Lil Durk in the diss track, “AHHH HA,” directed to YB where Durk rapped:\n\nI told Von to leave that bitch alone, she post on OnlyFans (Yeah, eater)\n\nThe release of the song led to YB responding with his own diss track, “I Hate YoungBoy,” where he spoke on the matter:\n\nBitch, don’t bring my baby mama up, she richer than your niggas (Rich)\n\nYB also refers to her in his August 2022, “Lost Soul Survivor” where he rapped:\n\nNene left and they saw I was sad, saw me down, thought I’d never shake back\nPut a twenty on top of that twenty, come out forty mil', and I’m fuckin' with that", "annotation_id": "26727163", "url": "https://genius.com/26727163", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Like A Jungle (Out Numbered)", "line": "Look, I’m a solider, but all the weight on my shoulders make me feel like I’m outnumbered, feel like I’m outnumbered Look, I’m a solider, but all the weight on my shoulders make me feel like I’m outnumbered, feel like I’m outnumbered", "vault_lines": ["I'm feelin' like I'm outnumbered, OG"], "meaning": "Being “a soldier” typically refers to one who has served in the military, however, YoungBoy uses it metaphorically to explain how he has pursued something despite its difficulty.\n\nFurthermore, when YoungBoy explains how he has “all the weight on [his] shoulders,” making him “feel like [he is] outnumbered,” he could refer to him always being called “better” despite not receiving much, or mutual support from other artists and the rap industry, leading him to feel “outnumbered.”\n\nYoungBoy noting that he feels “outnumbered” could also refer to other artists in the rap industry — who he has “beef” with — cliquing up together and making music with each other. In contrast, he rarely does features or collaborates with other artists. YB has mentioned this in his August 2022, “Kamikaze,” where he begins the song with:\n\nLook, niggas cliquin' up like hoes, huh\nPull up and I’m strapped down with a lot of poles\nYou better have your flag if that’s the gang you chose (Let’s go)\nYou better hit the gas and get your name unknown (Bitch)", "annotation_id": "26726855", "url": "https://genius.com/26726855", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
