{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Like Madden", "line": "I went to sleep on the wild, wild west And I came from the dirty, dirty south", "vault_lines": ["I went to sleep on the wild, wild west", "And I came from the dirty, dirty south"], "meaning": "Youngboy is from Batoun Rouge, Louisiana. A city filled with violence and crime. In this line, Youngboy uses the metaphors wild west and dirty south to represent where he is from.", "annotation_id": "34371623", "url": "https://genius.com/34371623", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Like Madden", "line": "Ooh (Fresher than a motherfucker, lookin’ like a whole lick)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This statement probably alludes to youngboy’s attire. The rapper considers himself fly and frequently wears high-end clothing and jewelry. When someone wears expensive clothing and jewelry, they are a potential target for robbery, also known as a lick.", "annotation_id": "34371599", "url": "https://genius.com/34371599", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Like Madden", "line": "Young nigga sendin’ them blitz out just like Madden", "vault_lines": ["Young nigga sendin' them blitz out just like Madden"], "meaning": "John Earl Madden was an American football coach and sports commentator in the National Football League (NFL). Born on April 10, 1936 and died on December 28, 2021 He served as the head coach of the Oakland Raiders from 1969 to 1978.", "annotation_id": "31642297", "url": "https://genius.com/31642297", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Like Madden", "line": "Maybach, back of the Cull’, huh", "vault_lines": ["Maybach, back of the Cull', huh"], "meaning": "NBA is mentioning the Maybach a German luxury car brand, partly owned by the Mercedes Benz AG.\nHe further mentions “Cull'” which is a shortcut for “Cullinan” as in Rolls Royce Cullinan which is an all season luxury SUV.", "annotation_id": "31589008", "url": "https://genius.com/31589008", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
