{"type": "song", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lo", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Youngboy-never-broke-again-lo-lyrics", "genius_title": "Lo", "genius_id": 12183598, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Load Up (Demon Baby)", "line": "Crated-to-the-grave you, nigga (Nigga) Let’s see if God gon’ save you, nigga (Nigga)", "vault_lines": ["Crated-to-the-grave you, nigga (Nigga)", "Let's see if God gon' save you, nigga (Nigga)"], "meaning": "In the context of that YoungBoy Never Broke Again line, “crated to the grave” means putting an enemy in a coffin and killing them.\n\nHere is the breakdown of the street and rap slang being used in those lines:\n\n“Crated”: This is a slang term for a casket, coffin, or wooden box used for burial. To “crate” someone means to put them in that box.\n\n“Let’s see if God gon' save you”: This is a direct, aggressive challenge to his rival. He is saying that once his crew targets them, only divine intervention could possibly keep them alive.\n\nEssentially, it is a classic, aggressive YoungBoy bar about street violence, meaning: “I am going to put you in a coffin and send you to the graveyard; let’s see if God steps in to stop it.” – Gemini AI", "annotation_id": "40654780", "url": "https://genius.com/40654780", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Load Up (Demon Baby)", "line": "Got four lil’ boys, I live for them", "vault_lines": ["Got four lil' boys, I live for them (I live for them)"], "meaning": "NBA YoungBoy is referring to his four sons, whom he has fathered with different women. He has been open about his experiences as a young father and has often referenced his children in his music and his primary motivation and purpose in life is to provide for and take care of his children. He is implying that his love and responsibility for his sons drive him to work hard and make a better life for himself and his family. This also conveys a sense of devotion and sacrifice, as he is willing to put his children’s needs above his own.", "annotation_id": "32174827", "url": "https://genius.com/32174827", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Load Up (Demon Baby)", "line": "You 4KTrey, we kill for you (We kill) She ain’t gangster, still ain’t doin’ shit for her", "vault_lines": ["Still ain't doin' shit for her"], "meaning": "“You 4KTrey, we kill for you”. This line suggests that the speaker and their group are fiercely loyal to 4KTrey. The phrase “we kill for you” is a metaphorical expression of their dedication and willingness to go to great lengths to support and protect 4KTrey. “you ain’t gang, still ain’t doing shit for her”. This line seems to be addressing someone who claims to be part of the group (gang) but is not genuinely contributing or showing loyalty. The phrase “still ain’t doing shit for her” implies that despite this person’s lack of commitment, they are not even making an effort to help or support a specific female figure, possibly a loved one or someone important to the group. The tone is critical and accusatory, suggesting that the speaker is disappointed and frustrated with this individual’s lack of action.", "annotation_id": "32174784", "url": "https://genius.com/32174784", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Load Up (Demon Baby)", "line": "‘Cause we gon’ hunt him down and leave him dead in the town", "vault_lines": ["'Cause we gon' hunt him down and leave him dead in the town (Dead in the town)"], "meaning": "The context of this line suggests that the speaker and their associates are seeking revenge against someone who has betrayed them by revealing information. The phrase is used to convey a sense of vengeance and violence, implying that they will track down the person who betrayed them and kill them in the town.", "annotation_id": "32174736", "url": "https://genius.com/32174736", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Load Up (Demon Baby)", "line": "You thinkin’ that’s gon’ help get you attempt wrong", "vault_lines": ["You thinkin' that's gon' help get you attempt wrong (Attempt wrong)"], "meaning": "suggests a sense of protection or invincibility associated with having a Teflon-coated object. The use of “Teflon” in this context likely refers to the Teflon coating known for its non-stick and heat-resistant properties. The implication is that the individual believes that obtaining a Teflon-coated item will provide them with a form of protection or advantage in a certain situation.", "annotation_id": "32174732", "url": "https://genius.com/32174732", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Load Up (Demon Baby)", "line": "Live or be killed, in other words, kill or get stepped on", "vault_lines": ["Live or be killed, in other words, kill or get stepped on (Stepped on)"], "meaning": "This reflect’s a stark and intense perception of survival and competition.", "annotation_id": "32174722", "url": "https://genius.com/32174722", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Load Up (Demon Baby)", "line": "We heard these niggas had told somethin’, like, “Who knowin’ somethin’?”", "vault_lines": ["We heard these niggas had told somethin', like, \"Who knowin' somethin'?\""], "meaning": "These lines suggest the speaker and his group are seeking retribution against someone they believe has provided information (“told somethin'”) about their activities. They threaten to track down and kill this person.", "annotation_id": "32174671", "url": "https://genius.com/32174671", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Load Up (Demon Baby)", "line": "These niggas ain’t on nothin’, we gon’ load up", "vault_lines": ["These niggas ain't on nothin', we gon' load up"], "meaning": "These lines depict the speaker and his group arming themselves with guns (“pipes”) and preparing to attack and destroy the property (“block”) of their perceived enemies.", "annotation_id": "32174662", "url": "https://genius.com/32174662", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
