{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "I’m just a lonely child Who wants someone to help him out, oh, oh, ah, ah Take this pain away, this pain away Because my head been runnin’ wild, wild I’m just a lonely child Who need someone to help him out, oh, oh, ah, ah Take this pain away, my pain away Because my thoughts been runnin’ wild", "vault_lines": ["I'm just a lonely child", "Who wants someone to help him out, oh, oh, ah, ah"], "meaning": "YoungBoy is basically calling out for help because the pain he’s going through is more than he can handle.", "annotation_id": "35113761", "url": "https://genius.com/35113761", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "Feelin", "vault_lines": ["Right now my candle burning wax, I'm feelin' like it's burnin' me"], "meaning": "He expresses his love for yaya and how she didn’t make him feel basic while another girl he trusted did him wrong\n\nhe also talks about how he misses his father whose in jail calling a man who raised him his father and another his mom.\n\nHe expresses how his grandpa is getting older and once he dies, he won’t have anyone. He also prays that his deceased grandmother keeps him strong as he watches over him.\n\nhe also tells us how he can’t leave the house because he’s on house arrest, he also says he wants to die and that his son will be okay because he has a lot of money.\n\nhe also says how he hopes his music helps people that grew up like him and hopes they grow out the hood.\n\nYoungBoy also talks about how girls come around for the fact he has money and how they don’t like him for his music or him.\n\nlastly YoungBoy talks about how he’s going to protect his brother regardless of the consequences because hell rather go to jail knowing that his brother is living rather than dead, and he didn’t attempt to do anything to prevent it.", "annotation_id": "35113571", "url": "https://genius.com/35113571", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "”", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "He goes onto explain his friend got killed at the young age of 16, YoungBoy says he was just a kid too young to be experiencing what he did.\n\nYoungBoy says he never knew how to fight but had to just do it because he is a man and has to hold his own.\n\nHe goes to talk about his love for a girl and how they grew apart. He also goes into saying how he goes to therapy because he can’t handle his thought steadily overthinking.\n\nhe also talks about how he can’t live without the girl and that with the fame he got he lost loved ones often going into the studio without anything written but using his pain to create music.", "annotation_id": "35113336", "url": "https://genius.com/35113336", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "The way I came in the game The image that I had put out They wouldn’t expect me to have feelings Know it probably don’t seem like it That’s why they talk about me like I ain’t human, but we all is But I’m still bein’ me I’m still in the streets and I’m still thuggin’ until them niggas put me under, yeah That’s how we livin’ and that’s how we goin’ out, you hear me? Open your mouth", "vault_lines": ["I'm still in the streets and I'm still thuggin' until them niggas put me under, yeah", "That's how we livin' and that's how we goin' out, you hear me? Open your mouth"], "meaning": "YoungBoy is explaining the way he entered the rap game and music industry; he expresses that theyy judge him off of his past. He is also saying the way they speak about him the way they talk is that he doesn’t have feelings\n\nHe says they talk to him like he has no feelings by speaking about him based on his past and not the music he makes also saying that they’re going to do it regardless\n\nhe also saying he isn’t going to change and that’s the way he wants to die being himself", "annotation_id": "35112909", "url": "https://genius.com/35112909", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "Happiness I’m chasin’, while killers behind me tryna blank me", "vault_lines": ["Happiness I'm chasin', while killers behind me tryna blank me"], "meaning": "Youngboy wants to be happy, but he has people trying to murder him.", "annotation_id": "28984764", "url": "https://genius.com/28984764", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "Go in with no pen and pad, I got this shit right on my sleeve", "vault_lines": ["Go in with no pen and pad, I got this shit right on my sleeve"], "meaning": "Youngboy is saying that he wears his heart on his sleeve, and he doesn’t need to write his lyrics because he spits straight from his heart.", "annotation_id": "28906896", "url": "https://genius.com/28906896", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "I never knew this fame would take the ones I love from ’way from me", "vault_lines": ["I never knew this fame would take the ones I love from 'way from me"], "meaning": "After Youngboy became famous he continued to lose his friends to gun violence.\n\nIt can also be inferred due to the next line that he may be referring to fame causing him to lose significant others such as Jania Meshell, the mother of his child “Kacey”", "annotation_id": "28906887", "url": "https://genius.com/28906887", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "I cannot barely, can barely sleep or even breathe I cannot hold on without you on side of me", "vault_lines": ["I cannot barely, can barely sleep or even breathe", "I cannot hold on without you on side of me"], "meaning": "Youngboy is struggling to do basic human functions, either due to thinking about his lost loved ones, or needing a significant other near him.", "annotation_id": "28906881", "url": "https://genius.com/28906881", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "I pay for therapy because my thoughts ahead of me They keep on draggin’ me, I play for keeps, they scared of me", "vault_lines": ["I pay for therapy because my thoughts ahead of me", "They keep on draggin' me, I play for keeps, they scared of me"], "meaning": "Youngboy is saying he’s paying for therapy to try and regain control of his mind because he can’t control his thoughts.\n\nHe’s saying his thoughts are dragging him along and making him do things he doesn’t actually want to do.", "annotation_id": "28906869", "url": "https://genius.com/28906869", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "Mind in a rage, I’m way too young to feel this pain I ain’t know how to fade, but I dove in ’cause I’m a man", "vault_lines": ["Mind in a rage, I'm way too young to feel this pain", "I ain't know how to fade, but I dove in 'cause I'm a man"], "meaning": "Youngboy is angry because of his friends death and other problems that he’s faced in his life.\n\nThis made him lash out and get into fights despite not really knowing how to.", "annotation_id": "28906854", "url": "https://genius.com/28906854", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "I ain’t know my age, he was sixteen, they killed", "vault_lines": ["I ain't know my age, he was sixteen, they killed Lil Dave"], "meaning": "Trauma often blurs the lines in your head and can make you forget certain details.\n\nHere Youngboy is saying he doesn’t even know what age he was when Lil Dave was killed.", "annotation_id": "28906848", "url": "https://genius.com/28906848", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "I got ice burned where my heart at", "vault_lines": ["I got ice burned where my heart at"], "meaning": "Youngboy’s heart has been extremely cold for so long that it’s become ice burned.", "annotation_id": "28906839", "url": "https://genius.com/28906839", "state": "pending", "votes": -7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "Right now my candle burning wax, I’m feelin’ like it’s burnin’ me", "vault_lines": ["Right now my candle burning wax, I'm feelin' like it's burnin' me"], "meaning": "When people say your candle is burning bright, it means your future is looking bright.\n\nIn this line Youngboy is making reference to that phrase but in his case his candle is dripping candle wax “burning wax” which indicates that it is in progress of dying out. This is how NBA Youngboy feels about his career or future, could be because all of the cases he was facing or other things hindering his growth and this wax is burning him, so this is literally affecting him emotionally and or physically.", "annotation_id": "24189595", "url": "https://genius.com/24189595", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "Lil Dave", "vault_lines": ["I ain't know my age, he was sixteen, they killed Lil Dave"], "meaning": "One of Youngboy’s closest childhood friends, was tragically murdered at just 16 years old.", "annotation_id": "22979798", "url": "https://genius.com/22979798", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "I fell in love with Kaylyn, without even knowin’ this bitch done snaked me", "vault_lines": ["I fell in love with Kaylyn, without even knowin' this bitch done snaked me"], "meaning": "This line is referring to YoungBoy’s ex-girlfriend, Kaylyn Marie. They broke up not too long after he was released from prison in September 2019.", "annotation_id": "22090184", "url": "https://genius.com/22090184", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "I’m missin’ Yaya daily, the one who don’t make me feel basic", "vault_lines": ["I'm missin' Yaya daily, the one who don't make me feel basic"], "meaning": "Yaya or Iyanna mayweather is Floyd mayweathers Eldest daughter and Youngboys expectng girlfriend", "annotation_id": "21297045", "url": "https://genius.com/21297045", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "I call Monique my mama, but Lord knows I need Sheronda", "vault_lines": ["I call Monique my mama, but Lord knows I need Sheronda"], "meaning": "After the death of his grandmother, Youngboy moved to the house of his childhood friend, he is known under the name NBA 3Three. 3Three mother, named Monique, cared about YoungBoy. Here Youngboy talks about how he calls Monique his mother, but he needs his biological mother, Sheronda.", "annotation_id": "19533620", "url": "https://genius.com/19533620", "state": "pending", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "I love that girl to death, as we get old, our feelings change", "vault_lines": ["I love that girl to death, as we get old, our feelings change"], "meaning": "As the father of 4 children by 3 different mothers, Youngboy’s romantic interests have already changed multiple times despite his youth. Although he mentions no one by name, it’s quite likely this line is a reference to his tumultuous relationship with Jania Jackson.\n\nIn February of 2018, TMZ obtained the following footage of a physical altercation between Youngboy and Jackson at a hotel in Waycross, Georgia:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ILgRZP8AlXw\n\nDespite the footage, Jackson insisted she and Youngboy were “just roughhousing” —even though authorities found blood inside Jackson’s hotel room.", "annotation_id": "18522119", "url": "https://genius.com/18522119", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "I wish that I can hear Dump say, “What up, lil’ brother?” one more time", "vault_lines": ["I wish that I can hear Dump say, \"What up, lil' brother?\" one more time"], "meaning": "NBA YoungBoy’s homie, Dump, was gunned down in a drive-by shooting that took place in Baton Rouge on Friday, May 4. Since then, YB has referenced him in many tracks and even immortalized him naming a song after him on his 2018 Album 4Respect 4Freedom 4Loyalty 4WhatImportant “R.I.P. Dump”", "annotation_id": "18386992", "url": "https://genius.com/18386992", "state": "pending", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "I wanna see Kacey bad, but I can’t seem to call Nene", "vault_lines": ["I wanna see Kacey bad, but I can't seem to call Nene"], "meaning": "YoungBoy refers to his son Kacey Alexander Gaulden, and his ex-girlfriend Jania Binia. Both Kacey and Jania have been key parts of YoungBoy’s life and his delivery of music since 2018.\n\nYoungBoy has name dropped both Jania and Kacey on songs since mid 2018. The first time YoungBoy name drops Jania is on his song “Drawing Symbols” where he says:\n\nHe got one tatted by his eye, it symbolizes Nene\n\nYoungBoy has only name dropped Kacey once before. He first name dropped Kacey in the song “4 Sons of a King” where he says:\n\nJust talked to Kacey through a iPhone, I coulda cried\n\nIt’s also worth noting that Jania has spoken about YoungBoy seeing his son Kacey. In an Instagram live video Jania said that YoungBoy is allowed to see Kacey whenever he wants.", "annotation_id": "18356116", "url": "https://genius.com/18356116", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "I miss my fuckin’ daddy, I’ve been callin’ Montana my father", "vault_lines": ["I miss my fuckin' daddy, I've been callin' Montana my father"], "meaning": "In this line YoungBoy is referring to his manager, Montana, as being his father figure.\n\n\n\nMontana is a 31 year man from Baton, Rouge Louisiana, growing up near the same area as YoungBoy. YoungBoy sees Montana as a father figure since his biological father is serving 55 years in prison for robbery and since Montana has done every thing for him to make him successful.\n\nIt’s also worth noting that Montana helped with the intro to YoungBoy’s song “War With Us” where he says:\n\nCity kinda fucked up right now\nI know pops\nMurder after murder\nBack to back\nKnow who run that motherfuckin' gang nigga\nAin’t none of my niggas crash\nAnd that’s something you don’t too motherfuckin' top nigga\nMontana, I'ma stand on that", "annotation_id": "18340533", "url": "https://genius.com/18340533", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Lonely Child", "line": "Dmac on the fuckin’ track", "vault_lines": ["Dmac on the fuckin' track"], "meaning": "This is the official producer tag for David McDowell, otherwise, known as Dmac.\n\nDmac has produced for many artists such as Dave East, BlocBoy JB, and TrenchMobb.\n\nDmac’s most popular tracks are, “No Stylist” by Dave East, “Left Right” by BlocBoy JB, and this track.", "annotation_id": "18216606", "url": "https://genius.com/18216606", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
