{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Long RD", "line": "Who coming straight up out the bayou?", "vault_lines": ["Who coming straight up out the bayou?"], "meaning": "Yb is from Baton Rouge, Louisiana, U.S. Kentrell DeSean Gaulden or also a place known as the (bayou – in the southern US) a marshy outlet of a lake or river.)", "annotation_id": "22470999", "url": "https://genius.com/22470999", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Long RD", "line": "Say, “YoungBoy, after all, can you tell me why them people chose you?” I really don’t know, fool How the fuck did they find a young nigga who thuggi", "vault_lines": ["Say, \"YoungBoy, after all, can you tell me why them people chose you?\"", "I really don't know, fool"], "meaning": "“I don’t think they really target, but if you got a name, they know who you is,” he told the hip-hop publication. “You do something, they gonna come get you, and whoever you’re with and whatever they do, you’re accountable for it just because you got the biggest name. That’s how that shit go.”  YB said back in November of 2016 arrested before his show in Austin, Texas.", "annotation_id": "22470949", "url": "https://genius.com/22470949", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Long RD", "line": "Since sixteen, young nigga been rich Nigga just turned twenty, still havin’ this shit", "vault_lines": ["Since sixteen, young nigga been rich", "Nigga just turned twenty, still havin' this shit"], "meaning": "YG started his rapping career at 15.  YoungBoy put pen to pad and founded a rap career based off of his troubled life. These early musings would become the basis for what is now his well-known 2015 debut mixtape, Life Before Fame.  since then YB has made countless Hit songs. YB also turned 20 last year October 20.", "annotation_id": "22470917", "url": "https://genius.com/22470917", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Long RD", "line": "Screamin’, “Fuck all that love,” steady runnin’ it up Let her get me caught up, I’ll never let her", "vault_lines": ["Let her get me caught up, I'll never let her"], "meaning": "What Nba portrays in these and what you can hear in his other songs that he is “done with love” and onto focusing on bigger things. The girl here “caught him up” this can mean many things but since he never said anything about her breaking his heart she probably “attempted” but he realized and said' “I’ll never let her”", "annotation_id": "22466234", "url": "https://genius.com/22466234", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
