{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Love Is Poison", "line": "Took my shit and ran with it (Ran with it)", "vault_lines": ["I gave my heart to you, you took my shit and ran with it (Ran with it)"], "meaning": "Took my shit and ran with it means he gave her his heart he gave her love she ran off and left him heartless", "annotation_id": "21393237", "url": "https://genius.com/21393237", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Love Is Poison", "line": "Don’t need no gun ’cause when I’m with you, you my heavy metal (Heavy metal) I hope you never leave my side, separate not ever (On God)", "vault_lines": ["Don't need no gun 'cause when I'm with you, you my heavy metal (Heavy metal)", "I hope you never leave my side, separate not ever (On God)"], "meaning": "In the line, YB uses a play-on-words and the metaphor of a gun to exclaim his deep connection to his partner. the phrase “heavy metal” typically denotes a subgenre of Rock and Roll characterized by highly amplified distortion, extended guitar solos, emphatic beats, and overall loudness. this is YB’s clever way of saying that she is his rock.\n\nHe later continues the same metaphor to show his deep personal affection for his partner stating that he’d rather keep her at his side than a gun.", "annotation_id": "19714215", "url": "https://genius.com/19714215", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
