{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Make No Sense", "line": "I feel like I’m Gucci Mane in 2006", "vault_lines": ["I feel like I'm Gucci Mane in 2006"], "meaning": "Back in 2006, the then 26 year old rapper Gucci Mane was beginning to take off in his music career. He also was running into a lot of trouble with the law, as he was charged with first degree murder in 2005. Gucci Mane turned himself in claiming that he shot the victim in self defense.\n\nHis debut album Trap House was released as he posted a $100,000 dollar bail.\n\n\n\nBy 2006 the murder charges against Gucci Mane were dropped and Gucci could focus on his music career.", "annotation_id": "19048744", "url": "https://genius.com/19048744", "state": "accepted", "votes": 151, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Make No Sense", "line": "He a million dollar nigga but be posted in the bricks, uh", "vault_lines": ["He a million dollar nigga but be posted in the bricks, uh"], "meaning": "Here Youngboy is referring to his own wealth with current estimates of his net worth to be $4.5 Million but he’s humbled himself to still be living in “the bricks,” the ‘hood’ or a dangerous part of city.", "annotation_id": "18514758", "url": "https://genius.com/18514758", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Make No Sense", "line": "All these diamonds dancing on my fucking neck cost like four bricks", "vault_lines": ["All these diamonds dancing on my fucking neck cost like four bricks"], "meaning": "A “brick” is a slang term for a brick of cocaine typically weighing 1 kilogram. In YoungBoy’s hometown of Baton Rouge, bricks can go anywhere from $17,000 to $30,000. Therefore, YoungBoy is boasting that the chains on his neck amount to around $100,000.", "annotation_id": "18253306", "url": "https://genius.com/18253306", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Make No Sense", "line": "Buddah Bless this beat", "vault_lines": ["Buddah Bless this beat"], "meaning": "This is the official producer tag for Atlanta-native producer, Buddah Bless. This song marks the first collaborative effort between both of the artists.\n\nBuddah Bless' most notable tracks are “Call Casting” by the Migos and “Modern Slavery” by Quavo and Travis Scott.", "annotation_id": "17562673", "url": "https://genius.com/17562673", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
