{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Murda", "line": "Like Cleo, it’s 1400/800 gang, bitch we set it off", "vault_lines": ["Like Cleo, it's 1400/800 gang, bitch we set it off"], "meaning": "“1400“ is the term Trippie uses to describe him and his friends. He explained the meaning behind the number in an interview with Power 106 Los Angeles, stating:\n\nIt’s my game. We don’t use it in a gang-related fashion, because we better than that now. But still, it is what it is.", "annotation_id": "19694976", "url": "https://genius.com/19694976", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Murda", "line": "Hit you with the Smith and Wesson", "vault_lines": ["Hit you with the Smith and Wesson, or beat your ass like Tekken"], "meaning": "Smith and Wesson is an American arms manufacturer best-known for revolvers and other handguns. Commonly referenced throughout the rap culture, the company has made a name for itself, being one of the best gun companies in the world.", "annotation_id": "19694896", "url": "https://genius.com/19694896", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Murda", "line": "Or beat your ass like Tekken", "vault_lines": ["Hit you with the Smith and Wesson, or beat your ass like Tekken"], "meaning": "Tekken is a series of Japanese fighting games, first released in 1994. Trippie likens himself to a character from the game.", "annotation_id": "19420699", "url": "https://genius.com/19420699", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Murda", "line": "187 we be wildin’, all I know is redrum", "vault_lines": ["187 we be wildin', all I know is redrum"], "meaning": "187 is the police radio code for murder.\n\nThe word “redrum“ backwards is murder, and the term was popularized in Stephen King’s The Shining\n\n\n\nYoungboy has previously mentioned redrum in multiple songs, and even went so far as to name his 2017 track under the same name.", "annotation_id": "19420690", "url": "https://genius.com/19420690", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Murda", "line": "Better live your fuckin’ best life, Lil Duval", "vault_lines": ["Better live your fuckin' best life, Lil Duval"], "meaning": "Lil Duval is a stand-up comedian who created the song called, “Smile Bitch”, featuring Snoop Dogg & Ball Greezy. The chorus repeats:\n\nI’m living my best life, I ain’t goin' back and forth with you niggas", "annotation_id": "15453890", "url": "https://genius.com/15453890", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
