{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Murder", "line": "So you know we flexin’ with them bands Whole lotta more up in my pants Try to take it all you hear is bang Try to take it all you hear is bang", "vault_lines": ["So you know we flexin' with them bands", "Whole lotta more up in my pants", "Try to take it all you hear is bang"], "meaning": "The lyrics express a sense of confidence and pride in having a large amount of money (“bands”) and possessions (“more up in my pants”).\n\nThe line “Try to take it all you hear is bang” implies a warning or threat of violence if someone attempts to take away the speaker’s wealth or belongings.\n\nThe context of the song suggests a tough and assertive attitude towards potential threats or challenges to the speaker’s material wealth.", "annotation_id": "29010813", "url": "https://genius.com/29010813", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Murder", "line": "Gon’ be a murder, if you thinkin’ ‘bout takin’ somethin’ from me Talk up out your body, but I bet you ain’t gon’ play with me", "vault_lines": ["Gon' be a murder, if you thinkin' 'bout takin' somethin' from me"], "meaning": "The lyrics suggest a warning or threat of violence if someone tries to take something from the speaker. The mention of talking about one’s body implies that the speaker is confident and not to be taken lightly. The context of YoungBoy Never Broke Again’s song “Murder” indicates a tough and assertive attitude towards potential threats or challenges.", "annotation_id": "29010803", "url": "https://genius.com/29010803", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
