{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "My Window", "line": "Out that N-O, and I don’t look out my window ’Cause all I see is the shitshow", "vault_lines": ["Out that N-O, and I don't look out my window", "'Cause all I see is the shitshow"], "meaning": "Out that N-O, he’s saying he’s out New Orleans and he don’t look outside his window because all he see is killing, robbing, and more bad behaviors around New Orleans", "annotation_id": "35574602", "url": "https://genius.com/35574602", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "My Window", "line": "Who’s that peekin’ in my motherfuckin’ window?", "vault_lines": ["Who's that peekin' in my motherfuckin' window?"], "meaning": "This lyric is a reference to Goodie Mob’s 1995 song “Cell Therapy.” Wayne interpolated the line on his 2020’s “Wayne’s World” and Talib Kweli and Z-Trip’s 2013 song “Celebrate.”", "annotation_id": "20817372", "url": "https://genius.com/20817372", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "My Window", "line": "Lit ’em up, roll windows up, the window wipers off", "vault_lines": ["Lit 'em up, roll windows up, the window wipers off"], "meaning": "The first part of the line continues with the previous lines about performing a drive-by.\n\nWhen Wayne says “the window wipers off,” he means he has clear vision. This could mean that he sees clearly so that he was able to aim well in the drive-by. It could also be a metaphor for his clarity of mind (he “sees things clearly” in general).", "annotation_id": "20793162", "url": "https://genius.com/20793162", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "My Window", "line": "I work the TEC like Window Microsoft, my windows on defrost", "vault_lines": ["I work the TEC like Window Microsoft, my windows on defrost"], "meaning": "Wayne uses a TEC, which is a TEC-9, and is pronounced like “tech”, which means technology, of which Microsoft Windows is a prime example.\n\nIn the second part of the line, Wayne is saying his windows are on defrost because he is so cold that he freezes his car.", "annotation_id": "20793113", "url": "https://genius.com/20793113", "state": "pending", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
