{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "NEXT", "line": "I think I’m Jason, the mask on, erase him", "vault_lines": ["I think I'm Jason, the mask on, erase him"], "meaning": "Jason Voorhees is a fictional horror film character from the Friday the 13th film franchise; Jason acts as the main antagonist in the film series as he’s a serial killer responsible for the deaths of numerous innocent lives.\n\nYoungBoy in particular mentions Jason’s signature mask — a goaltender hockey mask that has blood stains and dents to emphasize the severity and danger surrounding the masked serial killer. Comparing himself to Jason, YoungBoy notes that if provoked, he is not afraid to act as if he’s Jason.\n\nHowever, YoungBoy could’ve intended to use a double entendre as his in-house engineer and producer Jason “Cheese” Goldberg is normally responsible for the recording of all his tracks — in this case, it’s otherwise, YoungBoy recorded himself.\n\n\n\nPictured: Jason Voorhees in Jason Goes to Hell: The Final Friday (1993)", "annotation_id": "27925419", "url": "https://genius.com/27925419", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
