{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Nevada", "line": "Don’t know who I want, you the one I want", "vault_lines": ["Don't know who I want, you the one I want, oh"], "meaning": "YoungBoy is talking about the emotional pull of a relationship between jania (yb ex) after they broke up. The line shows him feeling conflicted—he says he’s unsure about everything else in his life, but when it comes to the person he’s thinking about, he still feels drawn to them. It reflects the complicated, on-and-off nature of a relationship he once cared about deeply, even if things ended or became strained.", "annotation_id": "37775328", "url": "https://genius.com/37775328", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Nevada", "line": "Niggas dyin’, fallin’ stars through the night", "vault_lines": ["Niggas dyin', fallin' stars through the night"], "meaning": "YoungBoy has had a lot of his friends die. In the intro he compares his fallen comrades to falling stars, which are dead stars. In the military it is usual to use the phrase “fallen” to describe a soldier who has passed in honor, YoungBoy compares his “niggas” to these soldiers.", "annotation_id": "37356881", "url": "https://genius.com/37356881", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
