{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Nevada", "line": "Choppers in the trunk, baby, this that slime tune", "vault_lines": ["Choppеrs in the trunk, baby, this that slime tune"], "meaning": "YoungBoy created his own gangsta genre, with a particular, acoustic bass heavy type of beats and “violent” lyrics, so he’s saying that his rifles sound like his own Slimey tunes.", "annotation_id": "24592800", "url": "https://genius.com/24592800", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Nevada", "line": "And you probably find my heart somewhere lost in Nevada (In Nevada)", "vault_lines": ["And you probably find my heart somewhere lost in Nevada (In Nevada)"], "meaning": "Nevada is home to the entertainment filled city, Las Vegas. Youngboy refers to how thousands of people travel to Vegas after heartbreak, or to celebrate events. The city is known for making many people depressed/sad after spending a lot on gambling, or just activities on the strip.", "annotation_id": "24267749", "url": "https://genius.com/24267749", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Nevada", "line": "If you turn me down, tell the truth, I just might spazz (Spazz)", "vault_lines": ["If you turn me down, tell the truth, I just might spazz (Spazz)"], "meaning": "Youngboy is saying that if he is rejected he might get upset or “spazz”. He is one of the most popular and most listened to young artists in the world, and probably isn’t used to being told no.", "annotation_id": "23648196", "url": "https://genius.com/23648196", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Nevada", "line": "I can’t hold you right now, so I been holdin’ on my tool", "vault_lines": ["I can't hold you right now, so I been holdin' on my tool"], "meaning": "Youngboy could be talking about a number of different people in this song, whether it is some of his ex lovers/babymoms or even some of his late friends he has lost to gun violence (Big Dump, Dave etc). Whoever this line is directed at, he is saying that it is sad he cannot hold them, so instead he is holding onto his weapon. This is unfortunately the reason why Youngboy is facing some legal troubles right now, and is fighting a federal firearms charge.", "annotation_id": "23648170", "url": "https://genius.com/23648170", "state": "pending", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Nevada", "line": "Ballin’ like a baller blocker", "vault_lines": ["Ballin' like a baller blocker"], "meaning": "Could be a reference to the 2000 film Baller Blockin' that sets in New Orleans.\n\nBirdman and Lil Wayne also appeared in the film.", "annotation_id": "23309807", "url": "https://genius.com/23309807", "state": "pending", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
