{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "No Sleep", "line": "I don’t know who the fuck I am or what I’m doin’", "vault_lines": ["I don't know who the fuck I am or what I'm doin'"], "meaning": "Ever since being released from prison on the 26th of October 2021 on bond NBA youngboy  hasn’t been feeling like himself , questioning his feelings and emotions as well as contemplating his persona… sometimes he’d feel like a rockstar and sometimes a gangster", "annotation_id": "29337641", "url": "https://genius.com/29337641", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "No Sleep", "line": "Fallin’ in love, that was my biggest mistake and I wish that it never came ’round", "vault_lines": ["Fallin' in love, that was my biggest mistake and I wish that it never came 'round"], "meaning": "He’s just like me fr😂", "annotation_id": "28508299", "url": "https://genius.com/28508299", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "No Sleep", "line": "No clues, young fool, sittin’ in front the T.V. see my daddy on the news", "vault_lines": ["No clues, young fool, sittin' in front the T.V. see my daddy on the news"], "meaning": "While YoungBoy reminisces on his childhood throughout the song, he dates back to December 2009 – where his father, Jeffery Staden, was sentenced to prison.\n\nStaden was accused of being an alleged assailant in an 2009 armed robbery case before he was sentenced to fifty-five years in prison. YoungBoy previously rapped about his father’s case in his April 2016 track “Cross Me,” exclaiming:\n\nOn my heart, that’s on my soul, I won’t tell no lies\nUncle told, now, my daddy doing 55\n\nYoungBoy additionally spoke about his father’s case again in his July 2022 single “I Don’t Talk”:\n\nDaddy lost his soul inside a trial, that’s fifty-five, one long ride\n\n\n\nPictured: Jeffery Staden’s December 2009 mugshot", "annotation_id": "27430817", "url": "https://genius.com/27430817", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
