{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "No Time", "line": "Fuck who out there reppin’, tell that nigga I done won", "vault_lines": ["Fuck who out there reppin', tell that nigga I done won"], "meaning": "He talking bout Lil durk here", "annotation_id": "31115411", "url": "https://genius.com/31115411", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "No Time", "line": "In here with Jason, makin’ sure they never get rid of me", "vault_lines": ["In here with Jason, makin' sure they never get rid of me"], "meaning": "Jason “Cheese” Goldberg has been YoungBoy’s go-to producer and engineer since his October 2021 release. Goldberg has recorded, mixed, and mastered almost every album released by YoungBoy while on house arrest. In an interview with Complex, Jason spoke about the two’s relationship:\n\nI know he trusts me to express himself however he feels. Any way he wants to go, he knows he has my support, and I show it to him when we’re making music together.\n\nYoungBoy has previously rapped about Jason in several songs, noting that he’s one of his only “real” friends. He most notably spoke about Goldberg in his January 2022, “I Got This,” in which he rapped:\n\nI’m forever thanking Jason for being my friend in need\n\nFurthermore, Top hints at the music industry’s attempt to blackball him and exclude him from the industry, noting that it’s fueling him to be in the studio with Jason and continue to record to ensure that they don’t succeed. It’s worth noting that in another interview, Jason stated that “working with YoungBoy means working anywhere and working fast” due to his high output.\n\n\n\nYoungBoy and Jason in the studio during his interview with Complex", "annotation_id": "31049865", "url": "https://genius.com/31049865", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "No Time", "line": "My wife wan’ buy horses, I mistake that shit for ’Rari", "vault_lines": ["My wife wan' buy horses, I mistake that shit for 'Rari"], "meaning": "Rari- Short  form of the famous luxurious car “Ferarri” is mistaken for a horse (animal). This is because the logo of a ferrari is a horse. Also, this line demonstrates the expensive lifestyle of NBA youngboy as both are deemed expensive", "annotation_id": "31040750", "url": "https://genius.com/31040750", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "No Time", "line": "Phantom, comin’ out bigger than a lie", "vault_lines": ["Phantom comin' out bigger than a lie"], "meaning": "In the music video we can seen YB driving around in his brand new Black and Green (interior) Rolls Royce Phantom, that cost him 500 thousand dollars.", "annotation_id": "30956795", "url": "https://genius.com/30956795", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "No Time", "line": "Patek rose gold, blue face on me, LeBron James", "vault_lines": ["Patek rose gold, blue face on me, LeBron James"], "meaning": "The watch YB is talking about is Patek Philippe, one of the most luxurious watch brands.\nThe watch he is seen wearing in the video is the “Patek Philippe Nautilus Travel Time 5990/1R-001”\n\n\n\nWhich as he states, on the second hand watch market will set you back from 250-360k dollars depending on the condition and the fluctuation in the market.\n\nHe then goes on and names LeBron James, who has been seen in some of the rarest watches on the planet, meaning that their “watch game” is on the same level.", "annotation_id": "30956653", "url": "https://genius.com/30956653", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "No Time", "line": "Eight-hundred thousand dollar AP, this shit ain’t a game", "vault_lines": ["Eight-hundred thousand dollar AP, this shit ain't a game"], "meaning": "The watch YB is talking about is Audermars Piguet, one of the most luxurious watch brands, but the actual watch he owns is the “Audemars Piguet Royal Oak Double Balance Wheel Frosted Rainbow Skeleton”\n\n\n\nWhich as he states will set you back from 600-850k dollars depending on the condition and the fluctuation in the market.", "annotation_id": "30956559", "url": "https://genius.com/30956559", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
