{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Not Wrong Now", "line": "I can go to shows now Got me a new pole now, got me a new hoe now ’Bout to cop that Rolls now, living on my own now", "vault_lines": ["Got me a new pole now, got me a new hoe now"], "meaning": "Youngboy in those lines show what type of time he is on. After being in and out of legal issues he can now get what he was been wanting, turn up, and put his legal issues behind him. He is basically saying he is back on feet", "annotation_id": "27458751", "url": "https://genius.com/27458751", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Not Wrong Now", "line": "I’ma die before this Christmas, I ain’t scared, I’ma face it", "vault_lines": ["I'ma die before this Christmas, I ain't scared, I'ma face it"], "meaning": "YoungBoy has been through periods where he does not feel safe, knowing people is out for him. Him saying he will die before this Christmas is a way of telling he is aware of his unsafety, and even feels that he is ready for it to happen without being scared.", "annotation_id": "25790696", "url": "https://genius.com/25790696", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
