{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Nussie", "line": "Cosa Nostra", "vault_lines": ["Real closure, Cosa Nostra"], "meaning": "Cosa Nostra refers to the Sicilian Mafia, an organized crime society originating in Sicily in the mid-19th century, which uses “Our Thing” as its own name. It later became known in the United States as La Cosa Nostra (LCN) or the American Mafia, a network of Italian-American crime families. The organization is known for criminal activities such as drug and arms trafficking, extortion, and contract killings, all governed by a code of silence called omertà. This explains the name of his leaked song “O'MURDER” Omertà stands for extreme loyalty and no snitching", "annotation_id": "36879957", "url": "https://genius.com/36879957", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
