{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "OMurder", "line": "We gon’ do it like this (We from the roman region)", "vault_lines": ["We gon' do it like this (We from the roman region)"], "meaning": "The “Roman region” serves a dual purpose here. Geographically, it refers to central/southern Italy (Regio I: Latium et Campania), which was heavily influenced by ancient Greek colonies. Metaphorically, YoungBoy is establishing a “conqueror” mentality. By claiming they are from the Roman region, they are setting up a theme of empire-building, discipline, and historical dominance for the rest of the song.", "annotation_id": "40868383", "url": "https://genius.com/40868383", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
