{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Of Late", "line": "Told her I want a family, she got pregnant, said no", "vault_lines": ["Told her I want a family, she got pregnant, said no"], "meaning": "This line indicates that YoungBoy expressed his desire to start a family to someone, likely a romantic partner. The partner became pregnant, but then rejected the idea of having a family, saying “No.”", "annotation_id": "32175054", "url": "https://genius.com/32175054", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Of Late", "line": "The fuck I think I’m doin’? No, that ain’t gangster at all", "vault_lines": ["The fuck I think I'm doin'? No, that ain't gangster at all"], "meaning": "YoungBoy is questioning his own actions and motivations, suggesting that his desire for a family is not in line with the “gangster” image he often portrays. He seems to be grappling with the contrast between his tough exterior and his genuine emotional needs, acknowledging that wanting a family is not typically associated with the “gangster” lifestyle.", "annotation_id": "32175050", "url": "https://genius.com/32175050", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Of Late", "line": "I ain’t worth it, I don’t deserve you, you don’t deserve this", "vault_lines": ["I ain't worth it, I don't deserve you, you don't deserve this"], "meaning": "The phrase “I ain’t worth it” suggests that YoungBoy feels he lacks value or is not good enough. This sentiment is often seen in his lyrics, where he expresses feelings of inadequacy and struggles with his own self-perception. The line “I don’t deserve you” implies that YoungBoy feels he is not worthy of the person he is addressing, likely a romantic partner. This could be related to his past experiences with relationships and his tendency to reflect on them in his music.  The final part, “you don’t deserve this,” indicates that YoungBoy believes the other person also does not deserve the situation they are in. This could be a commentary on the difficulties and challenges they face together, or a recognition that both parties are flawed and struggling.", "annotation_id": "32175041", "url": "https://genius.com/32175041", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Of Late", "line": "Wonder why it ain’t workin’, I ain’t perfect, I ain’t perfect", "vault_lines": ["Wonder why it ain't workin', I ain't perfect, I ain't perfect"], "meaning": "He questions why things aren’t working out and acknowledges his imperfections", "annotation_id": "32174991", "url": "https://genius.com/32174991", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Of Late", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Youngboy-never-broke-again-of-late-lyrics", "genius_title": "Of Late", "genius_id": 10216503, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Off 1Tenth", "line": "Incarceration time to the system", "vault_lines": ["Incarceration time to the system, mastermind, got plenty hats (Top, uh)"], "meaning": "Youngboy is saying that he has ties to the justice system, starting back to when he was only in ninth grade. Since then, he has had many run ins with the law and is currently facing two federal firearms offenses.", "annotation_id": "22911453", "url": "https://genius.com/22911453", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
