{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Out My Mind", "line": "We leave you dead in front your house, this shit ain’t safe for me", "vault_lines": ["We leave you dead in front your house, this shit ain't safe for me (This shit ain't safe at all)"], "meaning": "Blvd Quick was a Barton Rouge Rapper affiliated with the label Top Boy Gorilla, He was also close friends with fellow rappers Fredo Bang and Gee Money. Around November 2018 he was beefing with Youngboy and his Mom on Instagram, he was found dead outside his apartment shortly after.", "annotation_id": "37423166", "url": "https://genius.com/37423166", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Out My Mind", "line": "Ridin’ ’round in a drop-top with a stolen Glock (Who is you, nigga?) Mm, huh (Don’t come close) Searchin’ for my opps Hold on, hold on", "vault_lines": ["Ridin' 'round in a drop-top with a stolen Glock (Who is you, nigga?)", "Mm, huh (Don't come close)", "Searchin' for my opps"], "meaning": "A snippet of the studio session of this section went viral on social media after it surfaced online due to YB’s seemingly obscene energy and “unpleasant” vocal performance.\n\nThis led to the meme “rappers who can sing vs rappers who can’t,” where YoungBoy is compared to artists such as Rod Wave and most popularly, beabadoobee, and is classified as someone who can sing, which is obviously sarcasm.\n\nA prime example is this YouTube video which amassed over 4 million views and 300k likes:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BnrtJGBdOWU\n\nbeabadoobee even responded to the meme herself, expressing her disagreement with being classified as one who can’t sing, especially when compared to YoungBoy:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/shorts/MzAOEJpL9gw", "annotation_id": "34691448", "url": "https://genius.com/34691448", "state": "accepted", "votes": 74, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
