{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outside Today", "line": "Wraith", "vault_lines": ["With a hundred thousand dollars up in the Wraith"], "meaning": "The Rolls-Royce Wraith is a Full-size luxury car/ Grand tourer manufactured by Rolls-Royce Motor Cars and based on the chassis of the Rolls-Royce\n\nGhost.\n\n\n\nCosts about 300k+", "annotation_id": "22693866", "url": "https://genius.com/22693866", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outside Today", "line": "Got a TEC and a chopper", "vault_lines": ["Got a TEC and a chopper"], "meaning": "A TEC is a variant of a sub machine gun, and a chopper is just referring to guns in general, he also mentions this to show that he is always protected at all times", "annotation_id": "20857372", "url": "https://genius.com/20857372", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outside Today", "line": "Couldn’t find Hi-Tec, so I’m drinkin’ on Act’ today", "vault_lines": ["Couldn't find Hi-Tec, so I'm drinkin' on Act' today"], "meaning": "Hi-Tech is a pharmaceutical company that produces promethazine with codeine cough syrup, an ingredient for lean.\n\nSince Hi-Tech is in low supply, YoungBoy relies on Actavis, another company that makes this cough syrup.", "annotation_id": "20643610", "url": "https://genius.com/20643610", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outside Today", "line": "I’ma take it to trial, pray to Lord I beat the case", "vault_lines": ["I'ma take it to trial, pray to Lord I beat the case"], "meaning": "This line, along with the previous line, could be a reference to NBA YoungBoy’s criminal history, more specifically, his two murder cases where he was eventually found not guilty.\n\nThe charges spawned the infamous “I feel like I’m Gucci Mane in 2006” line in YB’s track “Make No Sense”, which is a reference to how Gucci Mane similarly was found not guilty of murder charges.", "annotation_id": "19502948", "url": "https://genius.com/19502948", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outside Today", "line": "(DMac got me too bangin’)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is the producer tagline for producer DMacTooBangin, best known for his work with Moneybagg Yo and Lil Baby.\n\nHe has worked previously with YoungBoy on his collaborative track “Homicide” with Moneybagg Yo. This is the breakout track for DMac with it peaking at number 31 on the Billboard Hot 100.", "annotation_id": "15750254", "url": "https://genius.com/15750254", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outside Today", "line": "I just bought a brand new watch from God I ain’t put it on yet", "vault_lines": ["I just bought a brand new watch from God", "I ain't put it on yet"], "meaning": "Maison Goyard is a French luggage maker established in 1853 as Goyard although it was originally opened in 1792 under the name Martin.\n\n It is a popular reference in Hip-Hop, used by popular artists such as Kanye West, Big Sean, along with the A$AP Mob avidly repping the brand, resulting in A$AP Rocky receiving a custom Goyard trunk.", "annotation_id": "15723358", "url": "https://genius.com/15723358", "state": "accepted", "votes": -7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outside Today", "line": "I’ma pull up in style, we gon’ do a drive by in the Wraith", "vault_lines": ["I'ma pull up in style, we gon' do a drive by in the Wraith"], "meaning": "The Rolls-Royce Wraith is a British luxury car, generally costing over $350,000.\n\nThe name “Wraith” comes from an ancient Scottish word meaning image of a ghost or spirit. This long has been used as a model name for Rolls Royce with it being used originally in 1938.", "annotation_id": "15723312", "url": "https://genius.com/15723312", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outside Today", "line": "My clip full of thunder, you know that I’ll strike ’em Wanna join NBA, go and catch you a body", "vault_lines": ["My clip full of thunder, you know that I'll strike 'em", "Wanna join NBA, go and catch you a body"], "meaning": "The clip full of thunder could be a metaphor for the sound some assault rifles make when fired.\n\nThis could also be an allusion to the NBA basketball team Oklahoma City Thunder, commonly known as OKC.\n\n\n\nYoungboy also shouting out his gang ‘NBA’ which stands for “never broke again.” He implies that to be apart of his gang you must have ‘caught a body’ which could mean to kill someone or dunk on someone in basketball.", "annotation_id": "13696907", "url": "https://genius.com/13696907", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outside Today", "line": "Free Kevin Gates, it’s a murder for hire", "vault_lines": ["Free Kevin Gates, it's a murder for hire"], "meaning": "Kevin Gates was in prison and served nine months out of a 30-month sentence for a felony weapons charge. He served 6 months previously for kicking a female fan at a concert.\n\nMurder for Hire is an album by Kevin Gates.\n\nYoungBoy and Gates are close friends and have collaborated in the past. For example, they teamed up to make the song “Like Me” in 2016.", "annotation_id": "13493697", "url": "https://genius.com/13493697", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outside Today", "line": "I just got a pet monkey, cashed out on a tiger But really don’t want it, my son don’t like him", "vault_lines": ["But really don't want it, my son don't like him"], "meaning": "In late 2017, YoungBoy was gifted a pet monkey (which at one point tried to drink 21 Savage’s lean).\n\nYoungBoy also bought a pet tiger around the same time. However, on January 6, 2018, a white tiger cub thought to belong to him was seized in New Orleans after it turned up in an unpermitted area showing signs of neglect. YoungBoy appeared in an Instagram video with a similar-looking white tiger a few months earlier.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BaE9JHvHMId/", "annotation_id": "13308306", "url": "https://genius.com/13308306", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outside Today", "status": "done", "targets": 16, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Youngboy-never-broke-again-outside-today-lyrics", "genius_title": "Outside Today", "genius_id": 3314180, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outta Here Safe", "line": "You see my cup, you see my stick, both of them dirty", "vault_lines": ["You see my cup, you see my stick, both of them dirty"], "meaning": "“Dirty” is a term used to describe an object obatained by illegal or violent means (ex: dirty money). “Dirty” has a different yet fundamentally equal meaing Dirty cup is a synonym for lean; An illegal drug beverage mix of prescriptiong cough syrup with codeine, promethainze, and a soft drink.", "annotation_id": "30096784", "url": "https://genius.com/30096784", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outta Here Safe", "line": "If it’s smoke", "vault_lines": ["Like the opps gay, if it's smoke, we gotta get it straight"], "meaning": "Smoke is a term that references tension that could result in a physical altercation or a gun fight. NoCap is no stranger to this as throughout his rap journey he’s admitted to losing friends to gun violence.", "annotation_id": "30096758", "url": "https://genius.com/30096758", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outta Here Safe", "line": "Free DDawg out the system, you forever my nigga, we all been caught as victims", "vault_lines": ["Free DDawg out the system, you forever my nigga, we all been caught as victims"], "meaning": "Ddawg is Youngboy’s homie. He was finally freed in 2022 after serving 7 years. But later that year he caught a manslaughter case.", "annotation_id": "28748600", "url": "https://genius.com/28748600", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outta Here Safe", "line": "It, Timmy tryna kill an opp (Oh, oh)", "vault_lines": ["Spin it, Timmy tryna kill an opp (Oh, oh)"], "meaning": "Here Quando is referencing his friend, Lul Tim who is a known shooter and one of his affiliates in Savannah, Georgia.\n\nLul Tim infamously shot and killed rapper King Von in November 2020.", "annotation_id": "25964643", "url": "https://genius.com/25964643", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outta Here Safe", "line": "Feelin’ like Drake, I’m straight out the 6", "vault_lines": ["Feelin' like Drake, I'm straight out the 6"], "meaning": "In this line, Cap is making a reference to fellow rap Artist Drake, who hails from Toronto, which is also known as the 6. NoCap, on the other hand, is from Mobile, Alabama, where he reps the 1600 block. He shortens 1600 to just “6”, so he can make this self-comparison to Drake.\n\nCap references this block in many other songs, one of which being in “What You Know”:\n\n“Supply all the ammo to 1600 army”", "annotation_id": "22165968", "url": "https://genius.com/22165968", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Outta Here Safe", "line": "Since a young boy, I been walkin’ ’round with a .38", "vault_lines": ["Since a young boy, I been walkin' 'round with a .38"], "meaning": "Youngboy is also called the 38 baby. He released a song back in 2017 called 38 baby.  Since a “young boy”…", "annotation_id": "21816376", "url": "https://genius.com/21816376", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
