{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Preach", "line": "NBA until the end, it’s a way of life", "vault_lines": ["NBA until the end, it's a way of life"], "meaning": "We all know “NBA” stands for Never Broke Again but Youngboy isn’t the only one with NBA in his name. It was originally a group with several other members that Youngboy grew up with in Baton Rouge. One of the members is NBA Meechy which most of us probably heard of in a lot of Youngboys songs. So Youngboy is saying his group is until the end and it’s a way of life.", "annotation_id": "33632766", "url": "https://genius.com/33632766", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Preach", "line": "Young nigga fillin’ up his arm with some heroin", "vault_lines": ["Young nigga fillin' up his arm with some heroin"], "meaning": "When Youngboy says he is filling his arm up with heroin he means he is taking drugs but by the arm (with a needle)", "annotation_id": "33632751", "url": "https://genius.com/33632751", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Preach", "line": "He was abandoned as a child screamin’, “Red rum” You spell it backwards, what that mean? Nigga, murder", "vault_lines": ["He was abandoned as a child screamin', \"Red rum\"", "You spell it backwards, what that mean? Nigga, murder"], "meaning": "Reminiscing on past experiences growing up in bad conditions, YoungBoy looks back at how he has always been surrounded by violence and drugs.\n\n“Red rum” does not directly mean anything. However, in the song it is explained that it is the word “murder” backwards. This word is partially used to further develop this picture that he is portaying.\n\nSomething which many might not know thoug is that this is potentially a reference to “The Shining”. This is a classic horror film from 1980 starring Jack Nicholson, which is just like the song, depicting a gritty image. However the reference is to one specific scene where “Redrum” is written on a wall in blood.", "annotation_id": "14925903", "url": "https://genius.com/14925903", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Preach", "line": "Keandre dead, the only thing I think about is Tyler I’m full of pain but wake up every morning and I’m smilin’ They think I’m dumb, you got me fucked up, I got plenty knowledge", "vault_lines": ["Keandre dead, the only thing I think about is Tyler", "I'm full of pain but wake up every morning and I'm smilin'", "They think I'm dumb, you got me fucked up, I got plenty knowledge"], "meaning": "Even though YoungBoy is hurting on the inside from his memories of his friends dying and people switching up on him, he still smiles every day.\n\n\n\nThe hardships he has experienced sharpened his proverbial sword, giving him knowledge about life on the streets. Despite this, many people have mistaken his ghetto spirit for stupidity. For instance, Malu Trevejo called him NBA ‘dumb boy’ in this video. Part of the reason people may think he’s unintelligent is that he never graduated from high school, dropping out in the 9th grade to pursue his music career.", "annotation_id": "14436604", "url": "https://genius.com/14436604", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Preach", "line": "Get on my knee on side the bed like “Father, forgive me”", "vault_lines": ["Get on my knee on side the bed like \"Father, forgive me\""], "meaning": "When he gets on his knees, he is praying for God’s forgiveness for the crimes he has committed in the past.\n\nYBNBA has had a history of crime, such as in November 2016, when he was arrested for two counts of attempted murder when he opened fire on a group in south Baton Rouge, Louisiana, his home city.\n\nHe most recently served time from February 25-March 15, 2018, for allegedly committing assault, weapons violations and kidnapping. Hotel surveillance footage showed YoungBoy assaulting his then-girlfriend, Jania.", "annotation_id": "14645049", "url": "https://genius.com/14645049", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
