{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Proof", "line": "In my daughter eyes, I see her future, fell out of love, now I beef with Cupid", "vault_lines": ["In my daughter eyes, I see her future, fell out of love, now I beef with Cupid"], "meaning": "A bow, arrow, and quiver are the attributes of Cupid, the god of love, and his arrows are used to make two people fall in love.\n\nUltimately, in this line, NBA YoungBoy addresses his heartbroken mindset as well as not believing in love. By showing his pain, NBA YoungBoy decides to “beef” with the god of love in his mind after losing what was possibly a long-term relationship with someone.", "annotation_id": "26462613", "url": "https://genius.com/26462613", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Proof", "line": "This ain’t no façade, as a child, I had it hard, as a man, I shed tears", "vault_lines": ["This ain't no façade, as a child, I had it hard, as a man, I shed tears"], "meaning": "A façade is an exterior of a building, supposedly of a mansion. The word comes from the French, simply meaning ‘frontage’ or ‘face’.\n\n\n\nPicture: A façade of a building\n\n\nHowever, in this line, NBA YoungBoy addresses his youth lifestyle proclaiming that he grew up in a area with many gang affiliations as well as gun violence.\n\nAlthough NBA was raised around gang life, in a May 2022 track titled “See Me Now,” the music video shows the rapper posing outside—what could be—his house, sees the rappers life changed.", "annotation_id": "26462422", "url": "https://genius.com/26462422", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
