{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Proud of Myself", "line": "No, she ain’t loyal, I ain’t fallin’, no way But inside that girl, I be far away", "vault_lines": ["No, she ain't loyal, I ain't fallin', no way", "But inside that girl, I be far away"], "meaning": "Youngboy is saying that he isn’t ready to fall in love with the girl because she’s not loyal but he is willing to have a sexual relationship with her.", "annotation_id": "31685350", "url": "https://genius.com/31685350", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Proud of Myself", "line": "Look, this Alice grandson", "vault_lines": ["Look, this Alice grandson, Kentrell (Mmm-mmm-mmm-hmm-mmm-mmm, son)"], "meaning": "Alice Gaulden was Youngboy’s grandmother and caretaker as his father was (and still is) serving a 55 year prison sentence for armed robbery and his mother was in and out of his life. When Youngboy was 11, his beloved grandmother died of heart failure. This would be a turning point in his life as after this he was sent to a group home where he said he used to get beat up by older kids there and in turn he became a angry and troubled kid. In an interview with Billboard he said “I used to get beat up inside the group home for no reason, the other boys would put their hands on me, and I would look up like, ‘Why are you hitting me, bro? What’d I do?’ It made me discover another side of me that I never glorified or liked. I found out how to be the person that you don’t want to do that with. [Before then], I never understood all the evilness or wrong because I was showered by so much love from this one person.” Youngboy was very close with his grandmother and has mentioned her in several tracks and even has a portrait of her in his mansion in Utah.", "annotation_id": "28315746", "url": "https://genius.com/28315746", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Proud of Myself", "line": "He don’t even smoke K2, but I’m smokin’ this shit with twin", "vault_lines": ["He don't even smoke K2, but I'm smokin' this shit with twin"], "meaning": "“K2”—also known as “fake marijuana” and “spice,” among a variety of slang terms—is a mixture of herbs, spices or shredded plant material, typically sprayed with synthetic substances. Although these products are labelled “safe,” they impact the brain more significantly than regular marijuana.\n\nUltimately, NBA YoungBoy shows capability whilst utilizing the drug as the substance is known for altering one’s mental state. The term “twin” alludes to a friend or two objects. In his case, he’s most likely along with a companion whilst he smokes the substance.\n\n\n\nPictured: K2 or “spice.”", "annotation_id": "26742520", "url": "https://genius.com/26742520", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Proud of Myself", "line": "Shorty, please don’t you leave, don’t you see that I’m in a two-way love affair?", "vault_lines": ["Shorty, please don't you leave, don't you see that I'm in a two-way love affair?"], "meaning": "Youngboy is referring to being in love with Jazz and being in love with Sarah Sydner( the girl he was mentioning in his song “Snow Bunny”.", "annotation_id": "25995101", "url": "https://genius.com/25995101", "state": "pending", "votes": -2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Proud of Myself", "line": "Stay off the ‘Gram, not makin’ friends and she fuck with that", "vault_lines": ["Stay off the 'Gram, not makin' friends and she fuck with that"], "meaning": "On April 10, 2020, YoungBoy cleared his Instagram entirely, wiping all posts and story highlights off of it. He took to Instagram live the next day with fellow rapper Bway Yungy to explain why, saying quote:\n\nYou know why I deleted my pictures off my page? Women trying to incriminate me. Posting stupid shit. Well, they say stupid shit. […] That shit be playing mind games. Well, I be playing mind games with myself because I be letting it eat me up.\n\nAlthough it wasn’t entirely clear who he was referring to, the aforementioned “women trying to incriminate [him]” could possibly be his former girlfriend Kay Marie, who sent pictures of herself with bruises to YoungBoy fan pages amongst Instagram.\n\nFive months after this hiatus began, on September 28, 2020, a video surfaced of YoungBoy reportedly being detained by police while on the set of a music video shoot, leading him to deactivate both his Instagram and Twitter accounts.\n\nSince then, YoungBoy has only made a few social media appearances, most notably reactivating his Instagram for a short period of time and going live on it after the release of his eighteenth mixtape, Colors.\n\nHis deactivation on these platforms show that YoungBoy feels as if he doesn’t need any type of social media promotion or use in general to boost his career and would rather go about by keeping to himself.\n\nYoungBoy is also well known for not relying on anybody but himself not only in the music industry—but in general. He touched up on his independency in his May 2021 track “White Teeth,” rapping quote:\n\nNo security, bros with me, no friends\n[…]\nDon’t fuck ‘round with these niggas, go home and take my meds", "annotation_id": "25908643", "url": "https://genius.com/25908643", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Proud of Myself", "line": "I won’t get paid, ain’t no love for the game (Mmm)", "vault_lines": ["I won't get paid, ain't no love for the game (Mmm)"], "meaning": "According to DJ Akademiks, on May 17, 2022, it was announced that YoungBoy Never Broke Again turned down a $25 million record deal from his current label Atlantic Records. Here, YoungBoy could possibly be referencing his prior record deal which entitled him to $2 million for five studio albums, this is typically seen as a bad deal due to YoungBoy’s tremendous fanbase and sales rates.\n\nThroughout his career with Atlantic, YoungBoy has shown no remorse for the label as they have been seen as neglecting him and disregarding him compared to their compassion for the other artists in their roster. YB publicly spoke about the label to DJ Akademiks:\n\nThey ain’t gonna come back to me because I ain’t trying to hear s**t they got to say\n\nIn January 2022, after the release of his mixtape Colors, YoungBoy claimed that Atlantic had removed his album from the Apple Music charts which were going #1 for two concurrent weeks. He said:\n\nI was going #1 two weeks straight with a mixtape so they took it down off the charts.\n[…]\nI don’t give a f**k you still can’t stop me don’t sign to Atlantic if you an artist they not gone support you especially if you live a certain way.\n[…]\nWhy blackball me, I’m the good guy!!??\n\nYoungBoy could also be referring to a public response from certain artists in the rap industry such as Lil Baby, Gucci Mane, and NLE Choppa, who have all sided with Lil Durk in relation to Durk’s and YoungBoy’s ongoing viral feud. The low support from his label and other artists in the industry seems to be the main reason he has “no love for the game.”", "annotation_id": "25895097", "url": "https://genius.com/25895097", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
