{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Rags to Riches", "line": "Whatever I want, I go get it (I go get it) Came from rags to riches (Rags to riches) Blew up and took over my city (My city) I’m thankin’ the lord I did it (I did it) I wanted a bite, and I bit it (I bit it) I swear it ain’t hard to get it (To get it) I stay with that rod, I’m with it", "vault_lines": ["Blew up and took over my city (My city)", "I'm thankin' the lord I did it (I did it)", "I wanted a bite, and I bit it (I bit it)", "I swear it ain't hard to get it (To get it)"], "meaning": "The chorus emphasizes the artist’s mindset of going after what they want, regardless of their starting point. They express gratitude for their success, acknowledging their journey from a difficult background to achieving wealth and influence in their city. The line “I stay with that rod, I’m with it” suggests a readiness to protect oneself and maintain a certain lifestyle.", "annotation_id": "28790723", "url": "https://genius.com/28790723", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
