{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Rags to Riches", "line": "Get up, go get it if I ever want it I got some Act in my cup, and I’m loaded I pop them Perkys, you know I control it Straight off the dome, you know I ain’t wrote it Gotta tell it, swear it’s hard for to hold it Up with the Glock, and you know I’ma blow it", "vault_lines": ["Gotta tell it, swear it's hard for to hold it", "Up with the Glock, and you know I'ma blow it"], "meaning": "The first lines indicate a strong desire to go after what the artist wants and a reference to having a drink with codeine (Act) in it, expressing a state of being intoxicated. They mention taking Percocet pills, suggesting control over their actions and emotions. The line “Straight off the dome, you know I ain’t wrote it” suggests that the artist is freestyling or delivering spontaneous lyrics.", "annotation_id": "28790706", "url": "https://genius.com/28790706", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Rags to Riches", "line": "CashAP got the beat tight", "vault_lines": ["CashAP got the beat tight"], "meaning": "This line is later used in many CashMoneyAP produced songs as his producer tag. For example “From The Start” & “Race Beginning” by Juice WRLD and “Move Move” by Trippie Redd.", "annotation_id": "23968541", "url": "https://genius.com/23968541", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
