{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Rain", "line": "Please, please don’t please me Leave, please just leave me (Just leave)", "vault_lines": ["Leave, please just leave me (Just leave)"], "meaning": "He doesn’t care about himself nor feels that he deserves love. He is alone with his inner problems and struggles which he can not explain to anyone else, and thinks that it’s best to just be left as he’s went through many times.", "annotation_id": "26987155", "url": "https://genius.com/26987155", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Rain", "line": "Can you tell me if it’s storming? Don’t wanna be wrong by asking you to go Tell me if it’s raining, I don’t wanna look outside my window", "vault_lines": ["Tell me if it's raining, I don't wanna look outside my window"], "meaning": "YoungBoy feels locked out from the world and asks his lover to tell him about what’s going on outside. He want to be left alone but doesn’t want his lover to feel that’s because he don’t appreciate them, so he let’s them fill up a meaning.\n\nThe line can also indicate YoungBoy’s house arrest and how he has accepted to stay inside at all times, so much that he no longer cares what is going on in the outside world. This makes sense as he doesn’t have any social media and the conclusion can be drawn that he does not care about news or media at all, he is in his own zone.", "annotation_id": "26987131", "url": "https://genius.com/26987131", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
