{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Ranada", "line": "I was fallin’ in love with you, I ain’t take you as no dub (As no dub)", "vault_lines": ["I was fallin' in love with you, I ain't take you as no dub (I— As no dub)"], "meaning": "Dub has its origins from NYC and their slang has spread beyond their boroughs to different states. It has alternate meanings, but it can mainly be defined as ignoring something/somebody in a way to reject an action.\n\nHere, Youngboy is stating that he was falling in love with a woman and didn’t consider her as somebody to ignore for her presence.", "annotation_id": "28977933", "url": "https://genius.com/28977933", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Ranada", "line": "Oh Lord, Jetson made another one", "vault_lines": ["Oh Lord, Jetson made another one"], "meaning": "This producer tag belongs to jetsonmade\n\nTahj Morgan, also known as jetsonmade (formerly stylised as JetsonMade), is a Carolina-based producer best recognised for producing many of DaBaby’s breakout songs, including “Suge,” “BOP,” “Goin Baby,” and “VIBEZ,” among others.\n\nHe has worked with 21 Savage, Roddy Ricch, Playboi Carti, YoungBoy Never Broke Again, Lil Keed, Young Nudy, Smokepurpp, and many other musicians, and has become a go-to producer in the Hip-Hop genre.\n\n@jetsonmade", "annotation_id": "28775825", "url": "https://genius.com/28775825", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
