{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Return of Goldie", "line": "Now, I’ma tell you I’ma Mac for life, I fuck over shit", "vault_lines": ["Now, I'ma tell you I'ma Mac for life, I fuck over shit"], "meaning": "Really, it should be “Now Ima tell em I’ma Mak4Life, I fuck ova shiit” Meaning he’s gon be a Pimp for the rest of his life to his dyin days. The whole point of this song is YB saying he’s not the new 2pac or “ Makavelli” of this generation like confusing people & critics like to say say he is, Instead he feels like he should be looked at as The New Goldie who is the main character & The Pimp From the 1980’s movie “The Mack”. A pimp/mak/playa/smooth operator are all the same thing and they are people who are very good at making (multiple) women go turn tricks for money just to bring it back for them and only give them a small cut back(if any at all) and keep the rest for themselves and make em go do it again. They also indulge in various other illegal activities and cannot be trusted once so ever because they are highly likely to fuck you over at some point if you cross paths with them,💁🏾‍♂️‼️💯", "annotation_id": "37564031", "url": "https://genius.com/37564031", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Return of Goldie", "line": "Want beef with me, best have some Ks", "vault_lines": ["Want beef with me, best have some Ks"], "meaning": "Basically this nigga YB is giving advice to niggas that you should be having weapons if you want to scuffle with him", "annotation_id": "30791392", "url": "https://genius.com/30791392", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Return of Goldie", "line": "We ain’t have no friends, after the end, we breakin’ in they place, yeah", "vault_lines": ["We ain't have no friends, after the end, we breakin' in they place, yeah"], "meaning": "he saying after they stop becoming friends they rob they place", "annotation_id": "30012027", "url": "https://genius.com/30012027", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Return of Goldie", "line": "Bitch, you gon’ die inside of this yard, we gon’ drag you to your grave", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, you gon' die inside of this yard, we gon' drag you to your grave"], "meaning": "lil rye if you run in this nigga yard or any nigga in general comes in the yard of his residence . You will be killed and dragged to your grave to rot.which in the previous line he stated guards are in the front and back yard", "annotation_id": "29973699", "url": "https://genius.com/29973699", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Return of Goldie", "line": "Uh, this ain’t no return of no Makaveli, this Goldie, bitch", "vault_lines": ["Uh, this ain't no return of no Makaveli, this Goldie, bitch"], "meaning": "Makaveli is a commonly known alias for the legendary 2Pac, who YoungBoy states that he shouldn’t be compared to, instead, he should be compared to John “Goldie” Mickens, the lead character of the 1973 crime drama, The Mack.\n\nIn the film, Goldie is released from a five-year prison sentence and decided to become a pimp—a person who arranges prostitution services for the prostitutes. YoungBoy referred to other rappers taking part in “pimping” in his October 2023’s “Deep Down.”\n\nThese niggas ain’t play at all, rap niggas, they bored from pimpin'\n\nYoungBoy states that instead of returning as a great rapper, he’d rather return as a pimp as he believes it pays more and is more worth it. This isn’t the first time YoungBoy has attempted to distance himself from 2Pac’s name as in his October 2022’s “It Could Go,” YoungBoy opened the track by responding to critics who compare him to the late rapper:\n\nI ain’t no 2Pac of this generation, I’m AI YoungBoy\nYou try to get ahead of this generation, you’ll get a run for it\nGot a lot of risks inside my situation, but I was born for it", "annotation_id": "29963783", "url": "https://genius.com/29963783", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Return of Goldie", "line": "All black GNikes, shirt on my face, run out, I’m down to fold a bitch", "vault_lines": ["All black GNikes, shirt on my face, run out, I'm down to fold a bitch"], "meaning": "Usually, when committing crimes such as robbery and murder, criminals dress up in all black clothing to conceal their identity. YoungBoy claims that, this time, he is going to murder one of his enemies.", "annotation_id": "29960740", "url": "https://genius.com/29960740", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Return of Goldie", "line": "When it go down, I’m gon’ run down right where it’s heat inside this place", "vault_lines": ["When it go down, I'm gon' run down right where it's heat inside this place"], "meaning": "heat", "annotation_id": "29960476", "url": "https://genius.com/29960476", "state": "pending", "votes": -3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Return of Goldie", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Youngboy-never-broke-again-return-of-goldie-lyrics", "genius_title": "Return of Goldie", "genius_id": 9687726, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Rich As Hell", "line": "Bitch, I trap out like Griselda (Trap), hollows, I mail ’em", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I trap out like Griselda (Trap), hollows, I mail 'em"], "meaning": "NBA YoungBoy claims to have the same drug dealing skills as The Godmother. The Godmother, also known as the Queen of Cocaine, The Black Widow and by her real name, Griselda Blanco, was one of the biggest biggest cocaine traffickers and alleged murderers from Columbia.\n\nBlanco operated out of Miami, Florida and was trafficking for almost fifty years. Most seem to agree that Blanco was responsible for around 40 murders but others claim that number to be in the two hundreds.\n\n\n\nThis isn’t the first time YoungBoy has compared his trapping skills to Griselda as he has on his 2018 platinum track, “Slime Belief”:\n\nCan you make it better? Trap out like Griselda", "annotation_id": "18328362", "url": "https://genius.com/18328362", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Rich As Hell", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Youngboy-never-broke-again-rich-as-hell-lyrics", "genius_title": "Rich As Hell", "genius_id": 4933863, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Rich Junkie", "line": "[Interlude] Old bitch ass I’ve been seeing I’ve been seeing these bitch-ass niggas talkin’ ’bout, “Put it on the floor,” all on, all in they pictures Bitch-ass nigga, it’s already on head The fuck you talking ’bout, boy? It’s 4KTrey, nobody safe, gang", "vault_lines": ["I've been seeing these bitch-ass niggas talkin' 'bout, \"Put it on the floor,\" all on, all in they pictures", "Bitch-ass nigga, it's already on head"], "meaning": "Quotes same line from a song called “New New” saying\n\n\nNew New “It’s on they head, these pussy niggas talkin' ‘bout puttin’ on the floor”", "annotation_id": "36425891", "url": "https://genius.com/36425891", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
