{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Right or Wrong", "line": "Baby Joe put that Draco to his back Baby Joe put that Draco to his cap", "vault_lines": ["Baby Joe put that Draco to his back", "Baby Joe put that Draco to his cap"], "meaning": "bbg babyjoe is  one of his closest friends since they met each other in jail and stayed close ever since. They have one released song together, and as far as we know, two that are unreleased. He’s the face of bbg, but also a well known nba member and fan favorite. He was best friends with nba youngboy’s cousin boozilla (boo) before he passed while babyjoe was in jail.", "annotation_id": "21632757", "url": "https://genius.com/21632757", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Right or Wrong", "line": "Show my scars, I do not wear a hat", "vault_lines": ["Show my scars, I do not wear a hat"], "meaning": "When YoungBoy was four years old, he gruesomely broke his neck in a wrestling accident. In order to reshape his spine, doctors gave him a halo brace which left scars on his forehead, as explained in an interview with DJ Smallz Eyes 2. YoungBoy doesn’t wear hats on purpose, in an attempt to show his scars, as he is proud of them.", "annotation_id": "14465524", "url": "https://genius.com/14465524", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Right or Wrong", "line": "Got twenty chains in the vault, put a dog food to my dawg", "vault_lines": ["Got twenty chains in the vault, put a dog food to my dawg"], "meaning": "Future has never been shy to talk about his extensive collection of jewelry, mentioning his chains on songs such as “Mask Off”:\n\nRick James, thirty-three chains\n  Ocean air, cruisin' Biscayne\n\n\n\n“Dog food” is slag term which refers to the drug heroin, often thought to resemble dog food in its raw form. Future also plays off of this connection by supplying product to his “dawg” or close friend.\n\nA similar comparison is made by Young Thug on his song with Future, “Mink Flow”:\n\nAbout to feed my dogs, need pedigree, oh", "annotation_id": "14436825", "url": "https://genius.com/14436825", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
