{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Run The Hood", "line": "Behind this one nigga, he deceased", "vault_lines": ["Behind this one nigga, he deceased"], "meaning": "Another diss to King Von. This correlates to saying everyone wants him dead behind the death of Chicago Rapper “King Von”", "annotation_id": "28364793", "url": "https://genius.com/28364793", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Run The Hood", "line": "I’m on the phone with Tim, oh, that’s ****, bitch, dig your brother up Tell ‘em fuck that nigga you fucking on, they ain’t gon’ fuck with us Tell your broke-ass menace come get me gone, we gon’ bust him off", "vault_lines": ["I'm on the phone with Tim, oh, that's ****, bitch, dig your brother up", "Tell 'em fuck that nigga you fucking on, they ain't gon' fuck with us", "Tell your broke-ass menace come get me gone, we gon' bust him off"], "meaning": "Alluding to the death of the late King Von, YoungBoy notes that on the night of Von’s murder, he was on the phone with the shooter, Lul Timm, making jokes about the death of Von.\n\nOn November 6, 2020, following the album release party of Von’s debut album, Welcome To O'Block, Von was shot after being involved in an altercation with Quando Rondo, subsequently leading to Timm, Quando’s close friend, shooting Von.\n\nWhere some thought YoungBoy was mentioning Lil Durk when he rapped, “Dig your brother up,” fans slowed down and reversed the lyric, after which it was revealed YoungBoy said, “Kayla,” the name of Von’s biological sister, Kayla B. YoungBoy has mentioned Kayla several times, most particularly in his February 2022, “I Hate YoungBoy,” in which he rapped:\n\nAnd that lil' bitch, she say, “4L,” huh? I say, “Heads or tails, slime”", "annotation_id": "28347830", "url": "https://genius.com/28347830", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Run The Hood", "line": "Drop tape by tape and don’t promote at all, that’s just my runner up", "vault_lines": ["Drop tape by tape and don't promote at all, that's just my runner up"], "meaning": "In 2022, YoungBoy Never Broke Again released a total of eight projects, with a goal to release ten.\n\nFollowing his fourth full-length studio album, The Last Slimeto, YoungBoy released five projects — Realer 2, 3800 Degrees, Ma' I Got A Family, 3860, and Lost Files— with little to no promotion, having his main Instagram account with over 10 million followers deactivated, announcing projects in his YouTube community section.\n\nWith all five of his projects being deemed “surprise projects,” YoungBoy would often be made fun of on social media as the projects all sold between 15K to 40K despite YoungBoy being the second-highest streamed artist in the United States.\n\nYoungBoy notes that numbers aren’t of affect to him and his passion for music and that despite being under scrutiny for not selling high amounts, he will continue to release large quantities of music.", "annotation_id": "28343604", "url": "https://genius.com/28343604", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
