{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Safe Then Sorry", "line": "Still been healin’ from my pain, I’m all in", "vault_lines": ["Still been healin' from my pain, I'm all in"], "meaning": "Why he also said, “Diamonds bought to shine, removin' all the darkness in the skies”", "annotation_id": "38827248", "url": "https://genius.com/38827248", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Safe Then Sorry", "line": "Diamonds bought to shine, removin’ all the darkness in the skies", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds bought to shine, removin' all the darkness in the skies"], "meaning": "He often makes expensive purchases for a reason, specifically diamond jewelry, to make himself feel good remind him of the good instead of the bad, showing his success how it shapes by helping him.\n\nWhat he meant:\n“Diamonds (Something shiny = Good) bought to shine (that brightens us, brings us joy daily.) removin' all the darkness (things that are bad memories, thoughts, or problems) in the skies” (,in our daily world/lives)\n\nHe made a similar word play on “Bout My Business” on 38 baby 2,\n\n“I just bought a brand-new bezel\nFor to make the hard times look pretty,\nAnd I came up straight up from the block,\nI watched my grandpa save pennies”\n\nEven though easier said than done, words will always have deep meanings no matter what the words are.", "annotation_id": "38827147", "url": "https://genius.com/38827147", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Safe Then Sorry", "line": "Used to be ready to die, but now I wanna live my nigga", "vault_lines": ["Used to be ready to die, but now I wanna live my nigga (Woah)"], "meaning": "he potentially means that he’s happy he’s on a different path now and that hes thinking with his head and not his feelings no more; which is giving his life meaning and worth….. in the song “drawing symbols” he symbolizes how he was insinuating on killing his self or wanting too or something of that nature at least\n\nhe could also mean that he is out of the gang activity cause he used to state that he been ready to die in songs or ain’t scared of death so he was ready or prepared at that time but now he’s maturing and realizing. :)", "annotation_id": "27479593", "url": "https://genius.com/27479593", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
