{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Shark", "line": "He be mouthin’, Sheep gon’ catch him on the scene, walk him ’bout it (Grrt)", "vault_lines": ["He be mouthin', Sheep gon' catch him on the scene, walk him 'bout it (Grrt)"], "meaning": "“He be mouthing”: This refers to an adversary or rival talking trash, making threats, or disrespecting YoungBoy and the Never Broke Again as a collective.\n\n“Sheep gon' catch him on the scene”: “Sheep” is a direct reference to Herm Tha Blacksheep, a loyal member of YoungBoy’s inner circle. YoungBoy is stating that Herm will physically spot or confront the rival out in public (“on the scene”).\n\n“Walk him ‘bout it”: “Walking” someone is specific Louisiana street slang for tracking an opponent down on foot to ambush or shoot them. YoungBoy is warning that Herm will violently handle the rival as a direct consequence of their internet talk or disrespect.", "annotation_id": "40194064", "url": "https://genius.com/40194064", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Shark", "line": "R.I.P. to Jordan", "vault_lines": ["R.I.P. to Jordan, 'member walkin' to school with .357, just me and Levi, Northside"], "meaning": "he mentions him in mr grim reaper.", "annotation_id": "39336985", "url": "https://genius.com/39336985", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
