{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Shark", "line": "E tore up the studio, that’s Eli (Grrt, Eli)", "vault_lines": ["I ain't playin' the front, I'ma fall in the back, E tore up the studio, that's Eli (Grrt, Eli)"], "meaning": "“E tore up the studio, that’s Eli” YB wanted to let us know that he’s not talking about Choppaboy / NBA Choppaboye", "annotation_id": "37567040", "url": "https://genius.com/37567040", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Shark", "line": "I got sent to the group home, my grandma had died and I started to pray to the 5 (5, 5)", "vault_lines": ["I got sent to the group home, my grandma had died and I started to pray to the 5 (5, 5)"], "meaning": "When his grandma passed from heart failure in 2010, YoungBoy was sent to a group home since his father was (and still is) doing a 55-year sentence with no one else to really support him even though his mother was around.\n\nHe claimed in an interview with Billboard in 2023 that he used to get bullied in there for no reason.\n\n“I used to get beat up inside the group home for no reason. The other boys would put their hands on me, and I would look up like, ‘Why are you hitting me, bro? What’d I do?’ It made me discover another side of me that I never glorified or liked. I found out how to be the person that you don’t want to do that with.”", "annotation_id": "36993435", "url": "https://genius.com/36993435", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
