{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Ship It", "line": "Aroma loud, it took percentage", "vault_lines": ["Aroma loud, it took percentage"], "meaning": "Because the shipment’s odor is so potent, concealing it becomes significantly more difficult and dangerous. This extreme smell “takes a percentage” of the profits because it forces the operation to take on heavy financial losses. Extra money must be spent on advanced masking logistics and vacuum-sealing, while drivers and distributors demand a higher financial cut (hazard pay) to transport a package that easily attracts law enforcement and drug dogs.", "annotation_id": "40137639", "url": "https://genius.com/40137639", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Ship It", "line": "Not watchin’, with no mask, I listen", "vault_lines": ["Not watchin', with no mask, I listen"], "meaning": "YoungBoy highlights his situational awareness and operational discipline during high-stakes operations. By stating he is “not watchin',” he implies he avoids making direct, obvious eye contact with his surroundings to keep from drawing attention or exposing his suspicion to law enforcement and rivals. Operating “with no mask” demonstrates a high level of confidence and bravado, as he refuses to hide his identity. Instead of relying on visual surveillance, YoungBoy prioritizes his hearing (“I listen”) to scan his environment for auditory threats, such as approaching vehicles or footsteps, allowing him to remain hyper-vigilant without exposing his focus.", "annotation_id": "40137599", "url": "https://genius.com/40137599", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Ship It", "line": "That beef get left out how we found", "vault_lines": ["That beef get left out how we found"], "meaning": "YoungBoy is saying, “We are going to find the person we have a problem with, shoot them, and leave their body lying right on the spot where we caught them.”", "annotation_id": "40137514", "url": "https://genius.com/40137514", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Ship It", "line": "This a made-man drug, I could make it pure as ya want I go out and get it, then I ship it with my fuckin’ unc’", "vault_lines": ["I go out and get it, then I ship it with my fuckin' unc'"], "meaning": "In the American Mafia, a “made man” is an official, fully inducted member who has reached an elite rank and commands absolute respect. By branding his product a “made-man drug,” YoungBoy asserts that he is not dealing low-level, stepped-on street narcotics. Instead, his product originates from the highest echelon of the supply chain, rendering it untouchable. The phrase also acts as a double entendre referencing a “man-made” pure chemical synthesis. This nod indicates a direct access to narcotics manufacturing labs (such as those producing pure heroin or fentanyl). Because he deals directly with the source, YoungBoy retains the power to control the chemical purity, allowing him to custom-manufacture the strength to a buyer’s exact specifications. Despite his status as a multimillionaire superstar, YoungBoy emphasizes his hands-on approach by physically securing and distributing the supply himself. Because high-stakes federal drug trafficking carries a massive risk of informant betrayal, he minimizes liability by keeping operations strictly within his family, enlisting his uncle to assist on the run.", "annotation_id": "40137099", "url": "https://genius.com/40137099", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Ship It", "line": "Pine Parish", "vault_lines": ["The volume reach to Barksdale (Yeah), then they gon' send him to Pine Parish"], "meaning": "Pine Prairie is a village in Evangeline Parish, Louisiana", "annotation_id": "40136934", "url": "https://genius.com/40136934", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Ship It", "line": ".45 Glocks same size as Timbs", "vault_lines": [".45 Glocks same size as Timbs"], "meaning": "The .45 ACP Glock 21 is the closest size to the Timberland boots. While an adult size is bigger, this is the only .45 ACP Glock closest to the height of Timberlands.\n\nGlock 21 (.45 ACP): 8.03\" Length × 5.47\" Height\n\nTimberland Premium 6-Inch Boot: 6.0\" Height", "annotation_id": "40136904", "url": "https://genius.com/40136904", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
