{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Shot Callin", "line": "They not swaggin’ like Lil Top, nigga, huh, wipe me down", "vault_lines": ["They not swaggin' like Lil Top, nigga, huh, wipe me down"], "meaning": "The phrase “wipe me down” is a way of saying that he’s ready to show off his style and confidence, referencing a popular phrase that signifies being clean, fresh, and flashy", "annotation_id": "35438379", "url": "https://genius.com/35438379", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Shot Callin", "line": "Through the town, my name been ringin’, yeah (Ring, ring, ring, ring) Swore once I get mine, I’m gon’ come home and I’m gon’ throw ’way all this cell phone", "vault_lines": ["Through the town, my name been ringin', yeah (Ring, ring, ring, ring)", "Swore once I get mine, I'm gon' come home and I'm gon' throw 'way all this cell phone"], "meaning": "Saying that his reputation is growing, and people are talking about him in his town. His name is spreading like a ringing phone, meaning he’s became well-known. Then, he expresses that once he achieves success and secures his goals, he plans to leave behind the stress and chaos of his current life.", "annotation_id": "35438368", "url": "https://genius.com/35438368", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Shot Callin", "line": "He got nuts while I was down, now I’m out and that’s his ass", "vault_lines": ["He got nuts while I was down, now I'm out and that's his ass"], "meaning": "He could be talking about multiple people but the first people that come to mind to me is Pyungin and Ricotaliban.\n\nPyungin is a rapper from Plaquemine, LA real close by to BR where YB is from. Pyungin was signed to yb’s NBA label. They were really closed made music together after a label issue they fell out. Pyungin and Rico Taliban was seen on social media Dissing Yb and 4KT members yb’s gang. Now that Yb is out u can see Pyungin On social media bumping his music sign to they want peace again.", "annotation_id": "35434805", "url": "https://genius.com/35434805", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Shot Callin", "line": "Tell my opps that I got Glocks and they got built-in beams in", "vault_lines": ["Tell my opps that I got Glocks and they got built-in beams in"], "meaning": "Glocks refer to pistols made by the Austrian company Glock, widely used by police and civilians.\n\nBuilt-in beams are integrated laser sights, which help aim the gun more accurately by projecting a laser onto the target.\n\nYoungboy also has a song called: Green dot, where he also raps about pistols with laser sights.", "annotation_id": "35431556", "url": "https://genius.com/35431556", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Shot Callin", "line": "Rolex cost a Benz truck, got my F&N tucked", "vault_lines": ["Rolex cost a Benz truck, got my F&N tucked"], "meaning": "F&N in this context refers to a firearm made by FN Herstal, typically the FN Five-seven pistol. Having a gun tucked is slang for carrying a gun.\n\nFN Herstal is a Belgian firearms manufacturer known worldwide for producing military and civilian weapons.", "annotation_id": "35431553", "url": "https://genius.com/35431553", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Shot Callin", "line": "Bitch, I’m real American made, run with Chargers like Vin Diesel", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm real American made, run with Chargers like Vin Diesel"], "meaning": "Run with Chargers like Vin Diesel is a wordplay combining car culture.\n\nChargers refers to Dodge Chargers, a muscle car featured heavily in the Fast & Furious movies.\n\nVin Diesel is the star of Fast & Furious, often seen driving a Dodge Charger", "annotation_id": "35427274", "url": "https://genius.com/35427274", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Shot Callin", "line": "I just pulled up in that motherfuckin’— gone", "vault_lines": ["I just pulled up in that motherfuckin'— gone"], "meaning": "This part of the song features an exhaust note from a Lamborghini Aventador SVJ a limited run Italian super car featuring a v12 engine and a 0-60 time of 2.5-2.8 seconds. The car featured in the video appears to be youngboy’s personal vehicle seen in orange.", "annotation_id": "35426132", "url": "https://genius.com/35426132", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
