{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Sincerely", "line": "Dmac on the fuckin’ track", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is the official producer tag for David McDowell, otherwise, known as Dmac.\n\nDmac has produced for many artists such as Dave East, BlocBoy JB, and TrenchMobb.\n\nDmac’s most popular tracks are, “No Stylist” by Dave East, “Left Right” by BlocBoy JB, and this track.", "annotation_id": "38469182", "url": "https://genius.com/38469182", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Sincerely", "line": "Really rich, rock star, high as fuck, hangover Let you come and fuck me ’til my pain over, okay Respect that girl so much don’t won’t no motherfuckin’ brain from her", "vault_lines": ["Really rich, rock star, high as fuck, hangover", "Let you come and fuck me 'til my pain over, okay", "Respect that girl so much don't won't no motherfuckin' brain from her"], "meaning": "He cares about and respect the girl so much that he doesn’t mind her not giving him oral sex", "annotation_id": "24486150", "url": "https://genius.com/24486150", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Sincerely", "line": "It’s a panoramic four seater", "vault_lines": ["It's a panoramic four seater"], "meaning": "Youngboy is likely referencing his Bentley Continental GT, that features a new state of the art panoramic sunroof.", "annotation_id": "24048053", "url": "https://genius.com/24048053", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Sincerely", "line": "Can buy a bitch to feed my needs, can’t buy another slime heart", "vault_lines": ["Can buy a bitch to feed my needs, can't buy another slime heart"], "meaning": "Youngboy is saying that money can get him a woman that will fulfill his needs, whether that is sexually or just having someone who is there for him. However, money cannot buy him another heart.", "annotation_id": "24048028", "url": "https://genius.com/24048028", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Sincerely", "line": "Fuck that Rolls-Royce, ooh I just wanna lose this cold heart, ooh", "vault_lines": ["Fuck that Rolls-Royce, ooh", "I just wanna lose this cold heart, ooh"], "meaning": "Youngboy is the owner of a Rolls Royce Cullinan with a sticker price over 300,000 dollars. He is saying that he doesn’t care about the money or the cars, he just wants to get rid of his cold heart.", "annotation_id": "24048016", "url": "https://genius.com/24048016", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Sincerely", "line": "I wasted time don’t give a fuck bout no clock", "vault_lines": ["I wasted time don't give a fuck bout no clock, these diamonds crushed they just rocks"], "meaning": "In this line YoungBoy depicts how he has been wasting time in his past going down the wrong path. He regrets choises he has made in his past. He is regularly reflecting over his earlier mistakes through his lyrics, including being involved in gang-violence.\n\nYoungBoy is known for using story-telling in many of his songs, he is often contrasting events of his past which he describes thoroughly. NBA YoungBoy, who has been in jail several times, is striving towards a different lifestyle where he can focus on himself, his career and his family, including his eight children.\n\nIn more recent projects of Kentrell, the rapper illustrates a new image where he is more responsible and focused on his, as well as his family’s, well-being. YoungBoy has gotten to the point in his life where he is finally willing to move on, while still accepting his miserable past. Realizing that time constantly moves on and the impossibility of changing the past, he is no longer wasting time mentally reflecting over his mistakes.", "annotation_id": "24036483", "url": "https://genius.com/24036483", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
