{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Solar Eclipse", "line": "I’m a 38 baby I swear that I’m ruthless", "vault_lines": ["I'm a 38 baby I swear that I'm ruthless"], "meaning": "NBA Youngboy is often called “38 Baby” as a nickname and even has a couple of albums named after it, including 38 Baby and 38 Baby 2. He released 38 Baby when he was only 17 and 38 Baby 2 a few years later in 2020.\n\nYoungboy is also known for being born, raised, or having some relation to 38 Chippewa Street in his hometown of Baton Rouge, Louisiana.", "annotation_id": "34850832", "url": "https://genius.com/34850832", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Solar Eclipse", "line": "Slatt, slatt Slatt, slatt, slatt, slatt", "vault_lines": ["So many times I could've died, but you niggas blew it (Slatt)"], "meaning": "Slatt is a common slang word used by members of the Blood gang. In recent years, however, its usage has become watered down, and many now use it as an acronym for “Slime Love All The Time”. This ad-lib is found on many of Young Thug’s songs, like in “Slime Shit”.\n\nYoung Thug claims to live the Slime Lifestyle and even released a whole mixtape series titled “Slime Season”.", "annotation_id": "30468934", "url": "https://genius.com/30468934", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Solar Eclipse", "line": "(Skrt)", "vault_lines": ["Hellcat not a Charger, way faster than a 'Rari (Skrt)"], "meaning": "Originally a Gucci Mane ad-lib, “Skrt” became extremely popular among rappers in 2015. The sound imitates the rubber of a car burning on the street when turning or stopping fast. Future, Fetty Wap, Chris Brown, Bryson Tiller, French Montana, Chance The Rapper,Jeremih, Post Malone, Chief Keef, Young Thug, Travis Scott, Lil Uzi Vert and Drake have all used “Skrt” in songs.", "annotation_id": "30468790", "url": "https://genius.com/30468790", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Solar Eclipse", "line": "Before the fame, I was strapped up on Valley Park with a Glock", "vault_lines": ["Before the fame, I was strapped up on Valley Park with a Glock"], "meaning": "Valley Park is NBA Dump’s neighborhood.", "annotation_id": "29415312", "url": "https://genius.com/29415312", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Solar Eclipse", "line": "Back in 8th grade, I ain’t have a thing, baby", "vault_lines": ["Back in 8th grade, I ain't have a thing, baby"], "meaning": "In NBA Youngboy life, He struggled a lot when his grandma died and his friend “Lil Dave” stated in his song Life. NBA Youngboy grandma helped him alot, NBA Youngboy says his grandma was there more than anyone in interviews.\n\n\n\n (Photo Of NBA Youngboy’s grandmother)", "annotation_id": "22365516", "url": "https://genius.com/22365516", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Solar Eclipse", "line": "If it go down now, I know Baby Joe gon’ shoot", "vault_lines": ["If it go down now, I know Baby Joe gon' shoot"], "meaning": "In this line, Youngboy is saying that if all falls down, fellow Baton Rouge rapper and collaborator BBG Baby Joe has his back.\n\n\n\nBBG Baby Joe pictured on the left and YoungBoy in the center", "annotation_id": "19106419", "url": "https://genius.com/19106419", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Solar Eclipse", "line": "Got snake on my collar, I tell you it’s Gucci", "vault_lines": ["Got snake on my collar, I tell you it's Gucci"], "meaning": "Gucci is a notable Italian luxury company founded by Guccio Gucci in 1921.\n\n\n\nYoungboy’s line references Gucci’s expensive top that incorporates a snake into the collar design, however, his first acknowledgement of the shirt came in his 2017 track “Bet”;\n\nGucci shirt with a snake up on it", "annotation_id": "14830085", "url": "https://genius.com/14830085", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
