{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Still Waiting", "line": "They got me wearing Bob Barker, wish I had on some VLONE", "vault_lines": ["They got me wearing Bob Barker, wish I had on some VLONE"], "meaning": "Bob Barker was a famous TV host, but Top is referring to the jail clothing that’s produced by the Bob Barker Equipment Company.\n\n\n\nYoungBoy states he would rather be wearing Vlone instead, a clothing company founded by A$AP Bari, the co-founder of rap collective A$AP Mob. Top also released a collaborative collection with Vlone in late 2020.\n\nThe whole line is a simple analogy for him wanting to be free, wearing what he wants, instead of being locked up and being forced to wear jail uniforms.", "annotation_id": "23824177", "url": "https://genius.com/23824177", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
