{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Switches", "line": "My hood is so unheard of (I heard they risin’)", "vault_lines": ["My hood is so unheard of (I heard they risin')"], "meaning": "His hood, in the northside of Baton Rouge, Louisiana, was 38th Street and Chippewa which was, at first, unheard of, so not many rappers were getting attention, but now they all are rising to fame.", "annotation_id": "38297311", "url": "https://genius.com/38297311", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Switches", "line": "Why the fuck you think these gangsters respect me? Bitch, I come from swervin’ (Hrr, hrr)", "vault_lines": ["Why the fuck you think these gangsters respect me? Bitch, I come from swervin' (Hrr, hrr)"], "meaning": "Gangsters respect YB because he came from doing drive-bys, which is no lie you can look it up for yourself. Even though he ain’t succeed, he still let off that fire.", "annotation_id": "38297286", "url": "https://genius.com/38297286", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Switches", "line": "As a juvie, a hundred-somethin’ pints in a ’Burban", "vault_lines": ["As a juvie, a hundred-somethin' pints in a 'Burban"], "meaning": "Juvie: Short for juvenile or teenager. YoungBoy references his youth growing up in Baton Rouge, Louisiana, where he was involved in street life before his music career took off.\n\nPints: Refers to pint bottles of prescription cough syrup (codeine/promethazine) used to make “lean.”\n\n‘Burban: Short for a Chevrolet Suburban. This large SUV is favored for its massive trunk capacity, making it ideal for hauling bulk cargo discretely.\n\nReal-World Context: YoungBoy uses this line to establish early street credibility by claiming he handled high-volume supply as a minor. A hundred pints carries an incredibly high street value. While it may be a hyperbole (lyrical exaggeration), it emphasizes the dangerous, high-stakes environment of his adolescence.", "annotation_id": "38297271", "url": "https://genius.com/38297271", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Switches", "line": "I’m flippin’ and servin’", "vault_lines": ["I'm flippin' and servin' (Flippin' and servin')"], "meaning": "Also the same as jugging and trapping, he’s just saying he’s flipping the drugs that he’s serving out to customers.", "annotation_id": "38297267", "url": "https://genius.com/38297267", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Switches", "line": "Juggin’", "vault_lines": ["Rappin' and juggin', what you doin'? (Brr)"], "meaning": "Selling drugs for money. Also known as trapping.", "annotation_id": "38297266", "url": "https://genius.com/38297266", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Switches", "line": "One bullet connect with your head and it’s knockin’ out more than your tooth", "vault_lines": ["One bullet connect with your head and it's knockin' out more than your tooth"], "meaning": "Not only will it knock out your tooth but it will knock out your brain as soon as the bullet connects. Diss to Pooh Shiesty", "annotation_id": "38297250", "url": "https://genius.com/38297250", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Switches", "line": "Dunk on his ass, I do it like Blake", "vault_lines": ["Dunk on his ass, I do it like Blake"], "meaning": "On this track, YoungBoy contrasts athletic dominance with street warfare. In basketball, a poster dunk requires explosive, unstoppable force that completely blindsides the defender. By referencing Blake Griffin—the premier poster-dunk artist of the 2010s—YoungBoy implies that his street operations are just as definitive and high-impact. This imagery mirrors the song’s title, “Switches,” suggesting that the rapid, overwhelming force of an automatic weapon allows him to completely overpower his targets without giving them a chance to react.", "annotation_id": "38297195", "url": "https://genius.com/38297195", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
