{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Tears of War", "line": "Last night, I cried tears of war Murdered you bitches, I deserve this", "vault_lines": ["Last night, I cried tears of war", "Murdered you bitches, I deserve this"], "meaning": "YoungBoy interpolates lines from Rick Ross' “Tears of Joy”:\n\nLast night, I cried tears of joy\nWhat did I do to deserve this?", "annotation_id": "32034553", "url": "https://genius.com/32034553", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Tears of War", "line": "Know Quando love me, put yo’ ass six-feet, huh", "vault_lines": ["Know Quando love me, put yo' ass six-feet, huh"], "meaning": "Quando Rondo is a rapper from Savannah, Georgia. He is signed to YoungBoy’s Never Broke Again records, signing to the label in 2018. He and YoungBoy have been friends for several years. The two even released a collaborative mixtape, 3860, in late 2022.\n\nQuando and YoungBoy frequently shout each other out in their songs, for example on Quando’s “50” or on YoungBoy’s “Young Stunna.”\n\n“50” by Quando Rondo:\n\nIt’s hard to stop the violence even though I’m ridin' with YB\n\n“Young Stunna” by YoungBoy:\n\nI bang that red and Quando bangin' blue\n\nQuando has frequently backed YB up and expressed his loyalty to the Baton Rouge rapper in multiple interviews. He views him as a GOAT and is grateful for the opportunities he provided, such as when YoungBoy gave Quando one million dollars.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/i2f8YrsLN7g\n\nIn juxtaposition to the rest of this song where YoungBoy talks about multiple people he’s been falling out with, he mentions that him and Quando still have a strong relationship and he knows he has love for him.", "annotation_id": "32032298", "url": "https://genius.com/32032298", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Tears of War", "line": "Try once too many times, we tear your show up with .40s", "vault_lines": ["Try once too many times, we tear your show up with .40s"], "meaning": "Youngboy is saying he might spare you if you play with him once, but if you mess with him too many times, he’ll kill you with a 40 caliber pistol.\n\nNotice the number wordplay in this and the last line (Five, once, too, .40s).", "annotation_id": "32031067", "url": "https://genius.com/32031067", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Tears of War", "line": "Ridin’ inside a Maybach, writin’ music, I’ma show you niggas", "vault_lines": ["Ridin' inside a Maybach, writin' music, I'ma show you niggas"], "meaning": "The sample of this song is Rick Ross' Tears of Joy. Ross' record label is called Maybach Music.\n\nYoungboy is saying he’s writing music in his Maybach, hence the play on Maybach Music.", "annotation_id": "32031043", "url": "https://genius.com/32031043", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Tears of War", "line": "Scared to vent to Yaya", "vault_lines": ["Scared to vent to Yaya but I could talk to my guys"], "meaning": "Here he is talking about yaya Mayweather. His Baby mama", "annotation_id": "32029972", "url": "https://genius.com/32029972", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Tears of War", "line": "Real niggas playin’ ball, they fuck with 4KTrey", "vault_lines": ["Real niggas playin' ball, they fuck with 4KTrey"], "meaning": "Youngboy could be refering to Ja Morant who has shown his love for Youngboy’s music in the recent years aswell as using a lyric from Youngboys,‘Fresh Prince of Utah’ : “Its a parade in my city yeah”, as his catchphrase", "annotation_id": "32029650", "url": "https://genius.com/32029650", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Tears of War", "line": "Mansion in the sky, plannin’ murders with my brother B", "vault_lines": ["Mansion in the sky, plannin' murders with my brother B"], "meaning": "YB is mentioning his close NBA friend Big B (Boomer). He has been a part of NBA since its founding. Big B also rap and has dropped several tapes like 5th God in 2019, Thoughts Of A Demon in 2020, Streets Aint Safe and Tru Scars in 2023.", "annotation_id": "32026776", "url": "https://genius.com/32026776", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Tears of War", "line": "It ain’t much that I can say, I been thinkin’ ’bout Vea", "vault_lines": ["It ain't much that I can say, I been thinkin' 'bout Vea"], "meaning": "YB is talking about YKWIHF Vea, a fellow Baton Rouge rapper. On March 30, 2024, YB and Vea went live on Instagram previewing an unreleased collab song between the two rappers. Vea is from Bankstown, a BR hood that some of YB’s close potnas like Herm Tha Blacksheep and NBA Big B also comes from.", "annotation_id": "32026522", "url": "https://genius.com/32026522", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
