{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Testimony", "line": "I come up straight from the block, me and Ten, we ran from cops, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I come up straight from the block, me and Ten, we ran from cops, nigga"], "meaning": "In this line, NBA Youngboy paints a vivid picture of his upbringing and the challenges he faced growing up in his neighborhood. By stating that he came straight from the block, he’s referring to his roots and the gritty environment in which he was raised. The mention of running from cops adds a sense of danger and rebellion, highlighting the constant struggle he and Ten had to endure to escape the clutches of law enforcement. The use of the word “nigga” adds an element of authenticity and raw emotion to the lyrics, reflecting NBA Youngboy’s personal experiences and cultural background. Overall, this line showcases NBA Youngboy’s resilience and determination to rise above his circumstances.", "annotation_id": "29642166", "url": "https://genius.com/29642166", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
