{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "The Gaulden’s", "line": "Old-ass nigga claimin’ he the hottest, I’ma hit his bitch-ass with a fan", "vault_lines": ["Old-ass nigga claimin' he the hottest, I'ma hit his bitch-ass with a fan (Fan)"], "meaning": "Talking about how Future claims to be the hottest in Atlanta, and he uses figurative language by saying he will hit Future with a “fan” since he’s so “hot.” Now notice my quotation makes around fan & hot. Fan is for a gun, no specific type, any gun. Hot in this sentence is slang for being a very well-known rapper, well-known for good music that it has you viewing yourself as a GOAT maybe or the best rapper of all time, whatever you wanna call yourself. It boosts your ego, self-esteem, pride, and more.", "annotation_id": "40645912", "url": "https://genius.com/40645912", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "The Gaulden’s", "line": "Why the fuck these niggas actin’ modern like back in the day they wasn’t my fan? (Fan)", "vault_lines": ["Why the fuck these niggas actin' modern like back in the day they wasn't my fan? (Fan)"], "meaning": "A diss to Doeboy, there’s a old tweet of him telling his homebody, “Man, you know how I get about YB,” now all of a sudden he on his IG story dissing, June 9, and says YoungBoy started it by commenting under his post. Talking like he been a gangster, and YB was never that nor 5, the internet got him acting gangster. YB responds to that by saying Doeboy was known to cry.", "annotation_id": "40645895", "url": "https://genius.com/40645895", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
