{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "The Story of O.J. (Top Version)", "line": "Tell me why your favorite rapper so fake-influenced Telling you he gon’ do things, that he Never wasn’t gon’ do, that’s the Mandela Effect", "vault_lines": ["Tell me why your favorite rapper so fake-influenced", "Telling you he gon' do things, that he", "Never wasn't gon' do, that's the Mandela Effect"], "meaning": "Rapper talk about how they do this and that but really known to lie and hide behind the camera.  The Mandela Effect is when the society believe something is valid and happened when in reality it never occured. So where do these rappers get validated from if none of the things they say happen but yall would believe it.", "annotation_id": "21525932", "url": "https://genius.com/21525932", "state": "pending", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
