{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "This Month Confessions", "line": "Fallin’, I done walked from out that cage, thought I was findin’ my way", "vault_lines": ["Fallin', I done walked from out that cage, thought I was findin' my way"], "meaning": "This refers to the fact that this song was made shorty after Youngboy got out of prison. Here he’s saying that even though he’s finally free, he keeps relapsing and falling into despair and bad decisions even though he thought he could be a good man.", "annotation_id": "38659226", "url": "https://genius.com/38659226", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
