{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "This Not a Song “This for My Supporters”", "line": "As I start to promote peace and I say, “Stop the violence,” I’m incitin’ a riot (D-Roc) If you ain’t hear me clear, my nigga I said, “As I start to promote the peace and I say, ”Stop the violence,” I think I’m incitin’ a riot”", "vault_lines": ["If you ain't hear me clear, my nigga"], "meaning": "“Stop the violence” is a tag (#stoptheviolence) that NBA Youngboy started spreading throughout his social media posts. Fans and music critics assumed this was Youngboy’s attempt at promoting peace, a radical shift in his music considering many fans consider much of his catalog as “murder anthems.”\n\n\n\nPhoto source  - xxlmag.com", "annotation_id": "29678223", "url": "https://genius.com/29678223", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "This Not a Song “This for My Supporters”", "line": "I FaceTimed my brother that Blood me in, you see this big, “4L,” on my neck Pussy nigga had the nerve to text me back and say, “Who the fuck is this?” Now, that’s cold, slime", "vault_lines": ["I FaceTimed my brother that Blood me in, you see this big, \"4L,\" on my neck", "Pussy nigga had the nerve to text me back and say, \"Who the fuck is this?\"", "Now, that's cold, slime"], "meaning": "This could be a shot to East Atlanta rapper 21 Savage. In 2017, 21 hopped on Youngboy’s remix of “Murder” which blew them both up pretty well. It seems here that YB is claiming 21 put him into the Bloods street gang as both have insinuated their affiliation for the gang. One of 21’s signature catch phrases is “4L” which means For Life and he is also in an East Atlanta street gang known as 4L. After the whole King Von-Quando situation, it seemed like 21 sided with Lil Durk and Youngboy’s saying when he tried to call him, 21 pretended to not know him.", "annotation_id": "28249742", "url": "https://genius.com/28249742", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "This Not a Song “This for My Supporters”", "line": "Shorty whole family evil and they controlled by the fuckin’ money", "vault_lines": ["Shorty whole family evil and they controlled by the fuckin' money"], "meaning": "This is a shot to Youngboy’s ex-girlfriend Iyanna “Yaya” Mayweather (And the mother of his son Kentrell Jr). Yaya is the daughter of famous boxer Floyd Mayweather. Youngboy’s saying that the entire Mayweather family is evil and is controlled by money and greed with Youngboy even making a diss song called “Dirty Iyanna”", "annotation_id": "28233882", "url": "https://genius.com/28233882", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "This Not a Song “This for My Supporters”", "line": "Can’t thug with my bro ’nem no more", "vault_lines": ["Can't thug with my bro 'nem no more"], "meaning": "This could be a reference to Youngboy’s close friend Ben10 who opposes Youngboy’s stop the violence movement. However this could be a reference to his other close friend DDawg (Who was recently released for attempted murder). Due to the fact that Youngboy’s on house arrest, there are certain rules that come with it such as the people who are able to visit. Both Ben and DDawg are some of the people that cannot visit him. (Ben is on top, DDawg is on bottom)", "annotation_id": "28233860", "url": "https://genius.com/28233860", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "This Not a Song “This for My Supporters”", "line": "My baby mama don’t fuck with me no more", "vault_lines": ["My baby mama don't fuck with me no more"], "meaning": "Youngboy has multiple baby mamas and it’s no secret to the public. However, it seems like he’s taking jabs at Jania (The mother of his son Kacey). Jania is currently married to Atlanta Hawk’s shooting guard Dejounte Murray but back in late 2017-early 2018, the two were the Will Smith and Jada Pinkett of rap. But in 2018, hotel surveillance footage showed Youngboy hitting Jania and he later accused Jania of being unfaithful and the two broke up. The two haven’t been on the best of terms with Youngboy accusing Dejounte of pushing his son out of car and Jania claiming that Youngboy doesn’t take time to talk or see his son.", "annotation_id": "28233832", "url": "https://genius.com/28233832", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "This Not a Song “This for My Supporters”", "line": "Why you think that boy from my city who y’all think murder man wanna down a nigga ’bout the paint on top my face? It’s really a money thing That nigga mad that I’m holdin’ That nigga mad that I’m chosen and he been doin’ this his whole life and I passed that bitch up", "vault_lines": ["It's really a money thing", "That nigga mad that I'm holdin'", "That nigga mad that I'm chosen and he been doin' this his whole life and I passed that bitch up"], "meaning": "This is a diss to rapper Boosie Badazz. Boosie (Who is also from Youngboy’s city, Baton Rouge Louisiana) came into the rap game in the early 2000’s and was an inspiration to Youngboy and they actually have a few songs together. But after a falling out for unknown reasons, the two have stopped being friends. Youngboy’s claiming that Boosie is jealous of his career as Youngboy was 17 years old when he was getting platinum records and millions of streams and dollars while Boosie’s projects haven’t reached high charts since 2017 while Youngboy’s recent album “I Rest My Case” reached number 9 on Billboards. He calls him “Murda Man” because after Boosie beat a first degree murder case, he began to refer to himself as such.", "annotation_id": "28231735", "url": "https://genius.com/28231735", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "This Not a Song “This for My Supporters”", "line": "And it hurt my heart that Kanye let them people break his soul How the fuck that go? Nigga, stay in your home! Nigga, hold your ground! You strong!", "vault_lines": ["And it hurt my heart that Kanye let them people break his soul", "How the fuck that go? Nigga, stay in your home!"], "meaning": "Kanye West is a rapper from Chicago who blew up in the early 2000’s with albums such as “The College Dropout”, “Graduation” and “808’s And Heartbreak”. In his career, he’s been subjected to many controversies such as supporting Donald Trump in the 2016 election and claiming slavery was a choice. Recently, he’s been under fire for wearing an “White Lives Matter” shirt and saying anti-Semitic comments on social media.\n\nThere are many reasons to why he acts the way to his fans. One is that when his mother Donda died, he spiraled as the two were very close. Another is that his bipolar disorder gets the best of him. Another is that he’s just trolling the internet.\n\nRegardless of what the excuse is, Youngboy is showing his support for Kanye and advising him to stand his ground against critics and haters.", "annotation_id": "28231687", "url": "https://genius.com/28231687", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "This Not a Song “This for My Supporters”", "line": "Yeah, I know you know they wan’ kill me in Atlanta", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I know you know they wan' kill me in Atlanta and every city out here"], "meaning": "Youngboy’s artist Quando Rondo was involved in an altercation with Lil Durk’s artist King Von in November of 2020 in Atlanta. The altercation left King Von dead and Lil Durk’s camp and Youngboy’s camp have been going back and forth. So Youngboy’s saying that pretty much every city with increasing crime (Atlanta, Chicago, Memphis, New York ect) that they want Youngboy and his camp dead.", "annotation_id": "28231667", "url": "https://genius.com/28231667", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "This Not a Song “This for My Supporters”", "line": "Shorty say he gon’ boom me on camera, and I ain’t got no more fight inside my heart So if you run into me, I’m just gon’ let it go down, I ain’t scared, my boy", "vault_lines": ["Shorty say he gon' boom me on camera, and I ain't got no more fight inside my heart", "So if you run into me, I'm just gon' let it go down, I ain't scared, my boy"], "meaning": "On November 27, 2022, an altercation between NBA YoungBoy and Florida native Bobby Shmurda sparked up on social media where Shmurda claimed that he sees no interest in other rappers talking about murders their friends committed, to which Bobby remarked:\n\nFuck y'all be jacking everybody other shit. What you doing? What you doing, homie? Stop talking ‘bout your brother shooter […] like what the fuck do you do? huh?\n\nYoungBoy, minutes later, replied to Bobby’s comments on an Instagram story, where he stated:\n\nOk mr “von shmurda” you better stop the violence boy !!!! I thought you was a fan😂& don’t lie. Go make a hit. I just want be friends. Well, talking violent help me keep the peace or just stay away slave.\n\nDespite NBA YoungBoy involving discriminative words, the two bounce back and forth responding on Instagram stories, which YoungBoy promoted to “stop the violence.” However, NBA YoungBoy particularly alludes to Bobby Shmurda’s verbal death threats on Instagram live where he was determined to murder YoungBoy, Wack 100 and DJ Akademiks:\n\nBut when I catch y'all lil' niggas, DJ Akademiks, everybody, bro. Any nigga I catch like, Wack, any y'all niggas, y'all can record this […] I’m going to boom them on camera […] on camera live. I’m on parole, I don’t give a fuck. I’m gonna boom one of y'all niggas on camera. On my dead grandmother, nigga. Next time you call my name and niggas who called my name already, Wack, all them niggas, when I catch y'all, on my dead grandmother, I’m gonna boom y'all on camera, I don’t give a fuck.", "annotation_id": "27398069", "url": "https://genius.com/27398069", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "This Not a Song “This for My Supporters”", "line": "I’m wide awake and I’m glad to say, she doin’ better than hoes I had around", "vault_lines": ["I'm wide awake and I'm glad to say, she doin' better than hoes I had around"], "meaning": "Again another shout out to glorilla. Yb is saying is that she is doing better than the prevous girls yb been around (idk how many hoes he got he has 10 children with serval different women and I can’t name em, the only ones I know is jania ngl 💀)", "annotation_id": "27379865", "url": "https://genius.com/27379865", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "This Not a Song “This for My Supporters”", "line": "I know they gon’ try to switch up my words Man, tell that girl, let’s do a song", "vault_lines": ["I know they gon' try to switch up my words", "Man, tell that girl, let's do a song"], "meaning": "If i’m not sure he might be talking about to the ppl that is gon switch up his words and people gon think this is a diss. Although some ppl think this a diss he even said “Man, tell that girl, let’s do a song”. Yo yb can u put in the black album in January 👀?", "annotation_id": "27379858", "url": "https://genius.com/27379858", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "This Not a Song “This for My Supporters”", "line": "Respect for many women, sad to say that most these bitches hoes You better not bump GloRilla, bitch, you gon’ get kicked up out this home You ain’t fuckin’ with no fuck nigga, bitch you know I’m the realest ’round, yeah", "vault_lines": ["You better not bump GloRilla, bitch, you gon' get kicked up out this home", "You ain't fuckin' with no fuck nigga, bitch you know I'm the realest 'round, yeah"], "meaning": "So YoungBoy is shouting out glorilla’s hit song “F.N.F. (Let’s Go)”.\nAnd since youngboy said “fuck nigga” that is what was being said in glorlla song “I’m F-R-E-E, fuck nigga free” (even tho free is not mentioned in this part)", "annotation_id": "27379812", "url": "https://genius.com/27379812", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "This Not a Song “This for My Supporters”", "line": "But it’s the holidays, everybody broke, so you knowin’ that’s why it’s trouble sent I’m Rolls Royce ridin’, please don’t tell me who said somethin’ I know this ain’t right, God please forgive, I misled some", "vault_lines": ["But it's the holidays, everybody broke, so you knowin' that's why it's trouble sent", "I'm Rolls Royce ridin', please don't tell me who said somethin'", "I know this ain't right, God please forgive, I misled some"], "meaning": "Youngboy is saying during the holidays, it’s especially tough of poverty stricken family and they might cause trouble just to provide. He is also riding in his luxury Rolls-Royce and is insinuating he does not want to hear about any negativity in his state of mind, but because hes made it out he knows he no longer is riding out the violence but the young kids still do that look up to him.", "annotation_id": "27275642", "url": "https://genius.com/27275642", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
