{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "This for The", "line": "This for them bitches who thinkin’ they real, but really they fake This for them niggas that’s thinkin’ they thuggin’, but really they ain’t This for them niggas that really be trappin’ up out the ra-a-ain I married that choppa you know that she with it I call her my ba-a-ae", "vault_lines": ["I call her my ba-a-ae"], "meaning": "All of the people out there claim that they are what they say they are, but YB says they’re just faking for the attention.", "annotation_id": "22111886", "url": "https://genius.com/22111886", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "This for The", "line": "DMac got me too bangin’", "vault_lines": ["DMac got me too bangin'"], "meaning": "This is the producer tagline for producer DMacTooBangin, best known for his work with Moneybagg Yo and Lil Baby.\n\nHe has worked previously with YoungBoy on his collaborative track “Homicide” with Moneybagg Yo and his major hit “Outside Today. However this is the first time that Quando Rondo and DMac have worked together.", "annotation_id": "15766084", "url": "https://genius.com/15766084", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
