{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Through the Storm", "line": "Now I’m in a two-door coupe, it used to be a four-door", "vault_lines": ["Now I'm in a two-door coupe, it used to be a four-door"], "meaning": "A two-door coupe refers to a vehicle with two doors that prioritizes sporty styling, handling, and a lighter, more compact design, often featuring sleeker, sloping rooflines (i.e., a sports car).\n\nA four-door refers to a vehicle with four doors that emphasizes practicality, offering easier rear-seat access, greater cargo space, and a five-passenger capacity (i.e., a sedan).\n\nHere, YoungBoy is saying that now he drives a sports car, implying a lavish and luxurious lifestyle, instead of a more practical and mundane lifestyle when he drove a sedan-like car.", "annotation_id": "38605024", "url": "https://genius.com/38605024", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Through the Storm", "line": "I get QRedd, lace the track just like a blunt of dope though", "vault_lines": ["I get QRedd, lace the track just like a blunt of dope though"], "meaning": "QRedd or QRedOnTheTrack is a music producer and audio engineer based in Baton Rouge, Louisiana. He is best known for his hip-hop work with fellow Baton Rouge rappers YoungBoy Never Broke Again and Fredo Bang.\n\nHere, YoungBoy is saying QRedd’s technical skill (as a producer) to create a song layer by layer (e.g., adding drums, then bass, then guitar) is like that of “lacing a drug” or, in this case, “lacing a blunt of dope”.", "annotation_id": "38604895", "url": "https://genius.com/38604895", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Through the Storm", "line": "Don’t pay for cable, he want static, tell him let me know though", "vault_lines": ["Don't pay for cable, he want static, tell him let me know though"], "meaning": "Static on cable TV usually indicates a weak or missing signal, often caused by loose, damaged, or disconnected coaxial cables, faulty splitters, or a glitch in the cable box.\n\nHere, static refers to trouble, conflict, heated opposition, or unwelcome criticism/interference from someone.\n\nYoungBoy is saying, although he doesn’t pay for/have cable TV, if his opps want static/smoke, he’ll give that to them instead.", "annotation_id": "38604842", "url": "https://genius.com/38604842", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Through the Storm", "line": "Remember me and Three we used to ride up in a stolo", "vault_lines": ["Remember me and Three we used to ride up in a stolo"], "meaning": "three aka 3Three is a member in never broke again\nA stolo is a stolen car", "annotation_id": "37764537", "url": "https://genius.com/37764537", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
