{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Thug Nigga Life", "line": "Patek and Audemar, got both and it don’t mean nothin’ (Uh uh) I rock too many chains, just one feel like I mean somethin", "vault_lines": ["Patek and Audemar, got both and it don't mean nothin' (Uh uh)"], "meaning": "YB explains how to him, significance and sentimentality are not attached to conventional definitions of significance- Patek Philippe and Audemars Piguet are both luxury watch brands, with YB possessing both but feeling nothing inside. This shows the fake significance of leading a materialistic lifestyle, where only the chain he has (probably the NBA chain) actually means anything to him.", "annotation_id": "36427087", "url": "https://genius.com/36427087", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Thug Nigga Life", "line": "We all makin’ choices just to die, not to live, it’s a lie", "vault_lines": ["We all makin' choices just to die, not to live, it's a lie (Yeah, it's a lie)"], "meaning": "YB shows a rather realistic and grim perception of the “Thug Life”, showing how by living treacherously and on the edge, each choice they make afterwards only pushes them closer to the end of their life, and even successful encounters or choices that lead to their survival are only prolonging the inevitable, and that being successful is a lie since a bullet will still kill anyone regardless of how powerful, rich or influential they are.", "annotation_id": "36427079", "url": "https://genius.com/36427079", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Thug Nigga Life", "line": "You would do better making a Doberman sit", "vault_lines": ["You would do better making a Doberman sit"], "meaning": "YB means to say that he is an unrestrained, uncontrollable force, and the figurative “you”- most likely referring to other gangster rappers, or the government and authorities, would have better luck making a Doberman- a large, intimidating dog obey orders and sit in an act of submission rather than making him comply and obey with  predefined regulations", "annotation_id": "36427037", "url": "https://genius.com/36427037", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Thug Nigga Life", "line": "A thug nigga life", "vault_lines": ["It's a thug nigga life"], "meaning": "YB refers to how his life, and like many other aspiring gangster rappers in general, is a “Thug nigga life”, not one for the soft hearted or sentimental, a life where every choice leads to death; or even the prolonging of the wait for death, stating how the choices made are not to live but rather to die, creating a false perception of life in “the trenches”.", "annotation_id": "36427020", "url": "https://genius.com/36427020", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
