{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Time I’m On", "line": "No more sleeping on Montana couch with a chopper somewhere close around", "vault_lines": ["No more sleeping on Montana couch with a chopper somewhere close around"], "meaning": "Kyle “Montana” Claiborne was YoungBoy’s first manager and the co-founder and CEO of YB’s label, Never Broke Again. The two met in 2016 when Montana began to drive YoungBoy to his shows for hours where he became his manager. Due to YB being under eighteen at the time, Montana founded the label under the two’s names as he was legally allowed to. In an interview with Billboard, Montana expressed his motivation for becoming YoungBoy’s manager at the time was that he wasn’t a rapper but desired the lifestyle of one.\n\nIn August 2017, following the release of YoungBoy’s hit single, “Untouchable” in which he mentions Montana, YoungBoy appeared in a Genius verified video in which he broke down the lyric he mentions Montana in, stating that he’s grinding so hard for his kids and for Montana to live well:\n\nThis shit for my little boys. All of this shit for my little boys. Me changing for the better is for my little boys. And I say Montana too because Montana give me anything. I got money, but I walk in the mall and still ask Montana to buy me this and he’ll buy it.", "annotation_id": "29989796", "url": "https://genius.com/29989796", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Time I’m On", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Youngboy-never-broke-again-time-im-on-lyrics", "genius_title": "Time I’m On", "genius_id": 4933860, "source": "api"}
