{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "To My Lowest", "line": "Tell that you lying ‘cause you get loud when we start fussin’ (I ain’t gon’ hit you)", "vault_lines": ["Tell that you lying 'cause you get loud when we start fussin' (I ain't gon' hit you)"], "meaning": "he can tell that she’s lying when she begins trying to use an amplified voice to get her plint across, a common habit amongst people who are being exposed for lying.\n\nad-libs ‘i ain’t gon hit you’ to highlight how well he treated her compared to her last boyfriends.", "annotation_id": "27662483", "url": "https://genius.com/27662483", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "To My Lowest", "line": "Fuck that nigga, he can’t do anything for you Mistreatin’ me, bitch, you could leave, I ain’t do you nothing", "vault_lines": ["Fuck that nigga, he can't do anything for you", "Mistreatin' me, bitch, you could leave, I ain't do you nothing"], "meaning": "mixed expressions, he begins the verse with saying he’d do anything, then he begins the next line completely shifting his sorrowful tone to anger.\n\nhe also expressed how the girl mistreated him, and he would’ve preferred that she’d left rather than lead him on as he didn’t do anything to her.", "annotation_id": "27662478", "url": "https://genius.com/27662478", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
