{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Untouchable", "line": "We untouchable come run that money up with me, nigga, yeah", "vault_lines": ["We untouchable come run that money up with me, nigga, yeah"], "meaning": "I didn’t really mean untouchable because you are touchable. I don’t give a fuck who you are. But when I said that I meant basically, we’re unstoppable at this point. The only thing stopping me is jail or death now. You gotta stop hating. Either you’re going to see me on the sideline or you’re gonna come get rid of us. It’s enough money for everybody. That’s it for the stingy niggas.", "annotation_id": "12489889", "url": "https://genius.com/12489889", "state": "verified", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Untouchable", "line": "We untouchable, come run that money up with me, nigga", "vault_lines": ["We untouchable, come run that money up with me, nigga"], "meaning": "I didn’t really mean untouchable because you are touchable. I don’t give a fuck who you are. But when I said that I meant basically, we’re unstoppable at this point. The only thing stopping me is jail or death now. You gotta stop hating. Either you’re going to see me on the sideline or you’re gonna come get rid of us. It’s enough money for everybody. That’s it for the stingy niggas.", "annotation_id": "12489884", "url": "https://genius.com/12489884", "state": "verified", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Untouchable", "line": "We untouchable, come run that money up with me, nigga", "vault_lines": ["We untouchable, come run that money up with me, nigga"], "meaning": "I didn’t really mean untouchable because you are touchable. I don’t give a fuck who you are. But when I said that I meant basically, we’re unstoppable at this point. The only thing stopping me is jail or death now. You gotta stop hating. Either you’re going to see me on the sideline or you’re gonna come get rid of us. It’s enough money for everybody. That’s it for the stingy niggas.", "annotation_id": "12489878", "url": "https://genius.com/12489878", "state": "verified", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Untouchable", "line": "This for Monique for loving me and bein’ my helpin’ hand", "vault_lines": ["This for Monique for loving me and bein' my helpin' hand"], "meaning": "That’s 33 mama. That’s my godmother, my second mom. She was crazy. She been with me ever since my grandma died. One day I guess she saw I was going through something. She been there for me, just supporting all the way—I think she paid for my first studio sessions, literally. She paid for me to take trips to chase this shit. She always been there. She said when my grandma was dying, she said my grandma called her. Because she stayed down the street. I met 3 because he stayed down the street out on Chippewa. She said my grandma called her while she was taking her last breath. And when she got there, she said my grandma made her promise that she’ll forever be there for me. She made that promise.", "annotation_id": "12489868", "url": "https://genius.com/12489868", "state": "verified", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Untouchable", "line": "This for that North 38 Baby, they know I ain’t playin’", "vault_lines": ["This for that North 38 Baby, they know I ain't playin'"], "meaning": "That’s for that north shit. My hood actually love me. I don’t know. They love me bro. When I say this for them. Yeah, I’m forever repping that. I stand on that gang. This what it is, forever always down for this. This is where I ran around at.\n\n38 Chippewa. 38 street is a strip on the north side. It’s a strip. 38 street. My first gang was the 38. My address on Chippewa start with a 38. It’s 38 all around.", "annotation_id": "12489864", "url": "https://genius.com/12489864", "state": "verified", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Untouchable", "line": "This for my sons and Montana, and can’t forget Lil Ben", "vault_lines": ["This for my sons and Montana, and can't forget Lil Ben"], "meaning": "This shit for my little boys. All of this shit for my little boys. Me changing for the better is for my little boys. And I say Montana too because Montana give me anything. I got money, but I walk in the mall and still ask Montana to buy me this and he’ll buy it. And Lil Ben, he’s with me. Forever with me. His name on my phone is forever with me with a red heart. Ain’t no changing that. For a fact.", "annotation_id": "12489860", "url": "https://genius.com/12489860", "state": "verified", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Untouchable", "line": "Now that I made it ain’t nothin’ the same, it all changed When I’m in public people see me they screamin’ my name", "vault_lines": ["Now that I made it ain't nothin' the same, it all changed", "When I'm in public people see me they screamin' my name"], "meaning": "Now that I made it, everything have to change. It’s not like an artist who trying to make a name for themselves. Get a fan base. That shit is hurtful and nerve-wracking because a lot of hurtful moments are going to come towards you on your way to that. Now that I made it, ain’t nothing the same, it all changed. Ain’t shit the same. Everything really changed. People fuck with you. It changed in a good way and in a bad way. Because you can’t fuck around. You gotta watch what you say. People take anything and twist that shit up. The media? Fuck the media. They’ll switch any story up. Literally.", "annotation_id": "12489857", "url": "https://genius.com/12489857", "state": "verified", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Untouchable", "line": "Never change on my gang, yeah, I’m stuck with my niggas", "vault_lines": ["Never change on my gang, yeah, I'm stuck with my niggas"], "meaning": "A lot of shit going on that you don’t see. People don’t see with us. We got a lot of problems. A lot. A lot of these flaws. I ain’t gonna say flaws, but a lot of disagreement. Some of us feel like we ain’t where we supposed to be at and that person here feel like—he doing this—and that shit ain’t real. Either way it goes we stay true to each other. Never change. We under investigation now and my team, my positive side tells me, you gotta fall back from them. I ain’t trying to hear that shit. We’re just gonna find a different way and a better way to do it. Where it don’t look like no gang shit. It’s a fucking music group. I ain’t changing, it’s what it is. You need me, you know what it is, I got you.", "annotation_id": "12489851", "url": "https://genius.com/12489851", "state": "verified", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Untouchable", "line": "We had nothin’, stayed down ’til I came up with my niggas Right or wrong, forever right, you know what’s up with me, nigga", "vault_lines": ["We had nothin', stayed down 'til I came up with my niggas", "Right or wrong, forever right, you know what's up with me, nigga"], "meaning": "We ain’t have nothing. Not a fucking thing. We ain’t have nothing but each other and a strong mind. We were slick with this shit. Niggas stayed down. Niggas stayed true to this shit until we came up. That’s what it is.", "annotation_id": "12489841", "url": "https://genius.com/12489841", "state": "verified", "votes": 189, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Untouchable", "line": "Get out BR, move to LA, where I ain’t got to keep a tool", "vault_lines": ["Get out BR, move to LA, where I ain't got to keep a tool"], "meaning": "BR, I wouldn’t say it made me who I am because, shit is just life lessons. The challenges. The every day life in this fucking state made me who I am. Standing up and being strong with my situations I went through, made me who I am, but BR did make a part of me. But honestly that part of me that it made, I don’t want that shit no more. I ain’t want none of that shit no more. So, I get out of BR and move to LA where I ain’t even gotta keep a tool. You ain’t gotta worry about it nine times out of ten. Eight times out of ten. I don’t have to worry about nobody fucking shooting you in California.\n\nMeek Mill told me I had to get out of Baton Rouge because I was gonna die. Because he knows. He experiences this shit with his young boys. And I know that shit hurt him, just from me being in front of him and he’s talking about this shit. Explaining it like how it happened. He told him not to go back there. He told him, “Niggas gone hate.” Meek couldn’t do nothing, but he kept it one hundred from the first time I ever met him. He introduced me to Nicki. Straight positive energy. Motivational, all of that.", "annotation_id": "12489834", "url": "https://genius.com/12489834", "state": "verified", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Untouchable", "line": "I do this shit for my mama, and my lil’ brother too", "vault_lines": ["I do this shit for my mama, and my lil' brother too"], "meaning": "Yeah, NBA Ken. That’s my little nigga, though. I don’t feel like a big brother figure, because I guess I don’t act like a big brother. I guess I’m a man figure towards him. Not a father figure, a man. That’s one of the reasons I want to go back to school and get my high school diploma. So, he feels like, “Shit, yeah. My brother did that.” Obviously he take after my steps anyway. This nigga just got me kicked out my condo for stealing somebody’s fucking bike. This nigga tripping. I don’t know what the fuck wrong with him. He good, though. That’s my little nigga.", "annotation_id": "12489829", "url": "https://genius.com/12489829", "state": "verified", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Untouchable", "line": "Whole lot of nights I went to sleep and I ain’t had no food", "vault_lines": ["Whole lot of nights I went to sleep and I ain't had no food"], "meaning": "Thanks to my mom and my grandfather, I always had a roof over my head. We always had water, but when you look in the refrigerator, all the money go to bills and ain’t shit in the house. Shit was gutter, literally. Now to this point, I see there ain’t nothing wrong with going to sleep with no food. I got $30,000 in my pocket and I can’t go to sleep at night without fucking eating. It’s just a way of living. But yeah, I went through that, though. I lived and went through that shit. I ain’t have nothing to eat, bro. And it’s sad to say my fucking little brother went through it with me.", "annotation_id": "12489825", "url": "https://genius.com/12489825", "state": "verified", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Untouchable", "line": "I got to make up for all them nights that my mama cried I’m goin’ in, I’m puttin’ everythin’ on the line", "vault_lines": ["I got to make up for all them nights that my mama cried", "I'm goin' in, I'm puttin' everythin' on the line"], "meaning": "I used to do a lot of fucked-up shit. A lot of back talk. I wasn’t the best son. I actually saw my mama cry one time. Once. She’s a strong woman, but I actually saw her cry one time. And my mama is like me, never exposing her pain. Basically the music is, but she doesn’t really expose her pain. Even for me to see that, I knew I had hurt her. So I had to make up for all them nights. All them nights I done fucking ran away. I used to run away from home and never come back. Time to make up for all of that shit. I wasn’t the best son. It all afforded me to get to this point.", "annotation_id": "12489822", "url": "https://genius.com/12489822", "state": "verified", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Untouchable", "line": "Dropped out of school to chase my dream, I had some for to prove", "vault_lines": ["Dropped out of school to chase my dream, I had some for to prove"], "meaning": "I dropped out of school in the ninth grade. I passed the eighth grade. I dropped out because my mind wasn’t there. Fuck school, but if you stay it’s cool, though. If you stay in school because it’s the best option for you. But I literally had something to prove. I felt like I couldn’t go hard with rap how I wanted to and give you this image I wanted to, waking up going to school every morning. As a matter of fact, I didn’t even have clothes or fucking shoes. I ain’t feel comfortable going to school. One pair of school pants, one shirt. Probably two pairs of shoes, and that’s bullshit. I didn’t feel comfortable going to school, so I dropped out. I actually told my principal, “I’m dropping out. I ain’t coming back here. I’m gonna be a rapper.” And she’ll tell you to this day, “He told me that shit, and that’s crazy.”", "annotation_id": "12489818", "url": "https://genius.com/12489818", "state": "verified", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Untouchable", "line": "I remember I wanted for to quit so many times But, I knew this moment’d come, now, it’s my time", "vault_lines": ["I remember I wanted for to quit so many times", "But, I knew this moment'd come, now, it's my time"], "meaning": "I used to give up. I used to really doubt myself. I used to think this shit wasn’t going to happen. I literally wanted to quit and there had been times I had quit for a short period of time. Like, a weekend and every time, I was like, “You know what? I gotta start back on this shit because this what people fuck with me for.” And I just know at one point, there wasn’t no stopping me. I knew that this moment was going to come.", "annotation_id": "12489812", "url": "https://genius.com/12489812", "state": "verified", "votes": 108, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
