{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Wagwan", "line": "Michael Jordan, 23 (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Michael Jordan, 23 (Ooh)"], "meaning": "Michael Jordan is one of the most well-known American basketball players from Brooklyn, New York; he is also famous for his shoe partnership with Nike.\n\nThe legendary athlete has most notably worn the number “23” during his long-lasting career with the Chicago Bulls.\n\n\n\nPictured: Michael Jordan at the 1987 slam dunk contest where he earned 50 points and won the competition\n\n\nMicahel Jordan’s number “23” could also refer to one’s twenty-third birthday — on October 20, 2022, YoungBoy Never Broke Again turns twenty-three years old.", "annotation_id": "25739706", "url": "https://genius.com/25739706", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Wagwan", "line": "I been guilty for your love, and I plead now", "vault_lines": ["I been guilty for your love, and I plead now"], "meaning": "Youngboy is relating his love for his partner to the number of court cases he has been the subject of. While he pleaded non-guilty to the recent charges that have culminated in his house-arrest, he pleads ‘guilty’ to loving his partner.", "annotation_id": "25533505", "url": "https://genius.com/25533505", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Wagwan", "line": "For to get this shit, I walked through Hell, and I ain’t givin’ nothin’", "vault_lines": ["For to get this shit, I walked through Hell, and I ain't givin' nothin'"], "meaning": "Wagwan is a way to say What’s going on? in Jamaican English, used throughout the Jamaican diaspora (or where Jamaican people live outside of Jamaica)\n\nhey homie, “wagwan”?", "annotation_id": "25497325", "url": "https://genius.com/25497325", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Wagwan", "line": "She say, “Hey” to me, I say, “Wagwan”", "vault_lines": ["She say, \"Hey\" to me, I say, \"Wagwan\""], "meaning": "Wagwan is a way to say What’s going on? or Wassup? in Jamaican English, used throughout the Jamaican diaspora (or where Jamaican people live outside of Jamaica)\n\nhey homie, “wagwan”?", "annotation_id": "25497305", "url": "https://genius.com/25497305", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Wagwan", "line": "I’m too street for industry", "vault_lines": ["I'm too street for industry (Ooh)"], "meaning": "This is most likely the answer to Gucci Mane’s question from his song “Publicity Stunt” where he diss YB:\n\nIs you in the streets or a industry nigga?\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=huyesPYXlcQ\nYou can read more about the beef here.", "annotation_id": "25488088", "url": "https://genius.com/25488088", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
