{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "War With Us", "line": "Caught ’em slippin’, blowed his brains out, nobody said who did it (Rah, rah)", "vault_lines": ["Caught 'em slippin', blowed his brains out, nobody said who did it (Rah, rah)"], "meaning": "This is a diss to his fallen opp Da real gee money when he left the studio after recording a song at 1 in the morning and he died.\n\nand PS fuck gee money broke ass bitch 🖕🏾🖕🏾🖕🏾🖕🏾🖕🏾🖕🏾 pussy nigga dead fuck him and i’ll fuck his mom since he did that to yb’s sister. #YBBETTER", "annotation_id": "27098995", "url": "https://genius.com/27098995", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "War With Us", "line": "Seven murders in one week, bitch, it’s crucial and it’s wicked (Wicked)", "vault_lines": ["Seven murders in one week, bitch, it's crucial and it's wicked (Wicked)"], "meaning": "Youngboy has had multiple cases involving murder. He is known for killing people so it shouldn’t come as a surprise that he killed seven people in one week. He has mentioned this in one of his recent songs as well.\n\nIn ‘Dead Trollz’, he mentions it again: “Seven murders in my hometown, tell them bitches I did that”.", "annotation_id": "20927596", "url": "https://genius.com/20927596", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "War With Us", "line": "And don’t think that we ain’t gon’ get you ’cause you stay in Denham (Pussy bitch)", "vault_lines": ["And don't think that we ain't gon' get you 'cause you stay in Denham (Pussy bitch)"], "meaning": "Just you move out of the area where you have trouble, doesn’t mean you will leave the consequences behind, I f you go to Denham, which is Denham Springs, near Baton Rouge, doesn’t mean you won’t be killed.", "annotation_id": "20402883", "url": "https://genius.com/20402883", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "War With Us", "line": "City kinda fucked up right now", "vault_lines": ["City kinda fucked up right now"], "meaning": "NBA YoungBoy, otherwise know as YoungBoy Ain’t Broke Again, is from Baton Rouge, which is in Louisiana. Louisiana and Baton Rouge have high crime and poverty rates, leading to the opening lyric talking about how bad it is in the city.", "annotation_id": "20402866", "url": "https://genius.com/20402866", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "War With Us", "line": "Nigga all I know is murder, swear to God that I’m with it (I’m with it) And everything I talk up in my songs, you know I live it (You know I live it)", "vault_lines": ["Nigga all I know is murder, swear to God that I'm with it (I'm with it)", "And everything I talk up in my songs, you know I live it (You know I live it)"], "meaning": "YoungBoy NBA has been tangled up in a multitude of legal issues dating back to attempted murder charges back in 2016. In May 2019, YoungBoy was involved in a shootout in which a stray bullet killed an innocent man’s life and resulted in 14 months of probation which was terminated December 19, 2019.\n\nYoungBoy NBA’s lyrical inspiration is evidently drawn from real life events and he certainly “lives” what he raps about.", "annotation_id": "18881048", "url": "https://genius.com/18881048", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "War With Us", "line": "Don’t go against the grain, bitch, we headed to the top", "vault_lines": ["Don't go against the grain, bitch, we headed to the top"], "meaning": "“Go[ing] against the grain” is a phrase derived from woodworking.\n\nGrain direction refers to the longitudinal, or vertical, axis of the trunk in which the structural cells are elongated. Cutting wood against the grain direction is often met with resistance and difficulty and has resulted in the phrase being extrapolated to refer the adoption of an unusual idea which is usually met with criticism.\n\nIn this line, YoungBoy asserts himself as destined for success (i.e. the top) and advises others to accept this fact as well.", "annotation_id": "18881017", "url": "https://genius.com/18881017", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
