{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Where I Been", "line": "I ain’t notice I was fuckin’ up my life, but that, they knew about", "vault_lines": ["I ain't notice I was fuckin' up my life, but that, they knew about (Lil Top, Lil Top)"], "meaning": "2024 he was on hard drugs man and obviously some drugs makes you forget things so he didn’t realize he was messing up his life they we us people (fans) and his friends and family know.", "annotation_id": "39254541", "url": "https://genius.com/39254541", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Where I Been", "line": "Came from them shootouts Tell ’em book the stage, ready for to blow the roof off", "vault_lines": ["Came from them shootouts", "Tell 'em book the stage, ready for to blow the roof off"], "meaning": "Refers to his history of being involved in violent situations, likely tied to his criminal past and street life. “Shootouts” here is slang for gunfights or confrontations.\n\n“Tell ‘em book the stage” – “Book the stage” is a theatrical term meaning to secure a place or opportunity to perform or take center stage.\nbasically he came from shooting around and stuff and now that he’s up he ready to take over on Stage.", "annotation_id": "39254535", "url": "https://genius.com/39254535", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Where I Been", "line": "Go and buy a brand-new home with new locks on the door Got a brand-new phone, out of contact with them hoes", "vault_lines": ["Go and buy a brand-new home with new locks on the door", "Got a brand-new phone, out of contact with them hoes"], "meaning": "After all the pain and drug abuse he faced in the 2024 year without realising, he knew that his fans, friends, and family care about him. He finally decides for himself, that his own life matters a lot around him because he has all the money and support around the globe, that he needs to still be here for himself and family aswell.\n\nJust saying that he wants to start fresh, a new life, and nobody that brings him down stays around no more.", "annotation_id": "39251129", "url": "https://genius.com/39251129", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Where I Been", "line": "Same day I pop like twenty Xans and don’t remember where I’m at But I say no more", "vault_lines": ["Same day I pop like twenty Xans and don't remember where I'm at", "But I say no more"], "meaning": "if you go to his music catalog for 2024, he talks about many times where he abuses drugs, you can also hear how he slurs and raps in his songs, as himself stated in one song, that he popped 50 Xans, he a real gremlin.", "annotation_id": "39251101", "url": "https://genius.com/39251101", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Where I Been", "line": "Don’t none of these people ’posed to be ’round, where the fuck my sister at?", "vault_lines": ["Don't none of these people 'posed to be 'round, where the fuck my sister at?"], "meaning": "Fake people who was around him when he needed help to get off drugs, a lot of people he talked to told him to stay off it.\n\nMakonnen, the producer he made music with, was left in the cold outside his door waiting for some period of time, before he left with no answer. This shows how much it affected some people around his circle that was real to him.\n\nHis sister most likely mentors him and reminds him that he has his own life too.", "annotation_id": "39251038", "url": "https://genius.com/39251038", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Where I Been", "line": "I hear somethin’ wrong that I don’t like, I just say, “Where my Glock at?”", "vault_lines": ["I hear somethin' wrong that I don't like, I just say, \"Where my Glock at?\""], "meaning": "Since he’s talking about his major drug abuse during 2024, he is referring to how the drugs really affected him to cause a paranoia to things, he might’ve been hearing and seeing things that he just didn’t like, just to ask for a glock.", "annotation_id": "39251027", "url": "https://genius.com/39251027", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Where I Been", "line": "People come around just for my lifestyle, thinkin’ clear, I ain’t like that", "vault_lines": ["People come around just for my lifestyle, thinkin' clear, I ain't like that"], "meaning": "They just come for the money, drugs, clothes, and possibly cars, just the rich rapstar life.", "annotation_id": "39251025", "url": "https://genius.com/39251025", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Where I Been", "line": "Nigga played, I murdered most of them guys, I ain’t gotta speak about that", "vault_lines": ["Nigga played, I murdered most of them guys, I ain't gotta speak about that"], "meaning": "Talking about the tbg gang and some other stuff allegedly.", "annotation_id": "39251021", "url": "https://genius.com/39251021", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Where I Been", "line": "Made twenty-five doin’ time, I’m a grown man", "vault_lines": ["Made twenty-five doin' time, I'm a grown man"], "meaning": "He turned 25 in Prison, he got arrested 2024 of April under a related prescription drug ring. His birthdays October 20th, 1999.", "annotation_id": "39250906", "url": "https://genius.com/39250906", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Where I Been", "line": "Admittin’ I’m tired, you got it, gangster, I ain’t tryna be with all that", "vault_lines": ["Admittin' I'm tired, you got it, gangster, I ain't tryna be with all that"], "meaning": "He could be Talking about all his opps from the past saying he’s tired of acting gangster and rap beefing with Them trying to change as an man\n\nthis can be seen as he has now made good friends with Fredo Bang", "annotation_id": "36993995", "url": "https://genius.com/36993995", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Where I Been", "line": "I was bumpin’ Peep when I was high", "vault_lines": ["I was bumpin' Peep when I was high, gone off a styrofoam bad"], "meaning": "Lil Peep (real name Gustav Elijah Åhr) was an American rapper, singer, and songwriter known for blending emo, punk, and hip-hop. Rising to fame in the mid-2010s through platforms like SoundCloud, he was a leading figure in the “emo rap” movement. His music often dealt with themes of depression, drug use, heartbreak, and alienation, resonating deeply with a young, online audience. https://filepicker-images.genius.com/a2b212551051884a57314f3899060abedb02d32846ee694c6624891a860431ef%2Fhiacnk6n285", "annotation_id": "35579600", "url": "https://genius.com/35579600", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Where I Been", "line": "Same day I give ‘em fifty grand same day they stealin’ out my bag", "vault_lines": ["Same day I give 'em fifty grand same day they stealin' out my bag"], "meaning": "NBA YoungBoy is referring to the time when BBG Baby Joe (BBG stands for Bottom Boy Gorilla) allegedly took some money from him", "annotation_id": "35513277", "url": "https://genius.com/35513277", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Where I Been", "line": "On top of that mountain, I smoked K2 and know them pills, I popped that", "vault_lines": ["On top of that mountain, I smoked K2 and know them pills, I popped that"], "meaning": "Talking about when he was on house arrest. In Utah On top of the mountain “Gravedigger Mountain” He would smoke k2 which would have him in a bad health state.", "annotation_id": "35434723", "url": "https://genius.com/35434723", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Where I Been", "line": "Had to learn everything ain’t finna get solved with my money", "vault_lines": ["Had to learn everything ain't finna get solved with my money"], "meaning": "He’s saying that not all of life’s problems can be fixed just by having money — and that’s something he had to learn the hard way.\n\nIt also implies that he once tried to use money as a way to fix things — maybe by spending on people, numbing himself with luxury or drugs, or thinking success would bring peace — but it didn’t work.", "annotation_id": "35418988", "url": "https://genius.com/35418988", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Where I Been", "status": "done", "targets": 15, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Youngboy-never-broke-again-where-i-been-lyrics", "genius_title": "Where I Been", "genius_id": 11817634, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Where the Love At", "line": "But hold up, I need to thank my grandfather He showed me how to fix them cars, now I can work that rod now", "vault_lines": ["But hold up, I need to thank my grandfather", "He showed me how to fix them cars, now I can work that rod now"], "meaning": "Throughout YoungBoy’s music, references to his grandparents are common due to him being raised by them, making it known in his raps. While employing a double entendre, YoungBoy particularly refers to his grandfather who taught him how to fix cars, otherwise known as “rods.” However, “rod” is also a term used to refer to a firearm, so YB states that because his grandfather taught him how to fix cars, he used that knowledge to use firearms correctly.\n\nWhile his grandfather isn’t referred to as much as his grandmother, in his August 2018, “No Mentions,” YoungBoy made a notable reference to him as he rapped:\n\nCut my ties with my people, now my grandfather poppin'\nRan it up, all by myself though, now they never gon' stop me", "annotation_id": "29989723", "url": "https://genius.com/29989723", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
