{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Whitey Bulger", "line": "Playin’ ’round with that, man, with them ice or tall men (Ice), don’t discriminate Kick that front door, I say, “Off him” (Say, I get ’em) I got knowledge (Bah) I told my Baba that they cannot fault him (Wallahi)", "vault_lines": ["Playin' 'round with that, man, with them ice or tall men (Ice), don't discriminate", "Kick that front door, I say, \"Off him\" (Say, I get 'em)", "I got knowledge (Bah)", "I told my Baba that they cannot fault him (Wallahi)"], "meaning": "https://images.app.goo.gl/ccCLgMWRGaDNWKZH8", "annotation_id": "35340060", "url": "https://genius.com/35340060", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Whitey Bulger", "line": "Just wan’ front my nine like I’m Whitey Bulger (Woo), yeah", "vault_lines": ["Huh, just wan' front my nine like I'm Whitey Bulger (Woo), yeah"], "meaning": "James Joseph “Whitey” Bulger Jr. was an Irish-American crime boss — the leader of the Winter Hill Gang in Somerville, Massachusetts.\n\nComparing himself to the likes of Whitey Bulger, in 2011, following Bulger’s Federal arrest, he was tried on nineteen murder charges; in 2013, he was found to be involved with eleven murders.\n\nThe “island” YoungBoy refers to is Alcatraz Island, the home to the Alcatraz Federal Penitentiary — a maximum security prison off of the coast of California, surrounded by sharks, making it impossible to escape from. In 1959, Bulger was transferred to the island, hence the reference. YoungBoy again compares himself to the crime boss, noting that the government will re-open Alcatraz just for him due to the severity of his crimes.\n\n\n\nPictured: Whitey Bulger’s 1959 Alcatraz mugshot\n\nYoungBoy makes a play on the word “nine” as he refers to the murders alongside .9 mm firearm ammo — which is often referred to in rap music.\n\nIt’s worth noting that referring to past gang leaders in common in YoungBoy’s music, for example, in his December 2018, “Slime Belief” and his October 2019, “Rich As Hell,” YoungBoy rapped about Griselda Blanco, a Columbian drug lord known to be an affiliate of the Medellín Cartel.", "annotation_id": "21304944", "url": "https://genius.com/21304944", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Whitey Bulger", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Youngboy-never-broke-again-whitey-bulger-lyrics", "genius_title": "Whitey Bulger", "genius_id": 6156741, "source": "api"}
