{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Worth It", "line": "Yeah, it’s the fault up in the sky, I be stressin’ at night (Ooh, stressin’)", "vault_lines": ["It's the fault up in the sky, I be stressin' at night"], "meaning": "YB blames the “fault up in the sky” for the way his life has turned out, as if something beyond his control has had his life set up against him since birth. Because of this, he finds himself stressing at night, when he has time to lie down, think, and reflect on his life and everything he has been through. The line captures his feeling that the circumstances surrounding his life were already working against him, leaving him to deal with the consequences and the thoughts that come with them.", "annotation_id": "41777901", "url": "https://genius.com/41777901", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Worth It", "line": "Would it all get better, yeah? (Ooh, yeah, yeah) Tell me, was it all worth it? (Yeah, yeah, ey, ey, ooh-ooh) No fortune tell’ll make me clever, yeah (Ooh) Deep inside, I been hurtin’ (Oh, I, I, ooh) Tired of tryin’ and I’m sick of cryin’, I’m searchin’ minds, baby, I been lurkin’ (Baby, I been lurkin’) Yeah You left me clueless time after time, I’m behind the blind, as I open up the curtains (Yeah, open up the curtain) Yeah Did you do this shit on purpose? (Did you do this shit on purpose?) Did you do this shit on purpose? (Did you do that shit on purpose?) Yeah I ain’t do that shit on purpose (Swear I ain’t do this shit on purpose) Yeah Swear I ain’t do that shit on purpose (Swear I ain’t do this shit on purpose)", "vault_lines": ["You left me clueless time after time"], "meaning": ".", "annotation_id": "33900634", "url": "https://genius.com/33900634", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
