{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Wrong", "line": "I can’t wait ’til Meech come home so he can get right back in charge", "vault_lines": ["I can't wait 'til Meech come home so he can get right back in charge"], "meaning": "Charged with felon in possession of a firearm and possession of an unregistered firearm. Charged with forgery, identity fraud, possessing a weapon as a restricted person and drug possession. NBA Meechy Baby was accused of shooting at a car with six people in it and was facing three decades in prison.", "annotation_id": "33222938", "url": "https://genius.com/33222938", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Wrong", "line": "I ain’t got no purpose, so I’m gon’ cut up for Big Dump, bitch We see the enemy, then we dump", "vault_lines": ["I ain't got no purpose, so I'm gon' cut up for Big Dump, bitch"], "meaning": "Yb feels like he has no purpose in life so he’d rather slide for big dump. Big Dump is Youngboys late and former manager who died in a drive by", "annotation_id": "33222853", "url": "https://genius.com/33222853", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Wrong", "line": "When grandma died, along my soul died I’m a lonely child, now just tell me I ain’t shit", "vault_lines": ["When grandma died, along my soul died", "I'm a lonely child, now just tell me I ain’t shit"], "meaning": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again was raised by his grandmother, Alice Gaulden, after both of his parents left him during his pre-teenage years—his mother flew abroad while his father on the other hand, was sentenced to fifty-five years in prison after a robbery gone wrong. However, after a life-long battle with heart problems, Alice tragically passed away from heart failure in 2010.\n\nThis untimely passing led YoungBoy to transfer into a group home where he would constantly get bullied. In an interview with Billboard, YoungBoy further explained:\n\nI used to get beat up inside the group home for no reason, the other boys would put their hands on me, and I would look up like, “Why are you hitting me, bro? What’d I do?” It made me discover another side of me that I never glorified or liked. I found out how to be the person that you don’t want to do that with. [Before then], I never understood all the evilness or wrong because I was showered by so much love from this one person.\n\nYoungBoy’s gratitude for his grandmother is seen almost everywhere throughout his discography. An example of this can be seen in his 2023 track, “By Myself”:\n\nI got pain inside my eyes from all this fuckin' cryin'\nMy grandma raised me as a man, but then I came out slime\nMy mama say, “Bitch, you a thug, you better not change up now”", "annotation_id": "30179754", "url": "https://genius.com/30179754", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Wrong", "line": "KD can’t walk", "vault_lines": ["KD can't walk, wish I could sit with him or fuck a bitch with him"], "meaning": "NBA KD was shot and is in a wheelchair cause he’s paralyzed", "annotation_id": "30125243", "url": "https://genius.com/30125243", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Wrong", "line": "Maybe I showed That I don’t need them around", "vault_lines": ["That I don't need them around"], "meaning": "In this line he says “Maybe I showed, that I don’t need them around” right after saying “I know that it got to be something wrong” this shoes that NBA YB feels as if he might be doing something wrong/pushing people away resulting in everyone leaving him. (babymamas, grandma, dead friends, ect)", "annotation_id": "30080920", "url": "https://genius.com/30080920", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "YoungBoy Never Broke Again", "song": "Wrong", "line": "Fucked up, wish I could call Rich Fuck that, I don’t know who my friend Niggas been cliquin’ up with niggas like they want it with me", "vault_lines": ["Niggas been cliquin' up with niggas like they want it with me"], "meaning": "“Rich” is Rich The Kid, and this line might refer to when Rich The Kid was seen with Lil Durk, who has a known rap feud with Youngboy.\n\nhttps://x.com/HipHopTiesMedia/status/1544149270634213377?s=20", "annotation_id": "30039243", "url": "https://genius.com/30039243", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
